window.FWN_MESMERIZING_GHOST_DOCTOR_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_MESMERIZING_GHOST_DOCTOR_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":4801,"title":"Chapter 4801: Let’s See How It Goes","paragraphs":["The faint, resonant sound of lightning tribulations echoed throughout the heavens, day after day, keeping everyone on edge with its persistent thunder and flashes. A day passed, then two, yet the relentless sound of lightning continued, with three powerful bolts striking down every single day. After each set of three bolts, there would be a tense pause until the dawn of the next day. Three days bled into five, and those who had initially presumed Feng Jiu would quickly succumb were now utterly surprised by her enduring resilience.","Feng Jiu’s ascension lightning tribulation was notably different from Mo Chen’s. It mirrored the pattern of Xuanyuan Mo Ze’s trial from back then: only three bolts of lightning descended each day, with each successive bolt proving more powerful and devastating than the last.","Seeing that Feng Jiu had already endured a staggering 49 bolts of lightning and was still sitting there, cross-legged and seemingly unharmed, the Four Great Emperors of the Upper Immortal Realm couldn’t help but descend into a state of growing panic.","\"How can this be? We have clearly strengthened the power of the lightning tribulation and the lightning bolts,\" one of them exclaimed, pacing anxiously in the hall with his hands clasped behind his back. \"So how can she still hold on?\" His voice was laced with disbelief and frustration.","\"Could she really be the Phoenix Star of Destiny? Does she truly possess such an extraordinary destiny?\" another Emperor worriedly mused aloud. Feng Jiu’s strength was undeniably immense, and her luck seemed incredibly profound. If she genuinely succeeded in ascending, would there ever be any peace in the future? At that point, it would likely be a never-ending, brutal conflict.","\"Have you forgotten?\" a third Great Emperor interjected, frowning, his voice calm yet serious. \"She has the ancient Blue Lotus inside her. I’ve noticed that after being tempered by the lightning tribulation every day, she is enveloped in a distinct green aura, and a blue lotus symbol appears clearly between her eyebrows.","According to ancient rumors, this Blue Lotus is the leader of the four great lotuses and possesses the extraordinary ability to quickly repair the body. I estimate that her ability to hold on until now has everything to do with this Blue Lotus.\" After a moment of thoughtful silence, he continued, \"I think that simply increasing the raw power of the lightning tribulation and lightning strikes will not be enough to defeat her. On the contrary, if she can withstand it, her bones and muscles will only become even stronger, and her immortal body will only become more powerful in the future. I believe we have to approach this from an entirely different angle.\"","An Emperor who had been silent throughout the discussion pondered for a moment, then looked at the one who had just spoken. \"Then, in your opinion, how should we proceed?\" he inquired, seeking a concrete solution.","\"How about we transform ourselves into clones and go deal with her directly?\" the third Emperor proposed. \"Only we, with our combined might, can truly deal with her. Otherwise, looking across the entire Immortal Realm, there is no one who can genuinely be her opponent. If we can’t change her personality and trajectory now, then if she ascends successfully, it will inevitably lead to a fight to the death between us.\"","\"If we send our clones, our power will be restricted,\" another Emperor immediately countered, shaking his head. \"I’m afraid we won’t be able to effectively deal with her. Besides, the risk to our main bodies is far too great.\" He clearly refused the suggestion.","\"That won’t work either? Then what do you suggest we do?\" Upon hearing this immediate refusal, the Great Emperor, who was already feeling somewhat uncertain and agitated, became visibly irritable.","The group fell into a tense silence for a moment, each seemingly deep in thought, attempting to conjure a viable solution. After a long while, a glimmer appeared in one of their eyes. He spoke, a calculated tone in his voice: \"How about this? She has already passed 49 lightning tribulations, but she still has 32 more to go before reaching the full 81. These remaining lightning tribulations are truly extraordinary. She may have been able to endure the current forty-nine, but she may not be able to endure the rest. Even if she can endure them, she will be utterly exhausted by then. We will wait for the very last lightning tribulation, and then combine the strength of the four of us to deliver her a heavy, decisive blow. What do you all think of this plan?\""]},{"number":4802,"title":"Chapter 4802: The Last One","paragraphs":["\"You mean, when the last tribulation lightning strikes, the four of us will combine our strength to intensify the lightning and thunder and deal her a heavy blow?\" One of the Emperors listened to these chilling words, his expression shifting slightly as he pondered the implications.","\"That’s right,\" the Great Emperor who proposed the plan affirmed with a nod. \"Although we’ve been working behind the scenes these past few days, we all know that the power of the heavenly thunder we can summon is, at most, two levels below our own cultivation. If it comes to that, the four of us will each use 60-70% of our strength. Do you truly believe that she, alone, will be able to withstand 60-70% of the strength of each of us?\" His voice was laced with an undeniable logic, a cold certainty that their combined might would be overwhelming.","\"Will there be any risk?\" asked a more cautious Great Emperor, his tone hesitant, his brow furrowed with concern.","\"What risk could there possibly be?\" the Great Emperor who made the suggestion countered, dismissing the worry with a wave of his hand. \"As long as we can kill her, even if we consume too much spirit energy and our bodies can’t recover in a short period, what’s the harm in resting and recuperating for a while?\" The more he thought about it, the more convinced he became that the plan was not only feasible but strategically sound.","The other two Emperors considered his words carefully, weighing the risks against the potential rewards. Finally, they nodded in agreement. \"Okay! Let’s do it!\" they declared, their decision made. Even if it meant injuring themselves, as long as they could eliminate the Ghost Doctor Feng Jiu, it would be a price worth paying.","And so, with a sinister accord, the four of them began to rest and recuperate, conserving their energy. They prepared to wait until the final, most potent lightning tribulation gathered, poised to strike. At that precise moment, they would combine their four immense powers, unleashing a coordinated, fatal blow upon Feng Jiu!","Meanwhile, in the distant Eastern Sea Spirit Realm, Guan Xilin and his wife, Wanyan Qianhua, had arrived. Besides them, other members of the Eight Phoenix Guard also gathered, their presence a testament to their unwavering loyalty.","They assembled there to protect her, watching her arduous advancement with a mixture of awe and profound worry. Over the past few days, they had watched the lightning tribulation in the sky unfold, accompanied by terrifying air currents that struck Feng Jiu with deafening force. Along with the raw power of the lightning tribulation, there were also blinding flashes of lightning that made them tremble with fear. Their hearts remained in their mouths, gripped by the constant dread that Feng Jiu would not be able to withstand the onslaught and might collapse at any moment.","\"She seems to be doing fine,\" Wanyan Qianhua said softly, but her hand was tightly clenched around Jun Jueshang’s hand, leaving several unnoticeable marks on his palm from her unconscious grip.","Jun Jueshang gently patted her hand, attempting to soothe her fears. \"Don’t worry! This isn’t her first time going through a calamity. She’s always made it through before. It’ll be fine. Relax a little.\"","\"How can I relax?\" Qianhua retorted, her voice tinged with anguish. \"You said that Mo Ze is in such a state, still lying at the bottom of the sea, sleeping, and no one knows when he will wake up. If something happens to her, what will we do?\" The more she spoke, the more nervous and worried she became, her beautiful eyes fixed intensely on Feng Jiu in the distance, a small, vibrant figure amidst the elemental fury.","\"Little Jiu has survived 77 lightning tribulations, so don’t worry! Nothing will happen to her. I believe in her,\" Guan Xilin said, his gaze also fixed on Feng Jiu in the distance, a flicker of pride in his eyes despite the tension.","From their vantage point, they couldn’t see Feng Jiu with perfect clarity, partly due to the distance and partly because of the swirling pillars of lightning that surrounded her. However, if they concentrated and looked closely, they could still faintly discern the Blue Lotus floating between her eyebrows and the distinctive Blue Lotus aura emanating from her body after each set of three lightning tribulations every day.","Watching her endure the relentless lightning tribulation, Qianhua’s heart was filled with mixed emotions—admiration for Feng Jiu’s strength, but also a deep sense of dread regarding such a path. She held Jun Jueshang’s hand and sighed softly, \"Let’s not go through this tribulation of ascension. With our cultivation, even if we can’t live as long as heaven and earth, we can still enjoy two or three thousand years of life. Not everyone can go through this tribulation of ascension, nor does everyone dare to.\" Her words reflected a profound respect for Feng Jiu’s courage, and perhaps, a quiet acknowledgment of the terrifying cost."]},{"number":4803,"title":"Chapter 4803: Different Aspirations","paragraphs":["Chapter 4803: Different Aspirations","Jun Jueshang gently patted Qianhua’s hands, as he had a faint smile on. “You’re overthinking this,” he reassured. “Not everyone can reach their level of strength, nor does everyone get the opportunity to undergo tribulations and ascend like them.”","Guan Xilin echoed his sentiment with a smile. “Exactly! How many people in this world truly reach the peak of Supreme power? Besides, while our strength isn’t weak, we’re still far from that supreme level. Some cultivate their entire lives and never even touch the edge of it, so it’s really too early for us to talk about ascending.”","He then looked up at the gathering clouds, a contented expression on his face. “What’s more,” he added, “I’m perfectly fine just the way I am now. I have my family—Ye Jing and my children—to keep me company, and I already feel incredibly satisfied. I don’t really think about anything else.”","Guan Xilin had never been a man driven by grand ambition. He grew stronger solely to protect those he cared about. With his current power, he was already among the most formidable in these celestial realms. Plus, with Little Jiu’s extensive connections, no one dared to harm them. In essence, the life they had now was precisely what they desired.","Wanyan Qianhua and Jun Jueshang exchanged glances upon hearing this. For them, too, their current life was exactly what they had wished for—peaceful and happy, a goal they had already achieved.","Everyone’s aspirations are different. Some seek to make a name for themselves, others desire both fame and fortune, some strive for strength for its own sake, while others are compelled by fate to grow stronger. Still others, like them, simply want to live an ordinary life with their loved ones, their children, and their families.","Ironically, Feng Jiu and her companions also longed for such a life, but fate had consistently pushed them to grow and become stronger. Perhaps only when they became the most powerful beings in the world would they finally be able to live the ordinary and warm life they truly wanted.","Deep in the sea, the sleeping Xuanyuan Mo Ze was frantically absorbing spiritual energy. Wisps of power flowed towards him, vanishing in the blink of an eye. The ocean churned beneath the surface, yet the world above remained calm, save for the area near Feng Jiu. There, powerful air currents caused the sea to surge, forming towering waves that crashed against the surface with a roaring sound.","Inside the lightning cylinder, Feng Jiu closed her eyes and gently raised her hands to form a seal. As her hands moved, the aura of the Blue Lotus spread out, swiftly repairing the marks left on her body by the lightning tribulation. The Blue Lotus appeared between her eyebrows, emitting a green light. With her red clothes and black hair, enveloped in this green glow, her face was beautiful and serene, her expression calm and steady.","After using the Blue Lotus’s power to repair the marks from the lightning tribulation, she gently turned her hands and placed them between her knees again, sitting quietly with her palms facing upwards. From beginning to end, she never opened her eyes.","In the Upper Immortal Realm, on Yunxiao Mountain, Hao’er and the other two watched as the days passed, counting the three bolts of lightning that fell each day. Forty-nine bolts had now struck, yet they still hadn’t seen their mother undergoing her tribulation in the Lower Immortal Realm. Growing anxious, they couldn’t help but ask their master to let them see her.","The Azure Emperor was sleeping on a soft couch under a tree. He heard footsteps but did not open his eyes."]},{"number":4804,"title":"Chapter 4804: Request","paragraphs":["Chapter 4804: Request","The three of them approached the plush couch beneath the verdant canopy of the tree, their gazes fixed upon their master, who appeared to be sleeping soundly. A shared, silent understanding passed between them, their eyes meeting in a moment as they exchanged glances.","“Big Brother, it seems Master is asleep,” Yue’er whispered, her voice barely audible, a soft, hushed tone that mirrored the tranquility of the scene. Hao’er, observing their master with a thoughtful expression, echoed her sentiment, his voice equally subdued. “Then we shall wait for Master to wake up,” he murmured, a hint of respect and patience in his words.","Upon hearing this, Muchen’s eyes, fixed on their master, gleamed with a fleeting, knowing light. He harbored a suspicion, a quiet inkling that perhaps their master’s slumber wasn’t as profound as it seemed. There was a distinct possibility, he mused, that their arrival had not gone unnoticed, and that the perceived sleep was merely a polite pretense. Yet, Yue’er, ever practical, simply nodded in agreement. “Alright, let’s wait here for Master to wake up,” she affirmed, settling into a patient stillness.","It felt inherently improper, almost disrespectful, to rouse their master from what appeared to be a restful sleep. Even if the nascent thought of feigned slumber flickered in their minds, the etiquette of the situation dictated that they refrain from any disturbance. Their only recourse was to remain obediently and patiently nearby. Thus, the three of them did not depart, but instead positioned themselves by the soft couch, a silent vigil commencing as they waited. As the minutes stretched into what felt like an eternity, and their master showed no discernible signs of stirring, a subtle stir of anxiety began to ripple through them.","Yue’er, her beautiful eyes suddenly sparkling with a mischievous glint, a tiny, fox-like smile playing on her lips, subtly nudged her two brothers. Leaning in, she lowered her voice conspiratorially. “Big Brother, have you noticed how good Master looks, even when he’s sleeping?” Her question, though seemingly innocuous, carried an undercurrent of playful intent.","Hao’er and Muchen instantly grasped the unspoken meaning behind her words, a shared understanding blossoming between the siblings. A fleeting smile touched their own lips, vanishing almost as quickly as it appeared, before Hao’er, fixing an intense gaze upon their master, responded in a low voice. “Indeed, Master is remarkably handsome. As Mother often says, he is a truly handsome man.”","“While I firmly believe Father is the most handsome man in the entire world, Master is undeniably very handsome too, perhaps just a fraction less handsome than Father,” Muchen declared with a solemn air, his eyes meticulously studying their master’s face.","“Hehe, our Father is absolutely the most handsome man, but Master is also incredibly handsome! Just look at Master’s eyebrows – aren’t they just like those sword-shaped eyebrows described in our books? And his eyes, even though they’re closed now, when he opens them, they sparkle like stars. His nose is perfectly straight and tall, so handsome. And his mouth! It’s also very handsome, with those slightly upturned corners. Mother said that’s called a lotus mouth, and anyone with a lotus mouth is handsome, no matter if they’re a boy or a girl. And then there’s his chin, and the elegant shape of his face...” Yue’er chattered on, her voice filled with an enthusiastic admiration.","The three children, their six eyes fixated with unwavering intensity, scrutinized the Azure Emperor from head to toe, their whispered commentaries filling the air. Even the Azure Emperor, renowned for his extraordinary patience, found himself struggling under the relentless, burning gazes and the continuous stream of observations from the three little ones.","Finally, unable to bear it any longer, he slowly opened his eyes. His gaze briefly swept over Hao’er and Muchen before settling, with a hint of amusement, on the incessantly chattering Yue’er. His voice, deep and resonant with a touch of charming laziness, broke the silence.","“Are you quite finished?”","Yue’er, mid-sentence, automatically snapped her mouth shut the moment his eyes opened. Hearing his question, she offered an innocent, pure smile, her eyes twinkling, and in a soft, sweet voice, she asked, “Master, are you awake?”","Seeing his lack of immediate response, a touch of playful guilt colored Yue’er’s expression. With a delightful smile and a hint of flattery, she added, “We were just waiting for you to wake up! We saw you sleeping and couldn’t help but think how incredibly handsome you looked!”","“Really?” the Azure Emperor inquired slowly, a subtle arch to his brow.","“Yes, Master! You are the most handsome man in the world, right after my father!” Yue’er declared, her flattery reaching its peak."]},{"number":4805,"title":"Chapter 4805: Endless Searching","paragraphs":["\"Master, we want to see Mother. Please, Master, let us see Mother!\" Yue'er pleaded, blinking her large, beautiful eyes at him with an irresistible charm.","The Azure Emperor glanced at the three of them, noting the anticipation and earnest pleading etched on their young faces. He paused for a moment, then, with a graceful sweep of his sleeve, a shimmering, ethereal image materialized before them.","In the projection, their mother sat cross-legged, enveloped in a vibrant green aura. Powerful currents of spiritual energy surged and swirled around her, a testament to her intense cultivation. Seeing her familiar face, so dear to them, the three children instinctively took a step forward, their voices rising in a unified cry. \"Mother!\"","Their heartfelt calls, however, went unanswered. Yet, seeing that she appeared unharmed, Hao'er couldn't help but turn his gaze to their master, seeking further reassurance. \"Master, my mother has already endured so many lightning tribulations,\" he began, his voice laced with a hopeful tremor. \"She will surely be able to navigate the remaining ones smoothly, won't she?\"","The Azure Emperor looked at Hao'er, observing the genuine worry and anxiety reflected in his young eyes. He then shifted his gaze back to Feng Jiu in the image, noting her robust spiritual state. With a reassuring nod, he affirmed, \"Barring any unforeseen complications, she should complete the remaining lightning tribulations without issue.\"","A visible wave of relief washed over Hao'er. He exhaled softly, then broke into a wide, joyful smile. \"That's wonderful! I knew Mother would be fine.\"","Muchen and Muyue exchanged glances, their faces also lighting up with happy smiles, echoing Hao'er's relief.","They watched the floating image for a while longer. Perhaps because the three lightning tribulations scheduled for today had already passed, they observed their mother primarily recuperating and restoring her energy. After a period of quiet observation, their master gently dispersed the image with another wave of his hand.","\"Alright, now return and focus on your cultivation,\" the Azure Emperor instructed, motioning for them to leave. \"Children shouldn't dwell too much on adult matters.\"","The trio had accomplished their objective. They had seen their mother, confirming her well-being, and received their master's assurance that her ascension would proceed smoothly. With their minds eased, the three bowed respectfully and withdrew, their mission complete.","Meanwhile, in the bustling city, Shen Shiqi and the scattered cultivators who had accompanied Yue'er on her previous visit found themselves back once more. Their ongoing quest to locate the elusive, fox-like girl they had encountered on the road, however, remained fruitless.","At a quaint restaurant, they sat by a window, sipping wine and idly munching on peanuts. One of the cultivators broke the silence, a note of frustration in his voice. \"Old Shen, it's been over a year now, and we haven't heard a single piece of news about that little girl. The people we dispatched to find her have also come up empty-handed. It seems she's either still secluded within her sect or deeply hidden in the mountains. Otherwise, with our network, we surely would have uncovered some trace of her.\" Fоr сhаrасtеr shееts аnd glоssаriеs, visit","\"Indeed!\" another chimed in. \"Over the past year, we've covertly investigated all the prominent families in the region, but there's no sign of that little girl whatsoever. She must not be from around here. But what I find truly perplexing is this: how could such a young girl have evaded our pursuit so completely?\"","\"Not only is she not in this city, but she's not even in any of the neighboring towns we've checked,\" added a third wandering cultivator, popping a peanut into his mouth as he spoke. \"We've even posted pictures of her, but there hasn't been a single clue. She's truly mysterious. And it's been over a year now since we last saw her.\"","Shen Shiqi, idly swirling the wine in his cup, chuckled softly. \"It is precisely because she's so mysterious that she remains so utterly interesting!\""]},{"number":4806,"title":"Chapter 4806: This Person Feng Jiu","paragraphs":["Chapter 4806: This Person Feng Jiu","“Besides, I already told you that the little girl we saw had her face covered. It’s not surprising we couldn’t find her. But I truly believe we’ll cross paths again someday.”","“Only you would be dedicated enough to search for a little girl for over a year,” another companion chuckled, casting a playful glance at Shen Shiqi. “The rest of us have been incredibly loyal, tagging along with you everywhere this past year, without even knowing your true objective. It’s a shame the little girl is a bit too young; otherwise, we could have pursued her on your behalf and made her your wife!”","The other two burst into laughter at the suggestion.","Shen Shiqi smiled, shaking his head. “Alright, alright, enough teasing. We’re just passing the time with nothing better to do, aren’t we? Are you guys heading back?” he asked, glancing at them.","“Not really, we’re quite comfortable out here. Going back would be too restrictive,” one replied. “But did you hear that a great emperor ascended from the Immortal Realm last year? Do you know anything about him?”","“It’s been so many years since a powerful being ascended from this realm,” Shen Shiqi began, taking a sip of wine and popping a few peanuts into his mouth. “That powerful being flew up from the lower realms, causing an uproar everywhere. How could we not have heard about it? What’s more, it’s been a year, so naturally, everyone knows about the existence of such a great emperor.” He continued, “It is said that this ascended emperor is reverently called the Great Emperor Holy Lord, or simply the Holy Emperor. His immortal body was transformed from the Primordial Golden Lotus, and when he ascended, he was bathed in dazzling holy light.”","“I’ve heard that too, but it seems that no one knows the true origins of this Great Emperor Holy Lord,” another person added. “After all, there are so many layers of heaven separating us. The lower immortal realm doesn’t know about our upper immortal realm, and the upper immortal realm cannot truly see into the lower realms. It’s truly intriguing!”","“You don’t know?” the third person interjected, lowering his voice conspiratorially with a laugh. “I’ve heard some fascinating news. Do you know that there’s a woman in the lower realm who is revered as the Ghost Doctor Feng Jiu?”","“Ghost Doctor Feng Jiu? That name sounds familiar,” one of them mused.","“I’ve definitely heard of this person,” Shen Shiqi stated, a look of admiration entering his eyes. “It is said that she is the Phoenix Star of Destiny, and her medical skills and alchemy are unmatched in the world. Her talent and strength are astonishing; she’s a true genius that comes once in a thousand years! I heard my father mention it once. He said that Ghost Doctor Feng Jiu is a soul from another world, the Phoenix Star of Destiny, and there’s a prophecy about her that says she will become the ruler of the world, surpassing all the immortals and becoming the supreme ruler!”","At this point, Shen Shiqi paused, his eyes burning with intensity as he leaned forward. “And it is precisely because of this that the Four Great Emperors have joined forces to eliminate her. I heard from my elders at home that the recent, continuous lightning tribulations we’ve been experiencing are likely caused by her undergoing her tribulations and ascending to immortality.”","“Are you saying that the person undergoing the lightning tribulation, the one with three bolts of lightning every day, is that Ghost Doctor Feng Jiu?” another person asked, clearly astonished by this revelation.","Shen Shiqi nodded decisively. “That’s right. Counting the days, she has already passed the minor tribulation of 49 bolts of lightning. As long as she can withstand the subsequent lightning tribulations, she will be able to ascend to immortality. My elders have said that she has a very high chance of succeeding. Moreover, if she does succeed, I estimate that our world will be completely turned upside down.”","Hearing this, the other three couldn’t help but exchange wide-eyed glances, clearly taken aback by the profound implications of Shen Shiqi’s words."]},{"number":4807,"title":"Chapter 4807: The Last Day","paragraphs":["Chapter 4807: The Last Day","Shen Shiqi gestured for the other three to lean in closer. He lowered his voice, “I’m only telling you this because it’s you guys. You’d best send a message back to your families. I’ve heard that the Four Great Emperors are working together to deal with that Ghost Doctor Feng Jiu. They want her dead because they’re afraid she’ll ascend, seize their power and territory, and eventually stand above them all. That’s why they want her eliminated.”","The three men were visibly shocked, exchanging stunned glances. One of them finally managed to ask, “Do you really think that even if Ghost Doctor Feng Jiu succeeds in ascending, she can defeat the Four Great Emperors on her own?”","“Hahea that’s why I said your information isn’t reliable,” Shen Shiqi chuckled, casting a knowing look at them. “This Ghost Doctor Feng Jiu is no ordinary person. Moreover, there’s something else you don’t know: the Immortal Emperor, who ascended to immortality a year ago, has a very deep friendship with Ghost Doctor Feng Jiu.”","This revelation stunned the trio; they clearly hadn’t anticipated such a connection.","“If she really ascends to immortality, will the Four Great Emperors join forces to suppress her? Would they even involve us, the prominent families, in suppressing the Ghost Doctor Feng Jiu? It seems...” one of them mused, a slight frown creasing his brow.","Shen Shiqi leaned back in his chair, seemingly unconcerned. “Just listen to me! You won’t go wrong. If there’s anything you don’t understand, simply pass the message back, and your family elders will consider it.”","Seeing his confidence, the three exchanged glances again, then bowed respectfully. “Old Shen, thank you very much.”","“We are all brothers, there’s no need to thank me,” he waved his hand dismissively, his gaze drifting towards the bustling street outside, wondering when he would next encounter that intriguing little girl. The next time he saw her, he was determined to ask her how she had so skillfully evaded them.","Days turned into weeks, and an unusual oppressiveness settled over both the lower and upper immortal realms. In the upper immortal realm, the aristocratic families and sects felt an uncanny sense of peace, almost as if it were the calm before a storm—a tranquility that stirred an unsettling anxiety for no apparent reason.","Today marked the seventeenth day of Feng Jiu’s ascension to the heavens, and also her final day. If she could successfully withstand the three remaining lightning tribulations today, she would undergo a complete rebirth, achieve an immortal body, and ascend to the Nine Heavens.","The three lightning tribulations scheduled for today were agonizingly slow to arrive. The clouds gathering in the sky, however, grew increasingly oppressive and terrifying. Over the vast sea, powerful winds whipped the waves into a frenzy. They roared as they crashed against the shore, sending towering waves high into the air before they collapsed with thunderous force.","In the Eastern Sea Spirit Realm, monarchs from all corners watched from a safe distance. Luo Yu and the eight Phoenix Guard captains, along with Du Fan and Guan Xilin, remained fixated on the steadfast red figure, who continued to sit quietly amidst the tempest.","After so many days of relentless tempering by the lightning tribulation, the special red robe she wore was now visibly charred and torn in places, its vibrant color faded.","Despite the punishing ordeal, her expression remained serene, as calm as ever. The Blue Lotus between her eyebrows continued to emit a steady stream of vital energy, providing her with continuous support. She seemed utterly oblivious to her surroundings, completely absorbed in the arduous process of her ascension.","In the Upper Immortal Realm, the Four Great Emperors had convened in the sky, their formidable gazes fixed downwards upon the dramatic scene unfolding below."]},{"number":4808,"title":"Chapter 4808: Ascension","paragraphs":["Chapter 4808: Ascension","Their divine senses pierced through the layers of clouds, locking onto the red figure below. Seeing that she had indeed persevered until this point, the four emperors’ expressions turned exceedingly grim.","“I didn’t expect Feng Jiu to possess such incredible fortune,” one emperor remarked, his voice calm yet tinged with a heavy mood. “Now, it’s the last day, and only the final lightning tribulation remains.”","“Since that’s the case, then let’s proceed as we agreed!” another Great Emperor declared, his gaze dark as he stared down. “I refuse to believe she can withstand the combined deadly blow of the four of us!” He continued, “The first two bolts of lightning will serve as a test of her strength. If she can endure them, then the four of us will combine our might for the final, decisive strike!”","“Agreed!”","Immediately, the four exchanged resolute glances. Two of them began to mobilize the immense pressure within their bodies, preparing to intensify the power of the impending lightning tribulation.","At the same time, at Yunxiao Mountain, the Azure Emperor and the three children were captivated by the scene unfolding in the floating mirror beneath a tree. They watched Feng Jiu’s final day of lightning tribulation with bated breath.","The three children were visibly nervous. So nervous, in fact, that even Yue’er, typically the most talkative, was now holding her breath, watching intently, not daring to utter a sound or even breathe too deeply.","The Azure Emperor glanced at the children, then shifted his gaze to Feng Jiu in the mirror, before finally looking up at the sky. He had a strong intuition that those individuals wouldn’t let Feng Jiu off so easily, especially since today marked her last three lightning tribulations. They wouldn’t simply stand by and observe.","He paused for a moment, then rose from the soft couch. With his hands clasped behind his back, he began to walk away slowly.","Hao’er, who had been intently watching the scene, noticed his master’s departure. He looked up to see him walking steadily towards the mountain peak. In just a few moments, his master disappeared into the shroud of clouds and mist that enveloped the summit. Hao’er couldn’t help but wonder what his master was doing.","Because the peak of Yunxiao Mountain was perpetually veiled in clouds and mist, even from the middle of the mountain, it was difficult to discern the scenery at the very top. Therefore, seeing his master ascend towards the summit, Hao’er pondered for a moment.","Since his master hadn’t offered any explanation, Hao’er chose not to ask questions or display curiosity. At that precise moment, his greatest desire was to witness his mother’s successful ascension. No matter who called him, he wouldn’t consider leaving.","Muchen and Muyue either didn’t notice their master’s departure or simply didn’t pay it much heed. In that critical moment, no one was more important to them than their mother—not even their master.","At the very top of Yunxiao Mountain, the Azure Emperor stood with his hands behind his back, facing the wind and gazing at the distant sky. After a prolonged moment, he finally withdrew his gaze and settled down cross-legged on a smooth rock.","He closed his eyes, resting his hands gently on his legs. In that instant, his divine consciousness was fully unleashed...","Down in the Immortal Realm, within the Ling Domain of the East Sea, Feng Jiu’s eyes were closed. Yet, at that very moment, she sensed a powerful, suppressed current of air enveloping her. The immense pressure and surging energy brought with them a profound sense of death and palpable killing intent.","From that overwhelming force, she distinctly perceived two powerful strands of killing intent. In an almost instantaneous flash, her mind became crystal clear. It was obvious: those individuals wanted to take her life.","But did they truly believe it would be that easy to end her life?","The corners of her lips curled upwards slightly, forming a faint, knowing smile.","In the very next moment, lightning flashed and thunder roared, signaling the imminent arrival of the next tribulation!"]},{"number":4809,"title":"Chapter 4809: Vomit Blood","paragraphs":["Chapter 4809: Vomit Blood","She felt a colossal impact, as a huge rush of energy plummeting from a great height, slamming into her body. In that moment, a painful and numbing electric current surged rapidly through her entire being. The lightning tribulation caused her flesh and bones to endure an intensely powerful impact and agonizing pain.","She gritted her teeth, her hands clenched into tight fists, desperately enduring the excruciating pain that felt as though every bone and tendon in her body had been shattered and crushed. Cold sweat trickled down her forehead, sliding down her cheeks, only to be instantly vaporized by the gusts of wind emanating from her body.","Guan Xilin and the others, observing from a safe distance beyond the reach of the tribulation’s pressure and air currents, gasped. This lightning tribulation was even more potent than the previous ones. Seeing her struggling, her face contorted in agony, their anxiety escalated.","In a serene palace in the Upper Immortal Realm, Mo Chen sat cross-legged, his divine sense fully extended. He knew that the Four Great Emperors would undoubtedly try to hinder Feng Jiu’s ascension, so he remained quietly poised. If Feng Jiu truly couldn’t endure, he was ready to offer his assistance.","However, he also held firm in his belief that with Feng Jiu’s inherent strength, she would undoubtedly achieve a smooth ascension. All he had to do was remain patient and wait.","Unexpectedly, about half an incense stick’s time after the first bolt of lightning struck, the second bolt immediately followed, its thunderous roar shaking the very heavens. The sound of the lightning reverberated through the sky.","There had always been a noticeable gap between the lightning tribulations striking Feng Jiu, allowing her crucial time to recover and adapt. The immediate succession of the second bolt after the first was a clear indication of the desperate lengths those individuals were willing to go to eliminate her.","The Four Great Emperors in the sky watched as Feng Jiu in the lower realm remarkably withstood two lightning tribulations. For a moment, their expressions darkened considerably.","“I didn’t expect her to be able to withstand it!” one of the Great Emperors exclaimed hatefully, a hint of anger in his voice.","“This Feng Jiu is truly extraordinary. She is so powerful and formidable,” another Great Emperor said, his voice gloomy and fierce. “No matter what methods we employ, we must not allow her to ascend smoothly. Now, two of the last three bolts of lightning have struck, and it appears she can withstand them. That leaves us with only one final bolt!”","“No, look, she’s coughing up blood!” one of the Great Emperors, who had been intently staring at Feng Jiu below, let out a low cry, his voice filled with unconcealed surprise and excitement.","Hearing this, the other three immediately looked down again. And sure enough, they saw Feng Jiu spit out a mouthful of blood, staining the corners of her mouth and leaving her face noticeably pale.","“Hahahaha! It seems our attacks are working! She shouldn’t be able to hold on much longer!” one of the Great Emperors looked up and burst into boisterous laughter, his face alight with excitement.","Feng Jiu’s act of spitting blood confirmed their belief that she could no longer withstand the amplified power they had added to the two lightning tribulations. Even if she was still clinging on, having endured the first two, there was no way she could survive the third and achieve immortality!","Perhaps it was her spitting blood that invigorated them, as the previously uncertain expressions on the faces of the few emperors suddenly broke into triumphant smiles."]},{"number":4810,"title":"Chapter 4810: Believe in Her","paragraphs":["Chapter 4810: Believe in Her","“Let’s send her on her way!” one of the Great Emperors snarled, his eyes narrowing with a flash of ferocious intent. “It would be best to make her soul fly away and dissipate between heaven and earth! She will never be reborn!”","“Good! The four of us will join forces and deal her a fatal blow!” the other three concurred, exchanging glances and revealing smiles tinged with a murderous aura.","Just as the Four Great Emperors were preparing their devastating final blow, back on Yunxiao Mountain, the three children watched in horror as their mother coughed up blood and her face turned pale. Panic surged through them.","“What should we do? Mother is coughing up blood. Will she be alright?” Yue’er’s eyes reddened with worry, tears welling up, though she bravely fought them back.","“Mother will be fine, she definitely will!” Muchen declared firmly, his small face tense as he stared intently at the scene unfolding before him.","“Mother...” Hao’er’s voice was a soft, choked whisper, his heart pounding. No one knew he was trembling slightly from fear and profound worry.","At the very top of Yunxiao Mountain, the Azure Emperor also observed Feng Jiu’s condition below. When he saw her spit blood, his eyebrows twitched almost imperceptibly, yet he remained seated cross-legged, his eyes still closed.","Perhaps, in his seasoned view, since Feng Jiu had survived so many previous lightning tribulations, she should be able to withstand these final three as well. Moreover, as a master alchemist, she undoubtedly had prepared potent divine pills or magical medicines for emergencies. It seemed unlikely that she would spit blood merely from being struck by two lightning bolts.","However, in the current situation, she did indeed appear injured. And if she was truly injured, the situation would become perilous during the final lightning tribulation.","Simultaneously, in the Eastern Sea Spirit Realm, Guan Xilin and the others were also shocked when they witnessed Feng Jiu spitting blood. Their hearts tightened with dread.","“She’s spitting blood, what should we do? There’s still the final lightning tribulation. Will she be able to withstand it?” Guan Xilin asked uneasily.","Wanyan Qianhua looked at Feng Jiu, took a deep, shaky breath, then turned to Jun Jueshang beside her. “What do you think?”","Jun Jueshang pursed his lips, his gaze fixed on Feng Jiu. His expression grave, he said, “I’m most afraid that her heart and internal organs are injured. If that’s the case, she won’t be able to withstand the power of the final lightning tribulation. Judging from her condition, the consequences of failure are likely to be...”","Hearing this, Wanyan Qianhua immediately interrupted, “We must find a way to save her! We can’t just watch her die in front of us!” As soon as she finished speaking, she took a decisive step forward.","“Wait.”","Du Fan and Leng Hua spoke in unison. They walked over, looking at Wanyan Qianhua and the others. “Our Master instructed us not to disturb her while she is advancing. We can only watch quietly and not approach her. No one can help her, and anyone who approaches her will not only fail to save her, but will also likely be accidentally injured by the lightning tribulation.”","Wanyan Qianhua’s expression darkened slightly. “But she’s coughing up blood. Do you know what will happen to her if she fails?”","Du Fan and Leng Hua exchanged glances and nodded. “Of course we know, but we are here to protect her on our Master’s orders, and we also believe in our Master.”","Du Fan looked at the embattled red figure. “Our Master has survived lightning tribulations before. She will definitely be able to withstand this last one! We believe in her!”"]},{"number":4811,"title":"Chapter 4811: Dazzling","paragraphs":["Seeing this, Jun Jueshang gently held Wanyan Qianhua's hand. \"Trust Feng Jiu! She never does anything she's not sure about. Besides, Du Fan and the others are right. She's survived so many lightning tribulations; there's no reason she won't survive this last one. Trust her!\"","Hearing his words, Wanyan Qianhua nodded, saying nothing further. She simply leaned into Jun Jueshang's embrace, unable to bear looking at the final lightning tribulation that was about to strike.","Guan Xilin listened in silence for a while, not speaking, just clenching his fists so tightly that sweat seeped from his palms.","\"Look, the waves on the sea are a little unusual.\"","Leng Shuang's gaze was fixed on the sea. Although the area was already more turbulent than usual due to her Master's ascension, with larger waves than normal, it was extremely rare to see a wave of seven or eight meters high.","At her words, everyone looked out at the sea. Indeed, a colossal wave was rising, accompanied by howling winds, surging toward the shore with such terrifying force that their expressions grew solemn.","If that terrifying wave crashed down, even Feng Jiu, sitting on the rock, would be affected. However, just as that thought crossed their minds, a loud crack echoed in the sky, and a bolt of lightning struck down. Simultaneously, a lightning tribulation with destructive momentum also descended upon Feng Jiu at that very moment. <abbr class=\"story-note-vis\">Thе mоst up-tо-dаtе vеrsiоn is оn</abbr>","Unnoticed by anyone, as the huge, dazzling lightning bolt streaked across the sky, Feng Jiu, who was already surrounded by lightning, swiftly threw a medicinal pill into her mouth. At the same time, she turned her palm, and an ancient mirror materialized within it.","The lightning and the heavenly thunder struck Feng Jiu with fierce momentum and overwhelming pressure. In that instant, it seemed as if four distinct auras appeared between the heavenly thunder and the lightning. These four different auras transformed into dragon-like shapes, like ferocious dragons opening their mouths, roaring and rushing directly towards Feng Jiu. The death aura that could annihilate heaven and earth also descended at that precise moment.","\"Boom!\"","It was a thunderous roar that shook the heavens, and the entire world seemed to tremble. The very land where the Eastern Sea Spirit Realm was located shook violently, and some of the ground even cracked with a loud, crackling sound, unable to withstand the terrifying pressure.","Just as the lightning tribulation, now infused with the four destructive auras, struck Feng Jiu, a strong, dazzling light, like pure sunlight, burst forth from her body. It was accompanied by a faint crackling sound, eerily similar to the sound of a mirror shattering.","\"Master!\"","\"Xiao Jiu!\"","Everyone cried out in alarm. The destructive aura of death was so immensely powerful, and the dazzling light so blindingly bright, that the area where she stood was completely obscured. No one could see her anymore.","\"Mother!\"","\"Mother!\"","\"Mother!\"","On Yunxiao Mountain, the three children shouted, their eyes red with desperation. Their three pairs of eyes stared intently at the scene, but in the very next moment, the image they were so desperately watching seemed to vanish before them, as if disrupted by some unseen force.","\"Mother! Wuuu... Big Brother, Brother, I can't see Mother, I can't see Mother...\"","Yue'er immediately collapsed into heart-wrenching sobs. She was terrified that the last lightning tribulation had grievously harmed her mother, and now, with the image gone, they couldn't even see her condition."]},{"number":4812,"title":"Chapter 4812: Feng Jiu Ascends","paragraphs":["Chapter 4812: Feng Jiu Ascends","Hao’er and Muchen were equally frantic. They stared at the vanished image, their eyes reddening with intense anxiety. “How could it disappear? Why can’t we see it? Master, Master!”","The two shouted frantically, their voices imbued with spiritual energy, echoing throughout Yunxiao Mountain with an undeniable blend of anxiety and panic.","The Azure Emperor, situated in the clouds above Yunxiao Mountain, heard their cries and understood their distress. However, he was also profoundly surprised himself because at that moment, he, too, could not perceive Feng Jiu’s situation below, let alone spare the attention to respond to his three distraught disciples.","He focused his mind and once again sent his divine sense down towards the Immortal Realm. But he was startled and quickly withdrew his divine sense.","In the Eastern Sea Spirit Realm, amidst the dazzling, sun-bright light, four powerful air currents and a domineering aura refracted from the radiance, shooting upwards towards the Nine Heavens. Their speed and momentum were terrifying, mirroring the four destructive auras that had struck Feng Jiu earlier.","In the sky above the Immortal Realm, the Four Great Emperors were leaning forward, eager to confirm if Feng Jiu had been reduced to ashes. However, in the very next moment, the fierce air currents suddenly assaulted them from all directions. Because these four air currents were eerily familiar, they had no time to react or dodge. They were simply knocked flying by the surging forces.","“Whoosh!”","“Bang!”","The sound of four powerful air currents cutting through the air and striking the Four Great Emperors was followed by a resounding thud. Even with their formidable strength, all four were sent hurtling through the air. As they spat out blood, their figures flew a hundred meters away, spun several times in mid-air, and then plummeted downwards.","“Arghhhh!”","Screams, accompanied by cries of alarm, erupted from the mouths of the four, but they fell into the clouds below due to the heavy blow, disappearing in an instant. All that was known was that the four seemed to be seriously injured.","The Azure Emperor of Yunxiao Mountain witnessed this scene, and Mo Chen in the Immortal Palace saw it too. After a brief moment of surprise, both of them broke into smiles. The former was surprised and excited, while the latter was relieved and at ease.","Simultaneously, in the Eastern Sea Spirit Domain, the dark clouds that had blanketed the entire sky began to disperse in the blinding light. The destructive, deathly aura in the air, along with the powerful air currents and oppressive pressure, all vanished as the light gradually dissipated. Even the seven- or eight-meter-high tidal wave that had risen on the sea surface disappeared back into the water in an instant, leaving only a thin layer of splashing water.","The oppressive atmosphere dissipated completely, replaced by enchanting celestial music echoing from the clear blue sky, and a majestic beam of divine light descending from the heavens.","A seven-colored rainbow stretched gracefully across the sea, extending all the way to the large rock where Feng Jiu was standing. In the immortal realm that now appeared in the sky, immortal cranes and magpies soared, seven-colored clouds floated serenely, and countless dots of holy light gently fell. Finally, the light dispersed and reappeared, enveloping Feng Jiu, who was now fully visible to everyone once more.","She slowly opened her eyes, her clear gaze filled with a brilliant light as she looked up at the celestial path in the sky. Within the sacred light, she stood tall and unyielding, facing the wind.","Her red robe fluttered elegantly, her black hair danced in the breeze, and a Blue Lotus mark bloomed beautifully between her eyebrows, enhancing her unparalleled beauty. At this moment, the edges of the Blue Lotus petals seemed to be covered with a layer of red flame, making her appear both mysterious and mesmerizing."]},{"number":4813,"title":"Chapter 4813: A Promise to Return","paragraphs":["Chapter 4813: A Promise to Return","“Master!”","“Little Jiu!”","“Ah Jiu!”","Du Fan, Guan Xilin, and the others watched the scene unfold with tears of excitement welling in their eyes. They shouted loudly, waving enthusiastically at Feng Jiu, who stood gracefully facing the wind.","After more than twenty days of agonizing anxiety, they could finally release their worries. In that moment, everyone’s hearts swelled with nothing but overwhelming excitement and profound joy.","She had finally done it!","She was finally about to ascend to the Nine Heavens! From the very moment the last bolt of lightning tribulation fell, she now possessed the bones of an immortal and the supreme longevity of the heavens and earth!","Looking at the radiant red figure standing resiliently in the wind, enveloped in holy light and celestial music, everyone’s eyes filled with immense pride. That was their Master, their cherished loved one!","When Feng Jiu heard their voices, she slowly turned, her red dress tracing a beautiful arc as she spun. As she completed her turn, the red skirt fluttered in the wind, looking like a charming and ethereal blooming flower.","Enveloped in that holy light, her figure gradually ascended into the air, her feet gracefully leaving the ground as she floated there quietly. When her clear gaze fell upon their familiar faces below, a hint of profound gentleness appeared in her eyes, and a beautiful smile blossomed on her peerless face.","“Take good care of my family for me. I’m leaving, but I’ll be back!”","Her voice, though soft, carried with an unmistakable firmness from the air, reaching everyone’s ears with perfect clarity.","“Master, rest assured! We will not let you down!”","Du Fan and the others declared in unison. They bowed deeply, their fists clenched, and knelt on one knee, gazing up at their master as she gradually began to disappear from their sight.","“Ah Jiu! We’ll wait for you to come back! Take care of yourself! You must be well!” Wanyan Qianhua shouted loudly, waving tirelessly at Feng Jiu.","“Little Jiu, take care of yourself! We’re here for you, don’t worry!” Guan Xilin also called out, waving enthusiastically. He watched her figure gradually fade into the rainbow bridge within the holy light, ascending higher and higher until she reached the colourful clouds above.","The celestial music in the sky gradually faded, the divine aura in the air dissipated, and the sacred light slowly vanished. The seven-coloured celestial path in the sky also disappeared without a trace, taking with it that dazzling red figure.","Watching her ascend, Wanyan Qianhua, Guan Xilin, and the others finally lowered their gazes and looked at each other. Guan Xilin grinned, letting out a loud, joyful laugh. “I’m going back to the Feng family’s old house to tell Grandfather and the others the good news. They will definitely be very happy when they hear this!”","Hearing this, Wanyan Qianhua nodded. “We’ll go back with you. Come to think of it, I haven’t seen them in a long time. Now that Little Jiu has ascended successfully, there’s nothing to worry about her anymore. Let’s go back with you to see them.”","“Yeah,” Guan Xilin replied, then looked at Du Fan and the others, wondering what arrangements Little Jiu might have made for them before her departure.","Du Fan and the others had already risen to their feet. Hearing the conversation, they briefly conferred amongst themselves before walking over.","Approaching them, Du Fan finally spoke. “Since you plan to return, we won’t be coming along. Our Master isn’t here, but we still have a lot of things to do. Except for the two of you who will stay here with the Feng Guards, the rest of us will make other arrangements to take care of things.”"]},{"number":4814,"title":"Chapter 4814: Wondering What Treasure It Is","paragraphs":["\"Well, you don't need to worry about the old house,\" Guan Xilin said with a nod. \"Just do as Little Jiu instructed before she ascended.\"","\"We know,\" they all replied in unison. They then bowed to Guan Xilin, Wanyan Qianhua, and Jun Jueshang, adding, \"Please convey our greetings and congratulations to the Old Patriarch and the others. If there's anything that needs to be taken care of, just send us a message, and we'll handle it.\"","\"Hahaha, congratulations!\"","The monarchs who had been watching Feng Jiu ascend from a distance approached, smiles gracing their faces, and bowed to them.","The Nancheng Monarch, his face beaming with a kind and friendly demeanor, addressed Guan Xilin and the others. \"The Ghost Doctor has finally ascended! This is truly a cause for celebration for all. We are fortunate to have witnessed the Ghost Doctor's ascension. We are deeply moved and excited. In a few days, we will personally bring gifts to the Feng family's old residence to pay our respects to the Old Patriarch and the others.\"","Guan Xilin bowed in return and smiled. \"Very well, I will report back to my foster father and the others when I return. We look forward to welcoming you all.\"","After exchanging a few pleasantries, the monarchs departed. Guan Xilin, Du Fan, and the others arranged for the Feng guards to protect the sea area before heading to the airship.","Meanwhile, on Yunxiao Mountain, the Azure Emperor returned, riding the wind, his hands clasped behind his back. When he saw Hao'er and Muchen, anxious with red-rimmed eyes, and Yue'er, openly sobbing with worry, the corners of his lips curved into a gentle smile.","\"Why are you crying? Your mother ascended to heaven; isn't that a happy occasion?\"","Hearing his voice and seeing his return, the three children immediately ran towards him.","\"Master!\"","Yue'er, tears still streaming down her face and sobbing bitterly, threw herself at him. \"Master, I can't see my mother! We can't see our mother, waaah...\"","\"Master, our mother...\" Hao'er and Muchen also gathered around him, looking at him with anxiety and worry. Before they could finish, he interrupted them.","\"It's okay, don't say anything, and don't cry. Your mother is fine and ascended successfully.\" Seeing their worried and anxious expressions, and seeing his little disciples crying their eyes out, he waved his hand, and the disappeared image reappeared in front of them.","\"Ah! It's Mother!\"","Yue'er quickly wiped away her tears, afraid that they would blur her vision and prevent her from seeing her mother clearly.","\"Mother ascended successfully!\"","Hao'er and Muchen exclaimed in unison, their faces alight with surprise and excitement, especially as they watched the image of their mother slowly ascending.","\"It's really Mother, sister, look!\" Muchen pulled Yue'er's hand, his small face radiant with joy.","\"Mother, Mother!\" Yue'er shouted, standing on tiptoe to get closer to the image.","The Azure Emperor looked at Feng Jiu in the picture, then glanced at his three disciples, and said, \"She ascended successfully. You can rest assured now, right?\"","Not only had Feng Jiu ascended successfully, but she had also utilized some kind of treasure to seriously injure the Four Great Emperors. Even he hadn't dared to release his divine sense to investigate at that moment, which spoke volumes about the treasure's immense power.","That was entirely understandable. If it wasn't incredibly potent, how could it injure those powerful figures in the Upper Immortal Realm from the Lower Immortal Realm?"]},{"number":4815,"title":"Chapter 4815: Immortal Palace","paragraphs":["Chapter 4815: Immortal Palace","“As long as Mother is all right,” Hao’er said with a smile. His little face, enlivened by that smile, radiated the vitality and happiness befitting his age.","“Master, can we go see Mother?” Muchen asked, looking up at their master.","“Master, take us to see Mother! We miss Mother so much,” Yue’er echoed, tugging at their master’s sleeve.","The Azure Emperor glanced at them and replied, “Have you forgotten what I told you? Even if your mother has ascended, you cannot go see her, nor can you let anyone know about your relationship with her. Otherwise, if her enemies cannot harm her, they will find a way to harm you and use you to threaten her.”","Seeing the disappointment on their three faces, he clasped his hands behind his back, sighed lightly, and said, “I’m doing this for your own good. You’d better gather your thoughts and cultivate!” As soon as he finished speaking, he waved his sleeve, and the image vanished.","“Ahhhhhh! Master!” Seeing that the image of their mother had been erased by their master, Yue’er cried out in surprise, her little face red and her eyes brimming with tears as she looked up at him.","The Azure Emperor turned and walked towards his cave abode, saying indifferently, “Go back and cultivate! It’s good that you know your mother is fine. As for the rest, it’s not something you need to worry about right now.”","Knowing that their master was a man of his word, the three of them didn’t dare to ask for more. They could only walk back with looks of disappointment on their faces.","At Mo Chen’s immortal palace, after witnessing Feng Jiu’s successful ascension, he no longer paid her any attention. Regardless, she had successfully ascended, and other matters were no longer his concern.","Feng Jiu ascended to a particular place in the Immortal Realm, where immortal music resonated in the sky and an immortal island emerged, with a magnificent palace materializing in the light. Her immortal palace was much like Mo Chen’s immortal palace when it was completed a year ago, only the palace and its surroundings were slightly different. Nevertheless, it was still an immortal palace, with immortal maids transforming, flowers blooming on the island, fruits filling the branches, immortal cranes flying about, and magpies chirping happily.","A seven-coloured rainbow bridge spanned the fairy island, adding a dazzling sight to the island, which was as beautiful as a fairyland with flowers in full bloom. However, compared to the bustle of Mo Chen’s fairy palace when it was completed, with people flocking to the gates and monarchs arriving to offer gifts, Feng Jiu’s palace was deserted, with no one coming to offer congratulations or gifts. What she did not know was that the rulers within her jurisdiction had already heard of the enmity between the Four Great Emperors and her, and that they sought to eliminate her. Therefore, even though she had become a great emperor in this realm, those rulers dared not pay their respects, fearing that congratulating this newly ascended emperor might offend the other Four Great Emperors.","Feng Jiu didn’t care much about these things. At this moment, she stood on the seven-coloured rainbow bridge, looking down at her private island. It was an endless island. Apart from her newly built palace, there were several mountains behind the palace that reached into the clouds, and a forest that seemed to stretch on forever. Here, divine mist swirled, and the land was vast. Before the palace and across the vast expanse, flowers bloomed in abundance, with branches heavy with ripe fruit, creating a breathtaking scene. And this rainbow bridge—as the celestial music faded and the surroundings gradually returned to normal, the rainbow bridge remained, not an illusion. Beneath the seven-coloured rainbow were tiered stone steps, proving that this was a rainbow bridge that would never disappear."]},{"number":4816,"title":"Chapter 4816: Fire Phoenix Emerges","paragraphs":["Chapter 4816: Fire Phoenix Emerges","“It’s as beautiful as a fairyland. This must be the place they were talking about, right?” She murmured softly, a wave of happiness washing over her. After overcoming countless difficulties, she had finally ascended to immortality. At this moment, she was naturally overjoyed.","In such a place, on such a beautiful island, she wished so much that her husband and children could be by her side, sharing her joy and enjoying this fairyland together.","“Mo Ze, if only you were here...” she said softly, a hint of regret flashing through her heart. “But it’s alright. I’ll get here first and take care of things. This place will be our home in the future, where our family will be reunited!” A determined light flashed in her eyes as she looked at this fairyland with her clear gaze, and a smile appeared on her face.","In the next moment, she flicked her sleeves, and several rays of light flew out. Some soared into the sky and spun, while others leaped and landed steadily on the ground.","“Master!”","“Master!”","“Master!”","Voices filled with joy and excitement came from the mouths of Feng Jiu’s contract beasts. As the Fire Phoenix flew into the air, a flash of light revealed its true form. The huge Fire Phoenix soared in the sky, its fiery wings flapping, its head raised, and a phoenix cry echoed in the sky, penetrating the clouds and reverberating throughout, reaching every corner of the island below.","In that instant, within the vast forest, all the beasts heard the phoenix cry from the ancient divine beast and immediately lowered their bodies, kneeling down, their mouths emitting howling sounds, daring not even lift their heads. At this moment, the appearance of the Fire Phoenix made it clear to the beasts in the forest that such a powerful ancient divine beast was guarding this island!","Cloud Devouring, Old White, and the other contract beasts saw the Fire Phoenix circling in the sky and crying out, and they knew exactly what it meant. Therefore, after glancing at it in the sky, they looked around happily, leaped up, and ran around in circles. After running for a while, they returned to the Rainbow Bridge and congratulated their master together.","Feng Jiu stood on the Rainbow Bridge facing the wind and looked into the distance, a slight smile on her lips. She watched the fairy maids transformed from cranes and the flower fairies transformed from flowers as they came gracefully behind Cloud Devouring, Old White, and the other contract beasts. When they arrived under the Rainbow Bridge, they bowed respectfully.","“Congratulations to the Phoenix Master on her ascension to immortality...”","Soft congratulations came from their mouths, nothing but auspicious words congratulating her on her ascension. Feng Jiu raised her hand, and some medicinal pills flew into their hands. She said slowly, “That’s enough, you may retreat first! Go prepare a place for us to rest. Also, I need some information, so the four of you are responsible for finding it out for me.”","Her gaze fell on the four immortal maids who had been transformed from cranes. The four immortal maids heard her words and did not hesitate, only responding respectfully, “Yes, we will obey the Phoenix Master’s orders.”","At Feng Jiu’s signal, the immortal maids retreated. Feng Jiu glanced at Cloud Devouring and the other contract beasts, gave them a few instructions, then her red figure flew up into the air and landed directly on the Fire Phoenix circling in the sky."]},{"number":4817,"title":"Chapter 4817: Deal With","paragraphs":["The Fire Phoenix flapped its wings, circling the fairy island with Feng Jiu to survey their new territory and establish a protective barrier.","Meanwhile, the Four Great Emperors, injured by the retaliatory force, had returned to their respective immortal palaces. Upon their return, they immediately entered seclusion to cultivate, instructing their subordinates to remain on high alert for any potential attacks.","One of the great emperors entered his mansion. As soon as the door closed, the blood churning in his chest could no longer be contained, and it gushed out. He staggered backward, leaning on the table and chairs before collapsing onto the bed. He sat up against the headboard, gasping for breath.","Pale-faced, he took a medicinal pill from his space ring and swallowed it. After a while, he sat cross-legged to repair his injuries. It wasn't until two days later that he finally opened his eyes.","\"Feng Jiu, you bastard! How dare you hurt me so badly!\" he muttered hatefully. In his heart, however, he knew that the powerful airflow that had injured him was actually the airflow they had used to attack Feng Jiu. He just didn't understand why their attack had been reflected back, causing them such severe injuries.","\"What kind of treasure is that? How could it reflect their attacks back?\" he wondered aloud, unable to comprehend how such a powerful treasure could exist in the lower immortal realm, let alone how Feng Jiu had obtained it.","Thinking of the other three who had also been counterattacked, he pondered for a moment, then got up and walked out of the room. At the moment, he was afraid that he couldn't simply seclude himself to meditate and repair his internal injuries. That blow had wounded them too severely. Even after taking medicinal pills and meditating for two days, they could only just get out of bed and walk around. If he truly needed to take action, his current physical condition wouldn't allow it. Especially since he had just checked and found that he only had 30% of his strength left. If Feng Jiu attacked him at this moment, he would surely die.","Therefore, while Feng Jiu had just ascended, he had to trip her up so that she wouldn't have a chance to seek revenge!","So, after leaving the room, he ordered someone to send a message to the Immortal Lords, Immortal Elders, and monarchs in the areas under his control, telling them to deal with the newly ascended Great Emperor. At the same time, he personally sent a message to the other three Great Emperors, informing them of his plan and asking them to prepare to join forces with the monarchs and Immortal Lords under his control to oust and defeat Feng Jiu.","After all, with the strength of the monarchs alone, it would be impossible to deal with the newly ascended Great Emperor Feng Jiu. If he let them handle it, they would most likely back down because they would have to face the battle directly. Therefore, he planned to have the monarchs and various clans under the jurisdiction of the Four Great Emperors join forces to cut off the supply of resources to Feng Jiu's jurisdiction.","Almost as soon as his order was issued, the monarchs hurriedly convened a meeting to discuss the matter.","At the same time, Mo Chen, who had received news from the monarchs below, only smiled when he heard about this matter and told them not to get involved. He instructed the immortal maids in the Immortal Palace to guard the palace, then brushed his sleeves and flew up into the sky alone, leaving the Immortal Island and heading towards the distant clouds.","It had been two days since Feng Jiu ascended to immortality. In those two days, she should have finished touring the immortal island she belonged to. He had nothing to do recently, so he was preparing to go see her, catch up with her, and see if she had any solutions to her current troubles."]},{"number":4818,"title":"Chapter 4818: Mo Chen Arrives","paragraphs":["Chapter 4818: Mo Chen Arrives","In the past, it would have taken at least two days to travel from his home island to the other side of the sky. However, after becoming the great emperor of this realm, they had acquired many divine abilities, one of which was called ‘shrinking the earth to an inch.’","It took him half a day to arrive outside Feng Jiu’s immortal island floating in the sky. Standing on the clouds, he looked at the misty immortal island in front of him, vaguely seeing the corners of the magnificent palace and the faintly visible mountain peaks. Upon closer inspection, sure enough, the immortal island was covered with a barrier. He smiled faintly, circled around to the main gate, and when he arrived at the entrance, he called out.","“Ah Jiu, it’s me.”","His voice was soft and gentle, yet it contained a powerful spirit energy that clearly penetrated the clouds and mist and reached Feng Jiu’s ears inside the immortal palace. Hearing Mo Chen’s voice, Feng Jiu’s eyes lit up, and she immediately got up and walked outside. Because it was Mo Chen who had come, she personally went to the entrance and opened the barrier to invite him in.","“Mo Chen, why are you here?” Feng Jiu looked at him, dressed in flowing white robes and looking like a fallen immortal, and asked with a smile.","Mo Chen walked in and followed her for a while before he could get a clear view of the place. With a gentle smile on his face, he said in a soft voice, “I should have come to congratulate you when you ascended two days ago, but I thought that since you had just ascended, there would be many people congratulating you, so I postponed it for two days.” As he spoke, his voice paused, and he looked at her and said, “I see that your place here is even bigger than my immortal island, and the environment is also very charming.” His gaze fell on the rainbow bridge not far away that spanned the entire immortal island, and a hint of surprise flashed in his eyes. “The rainbow bridge hasn’t disappeared?”","Hearing his words, Feng Jiu smiled lightly and said, “The rainbow bridge won’t disappear. You can walk on it. It appeared after I ascended that day.”","As she spoke, she strolled with him and said, “Since my immortal palace was completed, you are the only guest who has visited. I haven’t seen anyone else.”","“Oh?” Mo Chen raised his eyebrows slightly and looked at her. “Do you know why?”","“Mm, it’s the Four Great Emperors playing tricks.” She spoke slowly, looking at the road ahead and walking slowly, not really caring. “The Four Great Emperors have joined forces to deal with me and have even reached into my territory, threatening the monarchs and noble families under my jurisdiction. They are probably afraid of the Four Great Emperors. After all, those few are the authoritative figures in the Upper Immortal Realm. How much do they know about me, a newly ascended emperor?”","Hearing this, Mo Chen smiled and said, “I figured that since you’ve just ascended, there must be things you don’t understand about the Upper Immortal Realm, so I came here today not only to bring you some news, but also to tell you what I’ve learned over the past year or so.”","The two walked to a pavilion and sat down. Two immortal maids served them tea and then withdrew, waiting quietly in the distance.","“What news do you have for me?” Feng Jiu asked as he picked up his tea and took a sip.","“I received news that the Four Great Emperors have ordered that the supply of resources to your jurisdiction be cut off. I expect that there will be other measures to suppress you later.” Mo Chen said, picking up the tea in front of him and taking a sip.","Hearing this, Feng Jiu raised her eyebrows and laughed, “Is that so? That will be interesting.”"]},{"number":4819,"title":"Chapter 4819: She Knows","paragraphs":["Chapter 4819: She Knows","Seeing that she didn’t seem worried, Mo Chen smiled and asked, “Aren’t you worried?”","“Worried? What is there to worry about?” Feng Jiu said casually, playing with the teacup in her hand. “So far, none of my people have come to find me, and I haven’t received any news. There’s no need to rush. Let’s just wait until they can’t hold back any longer and come find me! What’s more, since they don’t take me seriously, I naturally have to teach them a lesson, don’t I?”","Hearing this, Mo Chen shook his head and smiled lightly. This was typical of her personality. Since she wasn’t worried, she naturally had a solution. Therefore, he didn’t continue the topic and asked, “What are your plans for the Four Great Emperors?”","Feng Jiu played with her teacup, the corners of her lips curving slightly, a smile appearing on her face. However, her eyes were cold, and there was even a cold light flashing in them. “All four of them suffered serious injuries. It’s impossible for them to recover in a short period of time. I’ve just ascended and am not yet familiar with everything in this world, so I’ll let them live a little longer! Sooner or later, I will settle the score with those four.” Now that the four of them had been injured by their own power, they would surely worry that she would come looking for them and go into seclusion. Even if she went looking for them, they might not necessarily hide in their immortal palaces. It would be better to put this matter aside for now and deal with the current situation first. Besides, she needed to gain a better understanding of the power of the Upper Immortal Realm.","“You were right not to act rashly. The Four Great Emperors have existed for too long, and their power is by no means as simple as it appears on the surface. Furthermore, some of the other great emperors have some friendship with them. Another thing is that even if you went looking for them, they probably wouldn’t be in their immortal palaces.”","Mo Chen said, glancing at her before taking some information out of his space and handing it to her. “This is some information I’ve collected over the past year. Before we ascended, there were ten Great Emperors, but some of them live in seclusion and don’t easily show themselves, so the information we were able to obtain is limited.”","Feng Jiu took the information he handed her and glanced through it, then smiled. “Thank you, this will be very useful to me.”","Mo Chen smiled and said, “The Four Great Emperors who are after you are very ambitious, and as far as I know, they fear your prophecy of becoming the Sovereign Ruler, so they want to deal with you. As for the others, they have been in seclusion for many years and rarely appear.” He paused for a moment, then continued, “Among them, there is one called the Azure Emperor. His strength is unfathomable, and even the Four Great Emperors fear him. However, this person does not concern himself with worldly affairs. But I hear that he has taken three disciples whom he treasures greatly. He even brought his three disciples to attend a banquet hosted by an immortal not long ago, where he obtained an ancient divine whip for his youngest disciple.”","Listening to him, Feng Jiu didn’t pay much attention at first, but when she heard him mention the three disciples, she paused and looked up at Mo Chen, listening to him finish. When he finished, she couldn’t help but smile and said, “Now that you mention it, I know who you’re talking about.”","Hearing this, Mo Chen was slightly surprised and said, “You know him?”"]},{"number":4820,"title":"Chapter 4820: It’s Him","paragraphs":["Feng Jiu smiled lightly and said, \"Yes, I know him, and I also know his three disciples.\"","Looking at her expression and the smile on her face, a flash of inspiration struck him, and he asked in surprise, \"Could it be... the three children?\"","Feng Jiu nodded slightly and smiled, \"It's a long story, but yes, it's them.\"","Seeing this, Mo Chen smiled and said, \"I understand.\" He was a very perceptive person. As soon as she said it, he could guess most of it, but he didn't know how she knew the Azure Emperor or how the Azure Emperor took the three children as disciples.","\"Right, I have one more thing to ask you,\" Mo Chen said.","\"What is it?\" Feng Jiu looked at him and asked.","\"On the day you ascended, what exactly was the treasure that seriously injured the Four Emperors? What kind of treasure was it that had such power?\" After all, they were so far apart, and what kind of people were the Four Emperors? Such individuals were actually injured, and in such an unguarded situation.","Not expecting him to ask about this, Feng Jiu paused for a moment, then smiled lightly and said, \"It was a mirror, but not an ordinary mirror. Many years ago, I...\" She then told him in detail how she had been led into a cave by a monkey and obtained the mirror that could open a passage to another world.","After hearing what she said, Mo Chen was slightly surprised: \"You got it that way? I didn't expect it to be such a precious treasure. I'm afraid it's not an ordinary object.\"","\"Actually, I didn't expect it to be so effective. It's just a pity that the mirror shattered after reflecting back the attack of the Four Great Emperors. When I ascended, I saw that it had been reduced to fragments,\" she said with some regret.","\"It's a good thing you had such a treasure with you at that time, otherwise you might not have been able to withstand the attack of the Four Great Emperors.\" Mo Chen shook his head and said slowly, \"We can only say that all this was predestined.\"","\"Now I have ascended successfully, but Mo Ze...\" She sighed softly and thought of Mo Ze, who was still in the East Sea Spirit Realm, and her mood became a little heavy. She didn't know when he would wake up, nor did she know when he would ascend. She only hoped that the Blue Lotus power she had sent him would help him.","When she mentioned Mo Ze, Mo Chen thought of his master, so his expression became a little somber, and he said, \"Don't worry! He is a good man and will be protected by heaven. What's more, my master risked his life to give him a chance at life, so he won't die easily. It's only a matter of time before he wakes up and ascends. One day, he will come here and reunite with you all.\"","\"Mm,\" Feng Jiu replied, looking at Mo Chen and saying, \"I'm sorry. It's because of Mo Ze that your master lost his life.\"","Mo Chen shook his head and said, \"Everything is predestined. What's more, my master had long since seen through life and death. He had his reasons for every decision he made.\" In fact, there was one thing he didn't tell her: because his master had revealed too many secrets, his lifespan had been shortened, and he was destined to suffer this calamity. No one was to blame for this.","The two chatted idly in the pavilion. Mo Chen carefully told Feng Jiu about some things in the Upper Immortal Realm to help her understand everything about it in the shortest amount of time.","Meanwhile, deep in the sea of the East Sea Spirit Realm, a steady stream of spirit energy was rushing into the barrier, all of which was absorbed by the sleeping Xuanyuan Mo Ze. On the surface of the sea, waves surged..."]},{"number":4821,"title":"Chapter 4821: Going Out","paragraphs":["Chapter 4821: Going Out","Gu Mo and Wei Feng were guarding the East Sea. When they saw the wind and waves rising on the sea surface, they couldn’t help but glance at each other, then gathered their energy and flew out of the airship to investigate.","“The spirit energy beneath the sea is surging. Could it be Hell’s Lord...” Wei Feng looked at Gu Mo with a hint of surprise on his face. His divine sense detected spirit energy surging from the sea floor and converging at a certain point, but he couldn’t detect where Hell’s Lord was. He guessed that it was the barrier set up by their master that was blocking his divine sense.","Gu Mo pondered for a moment and said, “Our master said that Hell’s Lord might wake up, but it shouldn’t be now. According to our master, Hell’s Lord probably won’t wake up for another three to five years. Today’s fluctuations in the sea are probably a sign that Hell’s Lord is getting better.”","Hearing this, Wei Feng said, “In that case, let’s wait and see what happens for two days before deciding what to do.”","“Mm,” Gu Mo replied. Seeing that there were no other unusual phenomena on the sea surface except for the wind and waves and the surging spirit energy, the two of them headed for the airship.","“I wonder how the Master is doing after ascending. Has she encountered any trouble?” Wei Feng said, his gaze involuntarily turning to the sky. Due to the Master’s ascension, even their communication jade had been cut off, so even if they wanted to know the Master’s whereabouts, they had no way of finding out.","“Don’t worry! Even if our Master is alone in the Upper Immortal Realm, she will definitely take good care of herself. Even if she encounters trouble, with her abilities and skills, how could we worry that she won’t be able to solve it?” Gu Mo smiled and said, “We just need to do a good job of protecting her as our Master instructed. She said she will definitely come back.”","“Right, didn’t Du Fan say that Gray Wolf and Shadow One were coming? Why haven’t they arrived yet?” Wei Feng asked, thinking of the two people he hadn’t seen in a long time.","“You know very well that after Hell’s Lord’s accident, the two of them took over his duties. In addition, the world Hell’s Lord ruled over has also undergone great turmoil due to his situation. With so many things to keep an eye on, how could they possibly leave?” Gu Mo landed on the airship and called two Phoenix Guards to patrol the sea. He and Wei Feng walked to a small table at the bow and sat down. “They couldn’t even make it when the Master ascended, so you can see how busy they are.”","Wei Feng nodded, sat down, poured two cups of wine, and said, “That’s true. With Hell’s Lord in his current situation and our Master not here, if they don’t keep an eye on things, I’m afraid there will be chaos.”","The two of them drank a few cups on the airship and chatted, and before they knew it, time had passed...After sending Mo Chen away, Feng Jiu instructed Fire Phoenix and Old White to stay behind in the immortal palace, then took Cloud Devouring and left, preparing to visit the territory under her jurisdiction.","Dressed in a dazzling red robe that shone like the sun, even with her aura and cultivation suppressed, her outstanding demeanor and unparalleled elegance still drew stares and admiration wherever she went. The people of this realm, whether from noble families or sects, had all become her subjects when she ascended to become the great emperor of this region. The power of life and death was in her hands, and she alone ruled over them."]},{"number":4822,"title":"Chapter 4822: Spreading falsehoods to deceive the masses","paragraphs":["Chapter 4822: Spreading falsehoods to deceive the masses","However, the people here were intimidated by the might of the Four Great Emperors. On the day of her ascension, not a single ruler or immortal sage dared to set foot on the island to offer congratulations. Though she did not hold it against them, she could not tolerate their disrespect.","Today, she left the mansion for two reasons: first, to visit her territory, and second, to see how they were coping with the disruption of their resources. Another reason was that her immortal mansion was too quiet, especially lacking cooks, so she planned to bring a few people back with her.","However, shortly after entering the city, she heard a commotion ahead as she walked down the street.","“What’s going on? Why has the price of spirit rice risen so much? This isn’t normal!” A middle-aged man who looked like a steward said with a frown, shouting, “Our Guo family has been doing business with you for a long time. The price of spirit rice has risen so much, you should at least give us an explanation.”","“Steward Guo, we don’t have the final say on the price of spirit rice. It was my master who said so. There’s nothing we can do about it!” The shopkeeper sighed lightly, looking helpless.","“Could what I heard be true?” a cultivator nearby said in surprise.","“What is true?” someone else asked.","“Don’t you know? I heard from a fellow cultivator that someone above has given orders to cut off the supply of resources to our area. Now it’s spirit rice, but I’m afraid that before long, spirit rice will not only increase in price, but it will also be difficult to find.” The cultivator said with a serious look on his face.","“That... can’t be!” someone nearby said in shock.","“How could it not be? You all know that not long ago, this area was divided and placed under the jurisdiction of the newly ascended Great Emperor. It is said that this newly ascended Great Emperor is a woman who ascended from the Lower Immortal Realm. Just imagine, she ascended from the Lower Immortal Realm, she is a woman, and she just ascended. How can she compare to the other Great Emperors?”","Seeing that everyone was listening with curiosity, the cultivator continued, “Furthermore, it is said that this female emperor has made enemies with the other four great emperors, which is why this has happened. There is also something else you must not know. I heard that other places are recruiting powerful families, and I’m afraid that in a few years, there will be few powerful people left in the territory under the jurisdiction of our female emperor.”","“How dare you! Who are you? How dare you spread such nonsense here!”","A cold voice suddenly rang out, startling everyone, especially the cultivator who had just spoken. He instinctively took a few steps back and looked in the direction of the voice, only to find that it was just a little girl of about five years old.","“You scared me! It’s just a little girl!” The cultivator let out a light breath and calmed down. He glanced at her from the corner of his eye and said coldly, “Little girl, you have quite an aura! But didn’t your parents teach you to be polite to your elders? Also, it’s not ‘demonising’ people, it’s ‘demonising’ the masses.”","The little girl’s cute, chubby face was puffed up with anger, and she stared at the cultivator with her big round eyes and said, “You’re talking nonsense! What qualifies you to be my elder?” As she spoke, she quickly covered her little mouth, looked left and right, then let out a soft sigh and muttered, “Oh my, I learned Grandfather’s bad language again. Fortunately, they didn’t hear me.”"]},{"number":4823,"title":"Chapter 4823: Meeting for the first time","paragraphs":["Chapter 4823: Meeting for the first time","In an inconspicuous corner, Feng Jiu stood leaning against the wall, observing the unfolding scene and the little girl. A gentle smile, like a blooming flower, graced her lips. It was as soft as a spring breeze and as light as a feather brushing against the heart. Those who had been secretly watching her couldn’t help but stare, utterly captivated by her breathtaking beauty and the enchanting smile that played upon her features.","How could such a beautiful woman exist in this world? Every smile and every glance seemed to stir the soul, and the subtle flicker of her eyes was even more alluring, drawing people uncontrollably into the spell of her unparalleled beauty.","“Little girl, you’re in trouble!” a cultivator declared, his face flushing slightly as he took a step forward, intending to intimidate her. However, he was quickly stopped by someone beside him.","“I suggest you don’t touch her. She is the most beloved young lady of the Shu family,” Steward Guo interjected, glancing at the cultivator. He then added, “If a single hair on her head is harmed, you won’t leave this city alive.”","Hearing this, the cultivator was startled and abruptly halted, his face paling.","“Hmph! I’m going to tell Grandfather that you’re spreading rumors here. Our family won’t just move like that! Our family has lived here for generations; we won’t move away,” the little girl stated, her voice soft and sweet, pleasing to the ear.","Knowing that this little girl was indeed the young lady of the Shu family, the cultivator dared not say anything more. “I won’t argue with a little girl like you,” he muttered. With that, he flicked his sleeves, turned around, and disappeared into the crowd.","“Hehe, Eleventh Miss, do you remember me?” Steward Guo approached with a smile, asking, “Why are you here alone? Are your attendants with you?”","“I remember, you’re Steward Guo from Sister Guo’s house.” The little girl smiled, revealing two sweet dimples on her small face. She spoke in a soft voice, “I came out with my second brother, but he saw Sister Guo, so he couldn’t leave, and I snuck away.”","Hearing this, Steward Guo was momentarily taken aback. “Is that my young lady?” he inquired.","“Yes!” The little girl nodded and pointed behind her. “They’re over there, picking out things at the treasure shop!”","Upon hearing this, Steward Guo promptly said, “Why don’t you go with the Eleventh Miss? It’s not safe for you to be out here alone.”","“Hehe, it’s very safe. My second brother always says that I look very safe, and besides, many people in the city know me, so no one will harm me,” she replied with a smile.","In her corner, Feng Jiu overheard the child’s words and couldn’t help but giggle.","Perhaps she heard the laughter, for the little girl’s cute, round, chubby face wrinkled, and she asked, “Who’s laughing at me?” She searched for the source of the sound and spotted Feng Jiu leaning against the corner in a striking red dress.","“Wow!” Her eyes widened, and she blinked her long eyelashes as she stared at Feng Jiu.","At this moment, the people surrounding them also noticed the stunningly beautiful woman in red in the corner. They were all momentarily stunned. It could almost be said that in the world of cultivators, few were truly unattractive. In the cultivation realm, whether it was handsome men or beautiful women, they were as common as grains of sand. However, often, what truly stood out and left people in awe was not merely their appearance, but their demeanor."]},{"number":4824,"title":"Chapter 4824: Cry","paragraphs":["Chapter 4824: Cry","But a woman like the one before them, who seemed to embody the essence of heaven and earth, was something they had never witnessed. Not only was she breathtakingly beautiful, but her demeanor was also extraordinary, especially when accentuated by her red robe, making it impossible to look away.","There were countless beauties in the world, each possessing her own unique charm. Even those who had seen many beautiful women in the cultivation realm had to admit that this red-clad woman’s beauty surpassed all others. She was like a full moon in the sky, and even the most dazzling lights around her could only shine like stars in comparison.","Feng Jiu noticed everyone staring at her, her beautiful eyebrows furrowing slightly, and the smile on her lips faded. She glanced at the chubby, cute little girl and offered her a small smile, then turned and departed. Seeing the little girl, she couldn’t help but think of her own daughter, Yue’er, who was just as adorable! It had been so long since she had seen them. She wondered if they were getting used to living with the Azure Emperor and how much taller they had grown.","She yearned to go see them, but she suppressed the thought as soon as it arose. Now was not the time. As she pondered, she continued walking, but after a short while, she suddenly stopped and looked at the little girl who was following her. The little girl also stopped and gazed up at her with her chubby little face.","“Little girl, why are you following me?” Feng Jiu asked, raising her eyebrows.","“Hehe, sister, you’re so pretty. It’s the first time Xin’er has met someone as pretty as you,” she said with a sweet smile, her round little face lighting up with two adorable dimples.","Before Feng Jiu could respond, the little girl took another small step closer, almost pressing herself against her. Feng Jiu observed her, raising her eyebrows, but remained silent, waiting to see what the child wanted.","“My Grandfather said that if you’re close to ink, you’ll turn black, and if you’re close to vermilion, you’ll turn red. So if I stay close to you, will I become as beautiful as you?”","Her soft and innocent words made Feng Jiu smile. What kind of family was the Shu family? How could they raise such a strange and cute little girl?","Feng Jiu smiled, squatted down, and said, “I’m old enough to be your mother, so you can’t call me sister. You can call me aunty. Also, even if you follow me and stay close to me, you won’t become like me. But you’re already very good just the way you are. You’re very cute and very lucky.”","She reached out and gently pinched the little girl’s chubby cheeks, smiling softly, “You’re still young. When you grow up, you’ll slowly blossom and become even more beautiful.”","The little girl rolled her eyes and looked down at the hand that was pinching her cheeks. She blinked and asked, “Then, beautiful aunty, when I grow up, will I become just like you?”","“No, you won’t.” Feng Jiu smiled lightly, rubbed her little face, and said, “People usually look like their parents.” Little did she know that as soon as she said this, the little girl’s eyes widened, and in the next moment, she pursed her lips and actually tilted her head back and started crying.","“Wah! Boo-hoo... I don’t want to, I don’t want to be like my father... Boo-hoo... I don’t want to...”","Feng Jiu was taken aback and quickly said, “Hey, don’t cry!” What was going on? How did she make the little girl cry? She hadn’t done anything!"]},{"number":4825,"title":"Chapter 4825: Something came up","paragraphs":["Chapter 4825: Something came up","“Oh my, alright, alright, don’t cry. If you cry, you won’t look pretty anymore,” she hurriedly coaxed, unsure whether to laugh or cry.","Hearing that she wouldn’t look pretty if he cried, the little boy quickly stopped, wiped away his tears, looked at her pitifully, and asked curiously, “Beautiful aunty do you have children? Are your children also as beautiful as you?”","Hearing this, Feng Jiu smiled, and her eyes softened as she thought of her two little treasures. “Yes, they are a little older than you, a pair of twins who look exactly alike and are both very handsome.”","“Wow! They look exactly the same? What are they like?” she exclaimed curiously. “Xin’er has never seen two people who look exactly the same!”","Feng Jiu smiled, ruffled her hair, and said, “Alright, hurry back home! Don’t make your family worry.”","“Beautiful auntie, will you take me home? I’ll have my Grandfather invite you to dinner.” She looked up at her, her little face full of hope.","Feng Jiu wanted to refuse, but seeing such a small child looking at her so expectantly, and with the man who had called himself Steward Guo following behind, she thought for a moment. “I’ll take you home! I’ll leave after you get home.”","“Hehe, beautiful aunty, come with me, I’ll take you home.” She ignored the last sentence and took Feng Jiu’s hand, walking away. “I live in a big courtyard with my grandfather. Usually, only my brothers come to the courtyard to play with me. Let me tell you, my grandfather is very powerful. He knows everything, and he can even make grasshoppers out of grass for me!”","Feng Jiu listened quietly, a smile playing on her lips. Listening to her talk about her grandfather, she thought of her own grandfather. Now that she had flown here alone, she might not see them for a long time. Although she felt sad, she knew that as long as they were all well, that was enough.","At the same time, the guards of the Shu family hurriedly came looking for them and found the second young master of their family in the shop.","“Second Young Master, hurry back, something has happened at home!”","The second young master of the Shu family was buying a jade hairpin for his beloved and talking to her when he heard the guards’ anxious words. He was taken aback and asked, “What happened at home?”","“Someone has come to seek revenge, and there are several powerful people. Second Young Master, hurry up and take the young lady back!” The guards looked around but couldn’t see the small figure, so they asked, “Second Young Master, where is the young lady?” She was the apple of the Shu family’s eye. If something happened to her, then...","“Xin’er? Xin’er isn’t...” He was startled and only then remembered his little sister. He looked around but couldn’t see her anywhere. His handsome face was filled with anxiety: “She was just here, how could she be gone?”","“Could she have sneaked out to play?” The fourth young lady of the Guo family said to the attendant beside her, “Quickly help me find Xin’er.”","“Miss, Second Young Master.” Steward Guo walked in and said, “I just saw Eleventh Miss on the street. She was following a woman in red. I was worried that Eleventh Miss might be in danger, so I followed them for a while. Then I saw First Miss leading that woman to the Shu family, so I came to pick up my young miss.”","Hearing this, Second Young Master Shu thanked him, said goodbye to his beloved, and hurried home with his guards."]},{"number":4826,"title":"Chapter 4826: Confrontation","paragraphs":["Chapter 4826: Confrontation","On the other side, Feng Jiu was escorting the little girl home. She had originally planned to leave after dropping her off, but the little girl cried and begged her to come in, leaving Feng Jiu with no choice but to follow her into the courtyard.","Listening to the little girl chatter non-stop, Feng Jiu learned that this courtyard was quite a distance from the main compound. This was also where the Old Patriarch of the Shu family resided, making it a relatively quiet area.","“Where is my Grandfather?” The little girl looked around but couldn’t find her grandfather, so she grabbed a maid and inquired.","“Eleventh Miss, the Third Elder just came to ask the Old Patriarch to come to the front. He just left a moment ago,” the maid replied, lowering her head, not daring to look at the stunningly beautiful woman in red.","“Then ask the kitchen to make us something delicious and send it to the pavilion.” She spoke like a little adult, dutifully playing the role of a little hostess entertaining guests.","“Yes,” the maid replied and withdrew.","Feng Jiu sat in the pavilion, resting her cheek on her hand. She felt that although this little girl was young, she was very capable, even if she sometimes used idioms incorrectly. However, at her age, that was to be expected. She possessed the innocence and kindness of a child, as well as the bearing of a woman from a distinguished family.","The kitchen staff worked quickly, and in about half an incense stick’s time, the dishes were served one after another. The two of them, one big and one small, ate in the quiet courtyard, feeling very comfortable.","“Beautiful auntie, I love this dish, it’s so delicious.” The little girl picked up a piece of meat and stuffed it into her mouth, eating with a satisfied look on her face, while recommending it to Feng Jiu.","Feng Jiu didn’t hesitate and tasted a little of each dish. Although the dishes tasted quite good, her palate had long been spoiled by her former cook, so no matter how delicious they were, they couldn’t compare to the dishes her former cook had made. Therefore, after eating a few bites, she put down her chopsticks.","However, just as Feng Jiu got up to walk around and digest her meal, she suddenly felt a fluctuation in the air. She raised her eyebrows slightly and released her divine sense to investigate.","At this moment, the front gate of the Shu family was littered with corpses, blood was flowing, and the smell of blood filled the air. Moreover, as they fought, a powerful aura permeated the surroundings.","The members of the Shu family were covered in wounds of various sizes. Standing at the forefront of the Shu family’s gate were the Patriarch of the Shu family and the Old Patriarch of the Shu family. At this moment, the Patriarch of the Shu family’s hand, holding the sword, was bleeding, and there was a trace of blood on the corner of his mouth that he hadn’t wiped away.","The Old Patriarch of the Shu family was uninjured, but his face was a little pale, as if he was trying to endure something. In the next moment, a mouthful of blood spurted out.","“Father!”","“Old Patriarch!”","“Grandfather!”","Cries rang out, and Old Patriarch Shu raised his hand, signaling them not to worry. After wiping the blood from the corner of his mouth, he looked at the people in front of him and asked in a calm voice, “What do you want before you’ll stop?”","“Stop? Hahahaha!” One of the men, who appeared to be only in his forties or fifties, looked up and laughed loudly, stroking his beard with one hand, his eyes filled with cruelty. “I specially invited several Immortal Lords to come and help me. Do you think I would stop? The Shu family and the Ruan family have been enemies for over a hundred years. It’s just a pity that we never had the chance to settle the score. Now that we have the Four Great Emperors backing us, how could I let such a good opportunity slip away?”"]},{"number":4827,"title":"Chapter 4827: Riding a Beast","paragraphs":["Hearing this, the Shu family's expressions turned extremely ugly. At that moment, an elder stepped forward and quietly informed the Patriarch and Old Patriarch Shu, \"The other prominent families in the city heard we were in trouble, but they all claimed their Old Predecessors were either absent or in seclusion, and they refused to help.\"","The two men's hearts sank upon hearing this. The enemy had only sent four individuals, but they were all extremely powerful warriors. With the Shu family's current strength, they might have a chance against one or two, but against four, they had no hope of victory.","Meanwhile, in the courtyard behind them, after sensing the commotion at the front, Feng Jiu turned to look at the little girl who was still lying on the table, happily eating meat. She couldn't help but shake her head and smile helplessly.","How did she end up entering the Shu family and stumbling into their troubles? She walked around the courtyard with her hands behind her back, admiring the flowers planted in the garden, and picked one to idly play with.","\"Xin'er,\" she called out to the little girl in the pavilion.","\"Beautiful Aunty, what is it?\" Hearing Feng Jiu call her, the girl quickly put down her chopsticks, took a big sip of soup from her bowl, and then trotted over to her.","Feng Jiu glanced at her and smiled. \"I have a contract beast. My child used to love riding it around. Would you like to try?\"","\"Can I?\" Upon hearing this, her eyes lit up, and two cute dimples appeared on her round little face. She nodded heavily. \"Beautiful Aunty, I want to ride it, I want to ride it!\"","Feng Jiu's lips curved slightly, and with a wave of her hand, the Cloud Devouring Beast materialized in front of her.","The Cloud Devouring Beast looked at its master and understood her intention, so it lowered its body to allow the little girl to climb onto its back.","\"Wow! What a big beast!\" The little girl wasn't afraid. Instead, she climbed onto the beast's back with excitement, her short legs kicking in the air.","\"It's called Cloud Devouring,\" Feng Jiu said with a smile.","\"Cloud Devouring? Does it eat clouds?\" She curiously touched Cloud Devouring's fur, noting that it appeared gentle and obedient, which made her bolder. She squeezed her legs tightly and held onto Cloud Devouring's fur with both hands as she said to Feng Jiu, \"Beautiful Aunty, I'll send it to Grandfather to see. He'll definitely be surprised, hehehe...\"","Seeing her happy smile as she rode Cloud Devouring forward, Feng Jiu smiled, played with the flowers in her hand, and slowly walked around the courtyard to aid her digestion.","As she walked forward, she observed that the maids and guards were all startled by Cloud Devouring. The little girl shouted \"drive\" as she rode forward, but before she reached the front courtyard, she was stopped.","\"Xin'er, where did this beast come from? How can you ride it? Get down quickly!\" A man in his thirties saw his little niece riding the fierce beast, his face pale and solemn. He wanted to go forward but didn't dare.","\"Hehe, Second Uncle, where's Grandfather? I rode it here to show Grandfather.\" The little girl didn't understand his fear and spoke to him with a smile.","\"Your grandfather and the others are at the front gate. Something has happened at home. Someone has come to seek revenge, and many people have been killed or injured. Hurry back, it's not safe up ahead.\" The man wanted to approach, but when he saw the beast glance at him, he froze in place, unable to move.","The little girl listened, the smile on her face disappearing, replaced by shock and panic. Before she could say anything, Cloud Devouring continued walking forward."]},{"number":4828,"title":"Chapter 4828: Help Me!","paragraphs":["Chapter 4828: Help Me!","It wasn’t there for the little girl to ride around on, but to deal with the trouble ahead, so it had no time to linger.","Watching the beast stride forward, the man broke out in a cold sweat. He wiped his brow and muttered, “Where on earth did this beast come from? Why is it so terrifying just by looking at it? And what was that smell coming from it? Could I have been mistaken?” He felt a little dizzy, so he took a deep breath and hurriedly gave chase.","The little girl, riding on Cloud Devouring, came to the forefront. Because she was sitting on its back, she could see the unfolding scene from a distance. Just then, she spotted her grandfather fighting with two individuals. One of them was about to launch a sneak attack from behind, his palm wind gathering a powerful pressure that was poised to strike her grandfather’s back. She was so frightened that she shouted, “Grandfather!”","Almost in that instant, Cloud Devouring leaped forward, throwing the little girl backward while shouting, “Catch her!” The man rushing from behind heard Cloud Devouring’s words and saw his little niece being tossed toward him. Almost instinctively, he reached out to catch her. When he held her in his arms, he breathed a sigh of relief.","“Thank goodness, you’re not hurt, are you?”","“Woo, Second Master, someone hit Grandfather...” The little girl cried, her eyes red.","“Roar!”","Almost at that very moment, Cloud Devouring’s beast roar rang out. That roar carried the awe-inspiring power and powerful aura of a Super Sacred Beast. As soon as it sounded, the three people fighting froze, instinctively looking toward the source of the roar.","However, all they saw was a majestic Super Sacred Beast rushing toward them with fierce momentum and terrifying bloodlust. In just a split second, the person who had been about to strike Old Patriarch Shu was torn apart by Cloud Devouring, his arm ripped clean off.","“Ssshh! Ah!”","The sound of someone gasping for air echoed, followed by a piercing scream that seemed to rip through the heavens, reverberating across the sky and sending a chill down the spines of everyone who heard it.","Old Patriarch Shu didn’t have time to react. He simply stared wide-eyed as the Super Sacred Beast that had appeared out of nowhere tore off the Immortal’s arm and sent him flying toward the gate, where he was caught by his son and the others.","“A Super Sacred Beast!”","Their voices were filled with shock and disbelief. Clearly, none of them had expected a Super Sacred Beast to suddenly appear in the Shu family, and moreover, one with such powerful fighting ability.","In that instant, aside from the immortal lord whose arm had been torn off and was screaming in agony, the other three swiftly retreated to avoid certain death. However, the immortal lord whose arm had been torn off was not so fortunate. He couldn’t dodge in time and was bitten by Cloud Devouring, then slammed violently onto the ground. Cloud Devouring stepped on him with one foot, and the faint sound of bones breaking could be heard, as if his Neidan had shattered at that moment, emitting a slight crackling sound.","“Help, help me...”","The man lay on the ground, looking at the three in the direction of the rescue, blood overflowing from his mouth as he spoke.","“Hiss!”","The three sucked in a cold breath, their faces turning pale in an instant, utterly shocked by this horrific scene."]},{"number":4829,"title":"Chapter 4829: Left","paragraphs":["Chapter 4829: Left","The arrival of the Super Sacred Beast sent shockwaves not only through the powerful individuals it was confronting but also among the members of the Shu family. They were utterly bewildered; the Shu family possessed no such creature, leading them to question its mysterious origins.","Cloud Devouring stood firm, one foot planted on the fallen assailant, its bloodthirsty gaze fixed on the three remaining figures. A low, fierce growl rumbled from its throat. “If you want to be so bold, you should know whose territory this is!” it snarled. “Get lost!” With a final, contemptuous kick, it sent the man it was treading on flying towards his companions.","Instinctively, the three individuals reached out to catch their comrade who was spitting out blood. One of them, after handing the man off to the others, turned to Cloud Devouring. Suppressing the palpable fear in his heart, he dared to ask, “Whose contract beast are you? Who is your master?”","Cloud Devouring offered no reply. Instead, it let out another angry roar, lowered its massive body, and lunged forward, pouncing on them. Its sharp claws sliced through the air, creating several fierce gusts of wind. The beast’s momentum was so overwhelming that the remaining attackers, overcome with terror, dared not stay and quickly fled the scene.","Everyone present stared in blank shock as the powerful individuals simply ran away. For a moment, they stood frozen, until a childish voice, filled with anxiety, broke their stupor. “Grandfather, Grandfather, are you okay? Are you hurt?” The little girl squeezed her way to the front, pulling on Old Patriarch Shu’s sleeve and looking up at him, her round little face etched with worry.","“Grandfather, I’m fine,” Old Patriarch Shu reassured her, patting her small hand. He then looked at the Super Sacred Beast and bowed, hands clasped in respect. “Thank you for saving us, but I don’t know who you are...”","Cloud Devouring simply walked over, glanced at the little girl, and then proceeded toward the Shu residence. This action caught everyone by surprise.","“Grandfather, that’s Beautiful Aunty’s contract beast,” the little girl stated clearly. “I brought Beautiful Aunty back from the street. I invited her to our house for dinner, and she just let me ride that beast, so I came here.”","“Father, let’s go inside first!” urged the Patriarch of the Shu family.","Hearing this, the Old Patriarch nodded and led his granddaughter indoors, while the people behind them quickly set about cleaning up the corpses near the gate before following inside.","Once inside, they didn’t immediately proceed to the backyard. First, they allowed Shu Xin to explain what had transpired. Only then did the Old Patriarch and the Patriarch, accompanied by Shu Xin, go to express their gratitude.","Upon reaching the courtyard, they searched everywhere but could not find the woman in red that Shu Xin had mentioned.","“How could she be gone? She was just here a moment ago,” the little girl said, anxious.","“Greetings, Old Patriarch, Patriarch,” a maid said, coming forward and curtsying. “The young lady has already left.”","Hearing this, they were taken aback. “She left?” They couldn’t believe it. She had just saved the Shu family, and she had simply departed without a word? What kind of person was she?","“Beautiful Aunty is gone? Why did Beautiful Aunty leave?” The little girl was distraught, turning to her grandfather and asking, “Grandfather, what should we do now that Beautiful Aunty is gone?”","“Father, who do you think this person who saved us is?” inquired the Patriarch of the Shu family beside him.","Old Patriarch Shu shook his head. “I don’t know, but someone who commands such a Super Sacred Beast is definitely no ordinary person.” As he spoke, he looked at his little granddaughter, sighing lightly. “Girl, today you accidentally brought a true benefactor to our Shu family! If it weren’t for her, I’m afraid our entire family would have been wiped out today!”"]},{"number":4830,"title":"Chapter 4830: Culinary God - Song Family","paragraphs":["Little Shuxin gazed blankly at her grandfather, a whirlwind of unfamiliar concepts swirling in her young mind. She couldn't fully grasp the intricacies of the situation, the hidden dangers, or the true power at play. All she truly understood was that the \"Beautiful Aunty\" she'd brought home for dinner that day possessed incredible strength. This powerful woman's contracted beast had not only saved her grandfather but had also rescued the entire Shu family from an unseen peril. The weight of their gratitude, however, was something the young girl couldn't yet fathom.","Meanwhile, having gracefully departed from the Shu family's residence, Feng Jiu found herself casually Browse a shop. Her presence at the Shu family's crisis had been purely coincidental, sparked by the innocent request of a little girl. She had intervened, resolving their dire situation with practiced ease. With the meal consumed and the danger averted, there was no lingering reason for her to remain and bask in their effusive thanks. Her attention was drawn by a voice, and a peculiar request.","\"Shopkeeper, do you have any good kitchen knives?\" a rather coquettish female voice chimed.","Feng Jiu, who had been idly examining items displayed before the counter, couldn't help but raise an eyebrow and turn her head. She observed a girl, perhaps sixteen or seventeen years old, entering the establishment. The newcomer was dressed in a neat blue outfit, her hair styled in two practical braids. While not strikingly beautiful at first glance, her features were well-proportioned, exuding a youthful and charming demeanor.","\"Hehe, young lady, how could we possibly have kitchen knives here?\" the shopkeeper chuckled, a genial smile on his face. \"We specialize in high-quality knives, you see. These are primarily for self-defense, certainly not for chopping vegetables.\"","\"I'm not looking for an ordinary kitchen knife,\" the young woman countered, her voice firm as she advanced further into the shop. \"I need a truly good quality one – the kind that won't chip even when cutting through the bones of a spirit cow.\" She paused, then inquired, \"Where are your knives? Let me take a look.\"","\"Of course, please, feel free to browse and see if anything suits your needs over here,\" the shopkeeper replied, his smile widening as he gestured towards the display of weapons.","Feng Jiu found the exchange rather amusing and continued to observe from the sidelines. She watched as the young woman meticulously selected two small knives. Once her choices were made, she posed another question to the shopkeeper. \"Is there a weapon smith in the city?\"","\"Hehe, young lady, there are, indeed,\" the shopkeeper confirmed, still smiling. \"However, they exclusively forge weapons, not kitchen knives. Young lady, shall I wrap these two small knives for you?\"","\"No, thank you,\" the young woman responded. She then produced a rectangular box and carefully placed the two newly purchased knives into designated empty slots within it.","Feng Jiu's gaze briefly flickered to the box, noticing that it contained an assortment of knives and various cooking utensils. Seeing such a comprehensive collection, her eyes sparkled with amusement, and a subtle smile touched her lips. \"Do you enjoy cooking?\" she inquired, her voice soft.","The young woman turned, as if only just noticing Feng Jiu's striking presence. She blinked, her eyes wide with surprise, and stared at Feng Jiu for a long moment before exclaiming, \"You're so beautiful! Who are you? How did you get so beautiful? I didn't even notice you earlier!\"","Hearing the genuine astonishment in the girl's voice, Feng Jiu simply smiled lightly. \"Do you like to cook?\" she repeated, maintaining her calm demeanor. \"And how are your cooking skills?\"","\"I absolutely love to cook!\" the young woman declared with enthusiasm. \"As for my cooking skills, I might not be considered the best at home, but outside, hehe, I haven't met anyone who can cook better than me yet.\" She grinned, her eyebrows arching with a mixture of confidence and pride.","\"Oh?\" Feng Jiu responded, raising an eyebrow as she regarded the girl. \"You look so young. I doubt you possess truly advanced culinary skills. After all, knowing how to cook a few dishes doesn't necessarily qualify one as a genuinely good cook.\"","At Feng Jiu's words, the young girl looked at her with a renewed sense of surprise. \"Sister, haven't you heard of the Culinary God, Song Lingbo?\" she asked, a hint of incredulity in her voice. As she spoke, she unfastened a jade pendant from her waist and held it out to Feng Jiu. \"Look,\" she urged, \"this is a jade pendant unique to my Song family and a symbol of our status. My family is renowned as a family of culinary masters. The dishes we prepare are far from ordinary. In fact, the food we cook can even enhance one's strength and cultivation!\""]},{"number":4831,"title":"Chapter 4831: Surprised","paragraphs":["\"Families like that exist? I've never heard of them,\" Feng Jiu said, a hint of surprise in her voice. Having only recently ascended, the information Mo Chen provided focused solely on powerful figures, so such specialized culinary families were indeed new to her.","At that moment, the shopkeeper, who had been listening intently, couldn't help but interject. \"I know of the Culinary God Song. He is, in fact, renowned for improving his cultivation through his culinary arts. His dishes are crafted from rare spirit beasts, whose meat naturally enhances spiritual energy. However, when prepared by Culinary God Song, that effect is said to increase tenfold. It's also rumored that he is most famous for his medicinal dishes, which can cure illnesses and are valued beyond measure, truly worth their weight in gold.\"","As he spoke, the shopkeeper looked at the girl in green with renewed admiration. \"I didn't expect you to be a member of the Song family. My apologies.\"","\"How about that? Impressive, right?\" The girl lifted her chin, her face beaming with pride.","Feng Jiu appeared thoughtful. \"I never imagined such a chef existed. I truly am ignorant,\" she said with a smile, a decision forming in her mind. She was, after all, looking for a chef. If such a culinary master truly existed, she would certainly extend an invitation for him to join her immortal palace.","\"I didn't expect that! You're actually from the Song family of chefs.\" A man's voice suddenly cut through the air from behind them.","A man dressed in elegant brocade and fine clothes entered, his hands clasped behind his back. He was followed by several bodyguards and a middle-aged man. Initially, the man in brocade focused his gaze on the pretty girl, but then his eyes landed on the stunning woman in red within the shop.","\"Who is this young lady?\" The man's eyes widened with amazement, his attention immediately diverted from the girl.","Feng Jiu offered no reply, simply casting an indifferent glance at the man before looking away.","\"Sister, let me treat you to dinner!\" the girl in green exclaimed, turning to Feng Jiu. \"I just bought two new knives, so it's the perfect opportunity to try them out!\"","Feng Jiu, having just been treated to a meal, couldn't help but smile at the prospect of another invitation, but she didn't refuse. \"Sounds good,\" she replied simply.","\"Let's go,\" the girl in green said, starting to move forward.","\"Hehe, don't rush off!\" The man in brocade clothes reached out, attempting to stop her. \"I've heard that the Song family of chefs are all incredibly skilled. It's a rare pleasure to meet a young lady from such a lineage here, so why don't you come to my residence?\"","\"Hmph! Do you think you can just invite me?\" The girl in green sneered, delivering a swift kick towards the man in brocade. \"Get out of my way, you dog!\"","When she made her move, the man quickly dodged and retreated, his face darkening with anger. He immediately barked an order: \"Catch her!\"","\"Sister, step back!\" The girl in green pushed Feng Jiu to the side, then, with startling speed, retrieved a frying pan from her spatial ring. She swung it directly at the heads of the two guards who were rushing towards her.","Feng Jiu stepped back, observing the scene. Her lips twitched when she saw the young girl using a frying pan as a weapon. As she watched the girl's peculiar method of attack, Feng Jiu couldn't help but focus her attention, studying it carefully. After a moment, a look of genuine astonishment appeared on her face.","She hadn't been mistaken. The girl's attacks clearly mimicked the movements used to stir-fry food and cut meat! Judging by her stance, it was as if she were treating the two guards as her ingredients. In the very next instant, Feng Jiu saw a small knife appear in the girl's hand. Immediately after, the girl shouted in a delicate voice, \"Skin them!\" As soon as the words left her lips, the small knife in her hand swiftly and precisely cut through the clothes of the two guards."]},{"number":4832,"title":"Chapter 4832: Not the same","paragraphs":["Chapter 4832: Not the same","Their clothes, now in tatters, lay scattered across the ground, leaving the two guards exposed in nothing but their hole-riddled underpants. Their faces flushed crimson as they instinctively covered their crotches, scrambling backward in a desperate attempt to retreat.","“Useless!” The man in brocade robes roared, his fury apparent. He turned to the middle-aged man beside him and commanded, “Take her down!”","“Yes!” The middle-aged man responded, lunging instantly at the girl in green.","Feng Jiu observed the unfolding scene. The girl in green, despite her peculiar techniques, clearly possessed considerable skill. Her unique style of combat was undeniably lethal. However, the middle-aged man’s cultivation was superior to hers. Feng Jiu estimated that the girl could hold her own for a few exchanges, but the outcome of a prolonged battle would be uncertain.","Therefore, Feng Jiu remained on the sidelines, watching. When she saw that the girl in green was unable to evade the middle-aged man’s attack, she subtly flicked her wrist, sending a silver needle flying. It instantly pierced the middle-aged man’s acupoint.","In that precise moment, his movements faltered, and he let out a muffled groan, instinctively attempting to retreat. At this opportune moment, the girl in green reacted swiftly, swinging her frying pan with all her might.","“Bang!”","“Pfftttttt!”","The bottom of the pan connected forcefully with the middle-aged man’s face, sending him flying backward. Blood spurted from his mouth as he landed on the ground. A flash of shock and fear crossed his eyes as he looked at Feng Jiu, who stood nearby.","“Damn it! You, you just wait!” The man in brocade robes shouted, his voice laced with rage. Seeing the ferocity of the girl in green, he wisely decided against engaging her further and instead prepared to flee.","However, just as he turned, Feng Jiu extended her hand and flicked her finger. Another silver needle shot out, piercing a pressure point on the man’s body. His legs buckled beneath him, and he stumbled forward, rolling and crawling ignominiously out of the shop.","“How dare you mess with me! Hmph! Well, you should ask my pot if it’s agrees!” The girl in green scoffed lightly. She then hurriedly inspected the bottom of her frying pan. Seeing that it was undamaged, a wide grin spread across her face. “My brother gave me this pot, so it’s good quality.”","Feng Jiu couldn’t help but chuckle as she walked over to the girl. “I didn’t expect you to be so skilled,” she remarked.","“Of course, our family isn’t just good at cooking; we’re also very good at fighting,” the girl replied, lifting her chin proudly. She then said to Feng Jiu, “Sister, why don’t you have anyone to protect you? With a face like yours, you’re bound to get into a lot of trouble outside. You’re lucky you ran into me today, otherwise, they would have probably taken you back. Let me tell you, there are few good young masters from wealthy families. They all rely on their families’ power to do whatever they want, especially when they see a beautiful woman; they want to take her for themselves.”","Hearing this, Feng Jiu smiled lightly. “Isn’t your Song family also a prominent family? You said your brother sent you this pot. Isn’t your brother a young master from a prominent family?”","“That’s different. My family is different,” she said, shaking her head.","“How is it different?” Feng Jiu asked with a smile.","“It’s just different. They wouldn’t do something so immoral,” the girl in green explained. She then added, “Sister, I said I would treat you to a meal. Come, let’s go to the restaurant. I’ll cook something delicious for you myself.”","Feng Jiu smiled. “How about you save it for tonight? I just had a big meal, so I’m a little full right now.”","Hearing this, the girl in green nodded. “Then let’s go in the evening. For now, let’s go sightseeing! I still need to buy a large knife for cutting bones.”"]},{"number":4833,"title":"Chapter 4833: Follow me","paragraphs":["Chapter 4833: Follow me","“That sounds like a plan,” Feng Jiu said, nodding. She accompanied Song Mi’er to various shops, helping her search for the perfect knife. Along the way, Mi’er regaled Feng Jiu with tales of her family, providing Feng Jiu with a general understanding of the unique culinary lineage. However, despite their efforts, Feng Jiu still couldn’t find a kitchen knife that truly suited her specific needs.","As evening fell, the two women entered a bustling restaurant. Song Mi’er, with her innate talent and resourcefulness, managed to borrow the kitchen and personally prepared a magnificent feast for Feng Jiu.","Gazing at the table laden with an array of visually appealing and aromatic dishes, Feng Jiu’s eyebrows rose in pleasant surprise. “Everything looks absolutely delicious,” she remarked.","“Sister Feng, please try some,” Song Mi’er urged, her eyes sparkling with anticipation. “I can cook many more dishes, but I don’t have all the ingredients here, so this will have to do.” She served Feng Jiu a portion, watching her intently, eager for her reaction.","Feng Jiu picked up her chopsticks and selected a piece of golden-brown meat from a bowl. The first bite revealed a delightful contrast: crispy on the outside, incredibly tender and juicy within, leaving a rich, lingering aftertaste. More remarkably, a surge of spiritual energy accompanied the swallowed meat, spreading through her body and leaving her feeling refreshed and invigorated. She couldn’t help but nod approvingly. “It’s very fragrant. What kind of meat is this? How did you make it so delicious?”","“Hehe, there happened to be a black spirit pig that had just been slaughtered in the kitchen,” Mi’er explained, a proud smile on her face. “I took the most tender and delicious piece and made this dish for Sister Feng. This cut of meat is also excellent for stir-frying, but unfortunately, there was only one spirit pig, so there was only enough for this single dish.”","Hearing this, Feng Jiu gave her a sincere thumbs-up. “Your cooking truly is exceptional. I once had a cook who was also excellent, but you are even better than her. You are truly amazing.”","Praised by Feng Jiu, Mi’er beamed with happiness. She eagerly served Feng Jiu another dish, saying, “Sister Feng, try this. This is...”","For the remainder of the meal, Mi’er diligently served Feng Jiu, enthusiastically describing the preparation of each dish. Feng Jiu, for her part, simply nodded almost continuously, focused entirely on savoring the food in her bowl.","Only when most of the dishes on the table had disappeared into her stomach did she finally set down her chopsticks. She exhaled softly, a look of profound satisfaction on her face. “I’m so full. I haven’t eaten this much in a long time. Every dish was so delicious that I simply couldn’t stop.”","“Everyone in my family is a good cook. My cooking isn’t even that good!” Mi’er said with a humble smile, watching Feng Jiu eat with evident satisfaction. As the chef, she was genuinely pleased to see her guest enjoy the meal so thoroughly.","“You’ve been busy serving me; you haven’t eaten much yourself,” Feng Jiu observed as she stood up, beginning to walk around the table to aid her digestion.","“Sister Feng, haven’t you heard the saying, ‘Even three years of famine won’t starve the cook’?” Mi’er winked playfully, a coquettish tone in her voice. “People who cook are often full before the food is even served. Think about it: they taste this dish and that dish, and by the time they’re done cooking, how could they still be hungry?”","Hearing this, Feng Jiu couldn’t help but laugh softly, her eyes filled with amusement. “Mi’er, you mentioned you came out on your own to gain experience and explore the world. How about you follow me?”","“Follow you?” Mi’er looked at Feng Jiu with surprise. “Sister Feng, I’m going out to gain experience. I can’t just follow you home.” While she genuinely liked the beautiful Feng Jiu, her personal quest to find unique ingredients and create new, delicious dishes was paramount."]},{"number":4834,"title":"Chapter 4834: Let’s escape","paragraphs":["Chapter 4834: Let’s escape","“I know, I’m not going home either,” Feng Jiu said with a smile. “I still have things to do elsewhere. Besides, if you come with me and cook while I’m busy, I can ask Grandmaster Iron to forge a kitchen knife and a large bone-cutting knife just for you. How does that sound?”","“Grand, Grandmaster Iron?!!!!” Song Mi’er’s eyes widened in stunned disbelief. “Sister Feng, are you talking about the top armament master, Grandmaster Iron?”","“Yes, that’s him.” Feng Jiu nodded, a slight smile playing on her lips. She was well aware that in the territory of one of the Four Great Emperors, there resided a powerful armament master known for his unyielding nature and volatile temper. Few were fortunate enough to obtain a weapon forged by his hand.","“But... his weapons are incredibly hard to come by. Even my father couldn’t get a knife from him back then. How could he possibly...” It wasn’t that she didn’t want to believe it, but the possibility seemed incredibly remote.","“Just tell me if you’re interested,” Feng Jiu prompted.","Song Mi’er looked at Feng Jiu, pondered for a moment, and finally nodded. “Mm hmm, I’ll go with you.”","Hearing this, Feng Jiu’s smile broadened. “Let’s go! We have serious business to attend to.”","Feng Jiu’s plan was clear: by disrupting the flow of goods and resources in the territory she controlled, she would deliberately stir up trouble in the domain of the Four Great Emperors. If they intended to undermine her, she would seize the opportunity to dismantle one of them first and claim their territory. Currently, the aristocratic families and powerful individuals within her domain still harbored reservations. They feared the might of the Four Great Emperors and hesitated to submit to her. They believed that, despite her ascension to the rank of Emperor and her title as Phoenix Sovereign, she was, at the end of the day, still just a woman.","For the powerful, convincing them to submit to a woman was no simpler than ascending to the rank of Emperor themselves. Throughout history, women had often occupied a disadvantaged position. Unless she could perform an act that compelled their heartfelt submission, it would be extremely difficult to secure their unwavering loyalty. However, for Feng Jiu, matters that could be resolved through sheer force were much simpler. She preferred to prove everything through her inherent strength.","Song Mi’er remained oblivious to Feng Jiu’s true identity. She only knew her as Feng Jiu, and the thought of connecting her to the legendary Phoenix Sovereign, who had ascended some time ago, simply didn’t cross her mind. Such a supreme figure was beyond her wildest imagination; in her perception, powerful beings were elusive, not individuals one encountered by chance.","After settling the bill, the two women headed for the exit. Song Mi’er walked beside Feng Jiu and noticed they were heading towards the city gate. “Sister, are we leaving the city?” she asked, a hint of curiosity in her voice.","“Mm, let’s go somewhere else,” Feng Jiu replied, continuing to lead her towards the city gate. However, just as they were about to exit, a loud shout echoed from behind them:","“It’s them! Catch them! Don’t let them escape!”","Feng Jiu and Song Mi’er glanced back. It was indeed the man in brocade clothes from the shop, now flanked by two different middle-aged men as leaders. Trailing behind them was the middle-aged man who had been struck by Song Mi’er’s frying pan earlier, clearly eager for revenge.","“They’re here to get revenge. Let’s go!” Song Mi’er exclaimed, grabbing Feng Jiu’s arm and pulling her along in a hurried escape.","Feng Jiu cast a brief glance at their pursuers but didn’t resist. Instead, she followed Song Mi’er out of the city. She mused that without Du Fan and the others around, she had to handle many things herself, and this presented an interesting opportunity."]},{"number":4835,"title":"Chapter 4835: Little beast","paragraphs":["Chapter 4835: Little beast","If Du Fan and his men had been there, this family would not have had the opportunity to escape her immediate wrath.","The pursuers watched as the two figures ascended on their swords, vanishing into the distance. Their faces contorted with hatred, but they knew further pursuit was futile. They were too swift. With a frustrated growl, they turned back, intending to report to their Patriarch. They might have escaped this time, but the next time they set foot in this city, there would be no escape!","Half a month later, in a bustling town, Song Mi’er kept glancing at Feng Jiu, a questioning look in her eyes.","“What’s wrong?” Feng Jiu asked, her gaze fixed ahead as she continued walking at a leisurely pace.","Song Mi’er paused for a moment before speaking. “Sister, who exactly are you? The people we encountered yesterday were incredibly powerful, yet they ultimately retreated with their tails between their legs. I know you must have done something to instill such fear in them.”","Hearing this, Feng Jiu offered a light smile. “I didn’t do anything extraordinary. I simply exerted some pressure. They realized they were no match for me, so naturally, they wouldn’t dare to make enemies of us.”","She turned her head slightly, her gaze playful. “Don’t worry, I won’t sell you.”","Song Mi’er smiled bashfully. “I know, I’m just curious.” Her own family was influential, and she had encountered all sorts of people, but the more time she spent with Feng Jiu, the more she felt that this woman was far from ordinary. Yet, she had never heard of a “Feng family.”","Feng Jiu merely smiled and didn’t elaborate further. She simply led Mi’er into an inn. Once inside their room, she addressed her companion. “You can rest at the inn today. I have some matters to attend to outside. If I’m quick, I might be back in a day, but it could take two or three.”","As she finished speaking, she flicked her sleeve, and Cloud Devouring emerged from her interspatial ring. However, it wasn’t in its usual imposing form. Instead, it appeared small, docile, and utterly harmless.","“This is my contract beast. Let it stay with you while I’m away,” Feng Jiu instructed, glancing at the small creature on the ground and communicating with it through her divine sense. “If you encounter any danger you can’t handle, it can at least protect you.”","“Wow! What a cute little beast,” Mi’er exclaimed, her eyes lighting up. Being a young girl, the appearance of such an adorable pet instantly captivated her. She reached out and gently touched the beast’s round, plump body, a smile spreading across her face. “So much meat. The meat of this little beast must be incredibly tender and delicious.”","In that instant, several dishes flashed through her mind, and she wondered how they would taste if she cooked them.","Cloud Devouring, hearing her thoughts, let out two indignant snorts, shook its head, and promptly dislodged the hand that was stroking it.","“Pfft!”","Feng Jiu couldn’t help but chuckle. She shook her head helplessly. “Mi’er, try not to look at every small beast and immediately think about turning it into a dish.” She glanced at Cloud Devouring. “Its name is Cloud Devouring. It’s not just any small beast.”","“Cloud Devouring?” Mi’er’s eyes sparkled. She looked at the white ball of fluff, which had by now sauntered to the side and hopped onto a chair. With a grin, she said, “It’s been a long time since I’ve made dumplings. Sister, I’ll go make you some dumplings to eat before you leave!”","Feng Jiu watched Mi’er, whose eyes were still fixed on Cloud Devouring, and the corners of her mouth twitched. She couldn’t help but wonder if Mi’er would still want to make dumplings if she knew that Cloud Devouring was, in fact, a Super Sacred Beast."]},{"number":4836,"title":"Chapter 4836: Unsettling feeling","paragraphs":["Chapter 4836: Unsettling feeling","Knowing that Feng Jiu had urgent business, Song Mi’er didn’t dally. She asked Feng Jiu to rest in the room, then quickly went downstairs to borrow the inn’s kitchen. Soon, she returned with two steaming bowls of dumplings.","After they finished eating, Feng Jiu gave a few parting words and then left alone, making sure to leave Cloud Devouring behind to protect Song Mi’er. Feng Jiu had noticed that along their journey, as soon as some people realized Song Mi’er was a member of the renowned Song family, they would often target her. While Song Mi’er wasn’t entirely defenseless, she was, after all, Feng Jiu’s personal cook. Feng Jiu couldn’t let anything happen to her while she was away.","This particular area was under the dominion of one of the four emperors who had opposed Feng Jiu, and it was conveniently close to her own territory. This strategic proximity was precisely why she had chosen this location for her annexation plans. She had spent a few days here already, occasionally venturing out to gather intelligence, and now had a good grasp of the local situation. Today, her objective was to ascend to the floating island rumored to be above this region and ascertain if the emperor was residing on the immortal island.","She gracefully rose into the air, soaring towards the clouds. Unsure of the floating island’s exact celestial coordinates, she released her divine sense once she reached the cloud layer, meticulously searching for its hidden location.","After approximately the time it takes for a stick of incense to burn, Feng Jiu opened her eyes. A flash of light gleamed within them, and the corners of her lips curved into a subtle, enigmatic smile that was neither a grin nor a frown. That floating island was cleverly concealed within the clouds, enveloped by a barrier and an array specifically designed to obscure its presence. If it weren’t for her unique spiritual consciousness, which surpassed that of ordinary cultivators, she would never have detected its whereabouts. But now...","She swept her sleeves aside, her red dress fluttering elegantly in the wind. In the next moment, her dazzling red figure transformed into a brilliant beam of light, shooting straight towards the shrouded clouds.","At this very moment, the Great Emperor, who was in secluded cultivation on the immortal island, remained blissfully unaware that disaster was about to strike. Due to the severity of his injuries, he had made arrangements for his subordinates, then consumed a medicinal pill to regulate his breathing and focus on cultivation, hoping for a swift recovery.","However, he and his fellow emperors were acutely aware of the immense energy they had expended in their recent attack. They knew a quick recovery was impossible. Yet, apart from isolating themselves for practice and recuperation, they had no other recourse. After all, the persistent fear of Feng Jiu seeking them out loomed large.","In the secluded cave abode nestled behind the Immortal Palace, the Great Emperor exhaled softly, a furrow forming between his brows as he opened his eyes. A nagging sense of unease plagued him today, an unsettling premonition that something was amiss, preventing him from calming his mind enough to cultivate and regulate his breathing effectively.","“What is going on? Could something be happening?” he murmured to himself. At their level of power, they often possessed a keen intuition for impending danger, and it was precisely this intuition that frequently allowed them to avert crises. He had always trusted his premonitions, just as he did now. When an unexplainable wave of panic welled up in his heart, he ceased his practice and breathing exercises. He opened his eyes, stepped off his ice bed, and began pacing back and forth in the cave abode, his hands clasped behind his back, his face etched with deep thought and worry.","“What could possibly be happening? Everything has been meticulously arranged, and for utmost safety, I even set up layers of barriers and formations. Even this immortal island is thoroughly hidden within the clouds, yet now...”"]},{"number":4837,"title":"Chapter 4837: At the door","paragraphs":["Chapter 4837: At the door","Unable to sit still, he finally left his cave abode and headed for the immortal palace ahead.","“Master?” Seeing him come out, a middle-aged man approached him in surprise and asked hurriedly, “Master, is something wrong?”","The Great Emperor of the Northern Flames stood with his hands behind his back, looking at him with a solemn expression and asked, “I was just about to ask you, is everything as usual? Have you carried out my order to cut off Feng Jiu’s resources?”","“Master, rest assured, everything has been arranged according to your orders,” the middle-aged man said respectfully.","Hearing this, he did not relax his tightly furrowed brow, but said, “Take your men and go patrol the area. I feel uneasy today, so it’s better to be careful.”","“Yes, sir.”","The middle-aged man replied, but just as his voice fell, there was a loud bang in the air, as if a barrier had been broken. With the sound of the bang, the air rippled in circles.","Almost as soon as he heard the loud bang, the Great Emperor of the Northern Flames’ expression changed, and his face darkened: “Damn it!”","He cursed under his breath and instinctively took a step back, his body assuming a defensive posture as he looked warily at the red figure that appeared in the sky as the barrier broke.","“Feng Jiu!”","He gritted his teeth and called out her name in a low voice, his eyes filled with hatred. Even if he had a thousand hearts to kill her, he knew that with his injuries, he was no match for Feng Jiu at this moment.","The middle-aged man beside him heard his words and felt a chill in his heart as he looked at the red figure.He saw the red figure flying through the air with his hands behind his back, his red clothes fluttering and his black hair dancing in the wind, his peerless face filled with a cold expression.","Unable to contain his surprise and shock, he instinctively shouted, “Someone, help! Enemy! Enemy!” His voice was filled with spirit energy and a hint of panic, echoing through the air.","As soon as his voice rang out, dozens of cultivators in powerful attire quickly appeared and drew their long swords to attack the red figure.","Unfortunately, there was a huge gap in strength between them and Feng Jiu. With Feng Jiu’s current strength, only the Great Emperor of the North, who was also at the Great Emperor level, could fight her. The others were no match for her!","Feng Jiu glanced at them indifferently, waved her hand, and at the same time, a clear shout came out of her mouth: “Get lost!”","A powerful and terrifying pressure visible to the naked eye swept out from her sleeves and attacked the dozens of cultivators like a wave. The powerful pressure was accompanied by the pressure of ancient divine beasts and her own strength.","Once it struck,the dozens of cultivators let out a miserable cry and were sent flying, crashing down below, spitting blood and unable to stand up for a long time.","Seeing this scene, the middle-aged man’s face changed, and he couldn’t help but turn back to look at the Great Emperor Northern Flame. He immediately said, “Master, your injuries have not yet healed. If you fight her, you will definitely be at a disadvantage. Why don’t we avoid the immediate crisis and wait until your injuries have recovered before settling old scores with her?”","The Great Emperor Northern Flame knew that with only 30% of his strength left, he was no match for Feng Jiu. Looking at her imposing figure, he gritted his teeth and said hatefully, “Let’s go!” He turned and tried to run away.","However, Feng Jiu’s gaze was fixed on him, and the corners of her lips curled up slightly, revealing a cold smile. Since she had come to kill him, how could she let him escape right under her nose?"]},{"number":4838,"title":"Chapter 4838: Enraged","paragraphs":["\"Do you think you can escape?\" Feng Jiu scoffed coldly, her red figure poised in mid-air. Her hands began to form an ancient symbol before her, and as they moved, visible spiritual energy rapidly intertwined, weaving itself into a shimmering net in the air.","\"Heaven and Earth Net, spread!\" With a clear, resounding shout, she pushed her clasped hands forward, and a ray of light shot forth. Instantly, the net that had quickly manifested on the ground connected with the net in the sky, completely blocking the Great Emperor Northern Flame's escape route.","The powerful air currents at his feet twisted and coalesced into a net, swiftly forming a giant web that blocked his path and enveloped him, leaving no avenue for escape. Witnessing this, the Great Emperor Northern Flame turned back, his expression grim, his sharp, cold gaze fixed on the red figure.","\"Feng Jiu, have you truly thought this through? If you genuinely become my enemy today, it's uncertain who will live and who will die!\" His cold voice carried an unmistakable threat, and his formidable aura as a powerful being erupted forth. Even with only 30% of his power remaining, he refused to display the slightest weakness.","\"What a joke!\" Feng Jiu retorted with a cold laugh, her icy eyes fixed on him. \"From the moment you and your men became my enemies and tried to kill me, we have been enemies. Do you believe there's any chance of stopping now?\"","She extended her hand, and a blue-edged sword with a vibrant green glow materialized. She pointed the sword diagonally downward, and sword qi burst forth, unleashing the full, powerful pressure of her being.","\"You are an emperor, after all. Running away like this, what's the difference between you and a rat?\" The utter contempt and disdain in her eyes completely ignited the Great Emperor Northern Flame's fury.","\"How dare you!\" A furious roar echoed through the air. The emperor's rage caused the very atmosphere to tremble. The middle-aged man standing beside him buckled under the overwhelming pressure, feeling his blood boil within him. In the next instant, he spat out a mouthful of blood and collapsed to his knees, barely able to remain upright.","\"How arrogant and conceited Feng Jiu is! Today, I will see just how capable you really are!\" The enraged shout burst from the Great Emperor Northern Flame's mouth. The anger festering in his heart was impossible to quell; his mind was in turmoil, and his breathing grew rapid.","Even though he had only 70% of his strength left, he was still a great emperor, accustomed to being revered and high above all others. When had anyone ever dared to compare him to a lowly rat that everyone sought to exterminate? This","Feng Jiu, a mere woman, dared to be so arrogant. Today, even if it meant expending his entire remaining strength, he would teach her a lesson! He would make her understand his power!","\"Then open your dog eyes and take a good look!\" Feng Jiu scoffed coldly. In the very next moment, her red figure transformed into a streak of light, hurtling towards him at blinding speed. The Blue Edge sword in her hand shimmered with fierce sword qi, radiating a chilling, murderous aura.","\"You're looking for death!\" The Great Emperor Northern Flame's throat tightened, a mouthful of blood rushing up. He tasted the coppery tang but swallowed it back down. Seeing Feng Jiu's murderous intent charging towards him, he moved his hand, and a double-edged spear appeared. With a swift swing, it cut through the air with a sharp, whistling sound.","\"Clang!\"","He leaped forward, gathering his remaining strength, and rushed to meet her. His long spear intercepted Feng Jiu's sword, but as he closed the distance, now only three steps away from her, his heart suddenly sank with a chilling realization."]},{"number":4839,"title":"Chapter 4839: Impending Death","paragraphs":["Chapter 4839: Impending Death","The powerful pressure and surging air currents emanating from both combatants formed a protective shield, deflecting each other’s sword qi and spear qi. The two were locked in a fierce exchange, their long swords and spears clashing, the distance between them a mere three steps. Because of this proximity, the Great Emperor Northern Flame could distinctly feel the immense pressure radiating from Feng Jiu.","If he hadn’t been injured, perhaps he could have held his ground, but now, a prolonged battle would undoubtedly lead to his defeat! This thought sparked anxiety within him, though he maintained a composed expression, his mind racing to devise a counter-strategy.","Feng Jiu, however, offered him no opportunity or time. His long spear successfully parried her long sword, preventing it from piercing deeper. Both weapons were extraordinary, and the force bursting from their clash was incredibly fierce. Observing the beads of sweat forming on the Great Emperor Northern Flame’s forehead, Feng Jiu’s eyes flashed, and the corners of her lips curled into a subtle, almost mocking smile. “I didn’t expect the mighty Great Emperor Northern Flame to be so weak!”","As her taunting words hung in the air, she twisted the hand gripping the Blue Edge sword. The long sword slid across his spear, then sharply pivoted, its tip deftly avoiding his weapon and thrusting towards his throat with blinding speed.","A chilling killing intent rushed directly at him, startling the Great Emperor Northern Flame. He swiftly moved his long spear to block, but in the next instant, the sword that had been aimed at his throat was deflected just enough to slash diagonally into his shoulder.","“Ssshh! Ah!”","The sharp blade pierced his shoulder, causing a searing, fiery pain that shot straight through him, down to his very bones. He involuntarily trembled, his grip on the long spear wavering. His momentary lapse in reaction gave Feng Jiu another crucial opportunity to strike.","“Whoosh!”","The long sword was yanked from his shoulder and then swung towards his arm with spectral speed, making it almost impossible to react. As her long sword exited the Great Emperor Northern Flame’s shoulder, it brought with it a stream of blood. When the blade descended again, a piece of flesh flew off with the sword, and in an instant, a piercing scream tore through the air.","“Ah!”","That shriek echoed unsettlingly. All that could be seen was the Great Emperor Northern Flame’s pale, panicked face, now streaked with blood, and his arm hanging limply at his side, trembling slightly. At that moment, darkness momentarily swam before his eyes, and his mind went blank. The ferocious killing intent assaulting him compelled him to retreat instinctually, leaping more than ten meters into the sky before he could finally catch his breath.","Beads of sweat, as large as beans, dripped from his forehead. He lay in the air like a fish washed ashore by a tidal wave, gasping for breath with his mouth wide open. His heart pounded wildly, and fear, terror, and shock consumed his entire being.","Feng Jiu looked at him, her lips curling. Her clear voice carried through the air: “If you were an ordinary person, that move would have been a fatal blow. But as you said, you are a great emperor. If you can’t even dodge that move, then your title is nothing but a false name. However, you won’t be so lucky next time.”","In that moment, her voice sounded like the grim reaper’s call to his ears. His injuries hadn’t healed yet, and with only thirty percent of his strength remaining, he couldn’t sustain the fight for much longer. Perhaps because he had truly experienced her might firsthand, the only thought in his mind at that moment was to escape. He had no doubt that if he continued fighting, he would undoubtedly die by her hands!"]},{"number":4840,"title":"Chapter 4840: Death by a thousand cuts","paragraphs":["Chapter 4840: Death by a thousand cuts","“Want to escape?” Feng Jiu smiled coldly, her gaze fixed on his expression. She knew he was desperately seeking an exit. A chilling smile played on her lips as she glanced at the net she’d cast. “I’ve modified this net. Even if something could escape, it won’t be able to break free from the net I’ve set up. Today, you won’t be able to escape from my grasp.”","Hearing her words, the Great Emperor Northern Flame’s heart sank. He had indeed been trying to find a weak point in the net, and her words confirmed she knew his every thought. However, he refused to believe he was truly trapped!","“Vermilion Tiger! Come out!” he roared. As his voice faded, a flash of fiery light appeared, and a majestic flying tiger with a pair of wings soared into the air. It let out a deafening tiger’s roar, vibrating the very air around them.","“Roar!”","With the tiger’s roar, a powerful current of air radiated outwards. It bared its sharp claws, its tiger eyes glaring, and flapped its wings, staring at Feng Jiu with a mixture of caution and fear. This apprehension stemmed from its sensing the potent aura of an ancient divine beast emanating from the human woman before it.","Even as a Super Sacred Beast, it was no match for the power of an ancient divine beast. The Vermilion Tiger, though summoned from its spatial realm, dared not approach. Instead, it took a hesitant step back and let out a low, trembling howl. This human, it was afraid of her.","Seeing his contract beast retreat the moment it appeared, the Great Emperor Northern Flame felt a surge of extreme frustration! But he also knew that Feng Jiu’s contract beast was the ancient divine beast Fire Phoenix, against which his Super Sacred Beast stood no chance. Therefore, he hadn’t intended for his contract beast to engage Feng Jiu directly. Instead, he wanted it to locate the weakest point in the net while he continued to hold her off, thereby creating an opportunity for their escape.","“Go! Find the weakest point in this net!” he bellowed, ordering his contract beast to swiftly find a way to breach the formation. If all else failed, its flame power should at least be able to weaken Feng Jiu’s formation somewhat. At that point, even if he had to expend all his remaining strength, he would shatter this damnable net!","Feng Jiu glanced at the Super Sacred Beast, then at Great Emperor Northern Flame, who was clearly struggling. She offered him no quarter, no chance to recover his breath, and attacked again with the Blue Edge in her hand. This time, a searing flame wrapped around the blade of her long sword with a whoosh, circling the Blue Edge like a fire dragon.","The two figures clashed back and forth, with Feng Jiu primarily on the offensive and the Great Emperor Northern Flame mostly dodging. As the Emperor gradually lost his ability to keep up, he suffered more and more wounds. His robe was already stained crimson with blood, its original color indistinguishable. Feng Jiu did not aim for an immediate fatal blow; instead, she slashed at him repeatedly, as if intent on making him endure every agonizing bit of pain before his ultimate demise.","“Arghhh!” A piercing scream tore through the air as Feng Jiu thrust her sword into his thigh. He plummeted from mid-air, crashing heavily to the ground, spitting out a mouthful of blood.","“Feng Jiu! If you want to kill me, just do it! Why torture me like this?” The Great Emperor Northern Flame glared at her furiously, his body covered in countless wounds, both large and small. Each wound burned with the icy sword energy and the searing heat of flames, as if fire itself was consuming his bones and flesh, causing him unbearable agony.","Feng Jiu slowly descended from the sky, her long sword pointing diagonally towards the ground. She looked at the Great Emperor Northern Flame lying before her, and an exquisite, cold, and almost bloodthirsty smile touched her lips.","“Because of you, my husband is in a deep sleep, with only a trace of his soul remaining,” she began, her voice low and dangerous. “Because of you, my child had to leave my side to seek safety. If I don’t make you taste a life worse than death, how can I live with myself for treating me as your mortal enemy?”"]},{"number":4841,"title":"Chapter 4841: Lure","paragraphs":["The Great Emperor Northern Flame opened his mouth, but no words escaped. When he first decided to act against them, he had indeed anticipated this day might come. However, he hadn't expected it to arrive so swiftly, or under such humiliating circumstances, forcing him, a great emperor, to endure such torment and pain.","Regret? No! He only regretted not killing her when she ascended, thereby denying her the opportunity to become an immortal and his sworn enemy!","\"The victor is king, and the defeated are bandits,\" he spat hatefully, his eyes fixed on her. \"There's no point in saying anything! Kill me if you want, but I will never beg for mercy!\" Despite being covered in grievous wounds, he stood tall, the inherent dignity of a Great Emperor refusing to allow him to admit defeat in her presence.","\"Is that so? Then let's try it!\" She twisted the sword in her hand, and a fierce burst of sword qi instantly struck out, severing his limbs.","\"Ahhhhhh!\"","A shrill, agonizing scream pierced the air, reaching the clouds and echoing across the sky. The sound caused the Super Sacred Beast hovering mid-air to let out a low growl and lunge frantically at Feng Jiu.","\"Hmph!\" Feng Jiu snorted coldly, flicked her sleeve, and a powerful burst of force sent the Super Sacred Beast hurtling through the air.","\"Bang!\" The Super Sacred Beast was propelled dozens of meters away, crashing heavily to the ground, blood spilling from its mouth. It struggled to stand, but its limbs were weak, and it collapsed again, panting heavily.","\"Ah... Feng Jiu! Feng Jiu! Even if I die, I'll drag you down with me!\" The resentful voice was thick with boundless hatred. Excruciating pain and profound hatred intertwined, filling the Great Emperor Northern Flame's chest. His four limbs had been severed, and blood gushed out like a fountain. The spirit energy within his body surged uncontrollably, his hair flew wildly, and he looked like a madman or a demon. His eyes were bloodshot as he cursed angrily.","In the next moment, his body suddenly swelled up like an inflated ball, his entire face distending. A powerful current of air, infused with the unmistakable scent of death, erupted in that instant, rushing directly towards Feng Jiu. She had been standing only a few meters in front of him. He unleashed his final, desperate power to kill her and take her with him, and his speed was so immense that no one had time to dodge.","When the powerful aura exploded, Feng Jiu immediately turned and vanished into her space, narrowly avoiding the deadly airflow surging towards her. She only heard a deafening bang, followed by a sustained rumbling sound. Being within her space, she couldn't perceive anything else.","Almost at the exact moment the Great Emperor Northern Flame gathered his qi and self-detonated, the immense spiritual pressure that permeated his territory vanished with his death. In that instant, the very land where his territory was located shook violently; rocks tumbled, rivers surged, and waves roared. At that moment, almost all the monarchs and immortal elders within this vast territory sensed that something catastrophic had occurred.","Feng Jiu, who had been in her space, emerged after a short while. When she saw that the entire immortal island had been obliterated by the Great Emperor Northern Flame's self-destruction, leaving only a pile of rubble, she couldn't help but raise her eyebrows, a hint of surprise flashing across her eyes.","\"I didn't expect the power to be so strong. Fortunately, I escaped into space, otherwise, I'm afraid I wouldn't have been able to avoid this mutual destruction.\" She glanced around and released her divine sense to investigate. At this moment, not a single living thing remained on this vast, devastated immortal island. Even the Super Sacred Beast had perished in the Great Emperor Northern Flame's explosive self-destruction."]},{"number":4842,"title":"Chapter 4842: The territory changed hands","paragraphs":["Chapter 4842: The territory changed hands","As the dust and smoke gradually cleared, a flash of golden light caught Feng Jiu’s eye. She moved forward to investigate and couldn’t help but raise her eyebrows. “Huh? The Imperial Immortal Seal?”","This Imperial Immortal Seal was the emblem of an emperor who governed a particular region. It wasn’t something she had personally forged; rather, it was formed by the Way of Heaven itself during an emperor’s ascension. Feng Jiu possessed an Imperial Immortal Seal as well, though hers had a distinct blue lotus base.","“I didn’t expect this thing to be so sturdy. Everything else has been destroyed, but this Imperial Immortal Seal is still intact,” she murmured softly. She picked it up and examined it. The words “Great Emperor Northern Flame” etched on the seal had already dissolved into golden light and vanished.","A smile played on her lips as she held the imperial divine seal in one hand, while with the other, she gathered a thread of her divine soul and infused it into the artifact. Instantly, the Imperial Immortal Seal in her hand burst forth with a brilliant green light. In the next moment, it flew from her grasp and soared into the air.","A radiant green light, akin to sunlight, refracted from the seal and transformed into thousands of luminous strands that rapidly spread across the sky. With incredible speed, as the previous spiritual consciousness that permeated the realm dissipated, this new green light swiftly re-intertwined, weaving itself into a vast spiritual net that enveloped the heavens and the earth.","Those immortal lords and immortal elders who had sensed something amiss and were rushing towards the Great Emperor Northern Flame’s immortal island suddenly froze mid-journey, staring blankly at the green light now appearing in the sky.","“What... what is that?” An immortal elder stared in utter shock, his eyes wide as he gazed at the visible green light.","“New spirit consciousness? How is this possible!” another immortal old man exclaimed, his voice laced with incredulity as he witnessed the powerful spiritual network rapidly interweaving and replacing the previous spiritual presence.","Elsewhere, several other immortal old men, also en route to the Great Emperor Northern Flame’s immortal island, halted in mid-air, looking up at the sky in stunned disbelief. “What on earth is going on? How could this be?” one of the immortal lords asked incredulously.","Another immortal elder’s face turned pale, and he muttered, “Could it be... Could the Great Emperor Northern Flame have... fallen?”","Hearing this, another immortal elder gasped, immediately refuting the idea. “How could that be! That’s the Great Emperor Northern Flame! He has a lifespan as long as the heavens and the earth; how could he have fallen? This is impossible!”","The immortal who had spoken earlier was pale, his figure swaying slightly. Lost in thought, he muttered, “Even if he has a lifespan as long as the heavens and the earth, what if he didn’t die of old age, but was killed?”","When he finished speaking, silence descended upon the group. For a moment, even their breathing seemed to stop. They couldn’t imagine, nor did they dare to imagine, that the mighty Great Emperor Northern Flame could actually be killed by someone! If he truly was killed by someone, then how incredibly powerful would that individual be?","Originally, they had been rushing towards the immortal island, but now they hesitated, gripped by panic. They feared that if they proceeded, they would encounter the very person who had brought down the Great Emperor Northern Flame. At this moment, even if they didn’t want to admit it, they had no choice but to acknowledge that only with the death of the Great Emperor Northern Flame would the spiritual consciousness that covered this world dissipate. And in just such a short time, the emperor of their world had actually been replaced!"]},{"number":4843,"title":"Chapter 4843: It’s really her","paragraphs":["Chapter 4843: It’s really her","“Who do you think it could be?” asked an immortal with a hoarse voice, the gravity of the situation heavy in his tone.","An immortal next to him shook his head. “I don’t know. With the Great Emperor Northern Flame’s strength, how could he be killed? Who has the ability to kill him? Killing an emperor is no joke. Who would dare?”","Another immortal stroked his beard thoughtfully. “A few days ago, I visited the Phoenix Sovereign’s territory, and the spiritual consciousness there seemed to be the same as ours.”","“Hiss! How is that possible!” The immortal lord beside him gasped, his disbelief palpable. “The Phoenix Sovereign ascended not long ago, and she is just a woman. How could she kill the Great Emperor Northern Flame? I don’t believe it!” He simply couldn’t conceive that the Phoenix Sovereign, so recently ascended, could achieve such a feat.","“It’s useless to talk about it,” an immortal interjected, looking at the others. “No matter who becomes the new emperor here, we should go and pay him a visit, don’t you think so?”","The others nodded in agreement. “Yes, no matter who this person is, he will be the emperor of our territory from now on. We must pay him a visit, no matter what. Moreover, not only did we notice this, but I believe the other immortal lords and immortals have also noticed it, and they will definitely pay him a visit as well.”","With that, they exchanged glances and said, “If we don’t go now, when will we? Let’s go!” As soon as they finished speaking, they instantly transformed into several beams of light and shot towards the sky.","At this moment, Feng Jiu watched as the Immortal Seal slowly descended back into her hand after she had successfully reapplied her spiritual consciousness. She played with it for a moment, admiring its new resonance with her, before finally storing it in her spatial realm.","Only then did she look at the devastated Immortal Island. Everything on the immortal island had been obliterated; even the mountains had been leveled to the ground. With her current strength, it wouldn’t be difficult to use immortal techniques to restore it, but she pondered what to do with the island itself. She already possessed a vast immortal island of her own, one that had almost everything she needed, so she naturally couldn’t abandon her own domain to reside here.","“It’s too wasteful to leave it here to ruin,” she murmured softly. “After all, it was bestowed by the heavens, and the immortality energy here is incomparable to ordinary places.” She considered her options and finally decided to move this entire immortal island to her own, merging them together to expand her territory.","“Yes, let’s do it!” A hint of satisfaction gleamed in her eyes. Just as she was about to use her immortal powers to begin the restoration, she sensed someone approaching.","She closed her eyes and released her divine sense to investigate. She saw that it wasn’t just one or two individuals, but a multitude: the immortal lords and immortal elders of this territory, as well as some powerful beings from other regions.","Her eyes flashed, and her red figure turned, rising into the air, standing with her hands clasped behind her back, facing the gentle breeze.","The immortal lords and immortal elders, still some distance away from the immortal island, clearly saw the red figure standing in the air. When they recognized her, almost everyone was stunned, their faces contorted with unconcealed shock and astonishment. When they had set out, they had speculated about who this new, powerful presence might be. Even if someone had suggested it was the Phoenix Sovereign, who had only recently ascended, they hadn’t truly believed it. But at this moment, as they beheld that striking red figure standing gracefully in mid-air, looking down upon them, their hearts suddenly trembled, and their minds were overwhelmed with astonishment and profound shock.","“It’s... it’s really her... It’s truly the Phoenix Sovereign who just ascended!”"]},{"number":4844,"title":"Chapter 4844: Pay respects to the Phoenix Sovereign","paragraphs":["Even though none of these immortal lords and immortals had ever personally seen the newly ascended Phoenix Sovereign, they had all heard the pervasive rumors: she was a woman of unparalleled beauty and charm, always adorned in striking red clothes. It was said that anyone who saw her once would forever be imprinted with her face.","At this moment, despite their lack of prior visual confirmation, looking at the exquisitely poised woman in red standing serenely in mid-air, they instinctively knew that this person had to be the Phoenix Sovereign!","\"What are you doing here?\" Feng Jiu's voice, cold and infused with a powerful aura, resonated through the air, clearly reaching every ear below.","It was her chilling tone that jolted them back from their stunned awe. They quickly lowered their heads, not daring to meet her gaze directly. One of the elder immortals, quicker to react than the others, swiftly lowered his robe and knelt before her.","\"We have come to pay our respects to the Phoenix Sovereign,\" he declared, his voice firm despite his inner trepidation. \"From now on, we will be the Phoenix Sovereign's loyal subjects. For the rest of our lives, we will revere the Phoenix Sovereign and obey her every command!\"","As soon as the old immortal's voice rang out, everyone else snapped back to their senses. Those who had initially hesitated immediately followed suit, dropping to their knees to pay their respects.","\"We have come to pay our respects to the Phoenix Sovereign. From now on, we will be the Phoenix Sovereign's loyal subjects. We will revere the Phoenix Sovereign and obey her every command for the rest of our lives!\"","Regardless of their private thoughts, no matter how profound their shock, the reality was undeniable: the Great Emperor Northern Flame had fallen, and the Phoenix Sovereign now ruled over their world. She was their sovereign, and they had no choice but to submit! Even if she was just a woman, in the face of her overwhelming strength and undeniable status, they had to kneel respectfully before her, without a trace of insolence or disrespect.","The voices of the kneeling crowd, imbued with their spiritual energy, converged into a single, powerful force, echoing mightily in the air. Feng Jiu stood calmly in the air, facing the wind, looking down at the multitude of powerful beings prostrated beneath her. Countless influential figures knelt at her feet, treating her as their supreme ruler. Yet, in this moment, her mood remained as serene as usual, devoid of any discernible excitement or joy.","It was as if this was merely the natural order of things, a state she had long grown accustomed to. The crowd remained kneeling, their heads bowed to their palms. No voice from above instructed them to rise. At that moment, they dared not lift their heads, dared not stand up, and dared not display the slightest hint of dissatisfaction.","They knew that there was an insurmountable gap in strength between them and the Phoenix Sovereign. If she desired to end their lives, even though they were noble Immortal Lords, she could extinguish their existence with a mere flick of her finger. Another unsettling thought nagged at them: just a few days prior, they had acted upon the Great Emperor Northern Flame's orders and cut off the Phoenix Sovereign's supply of goods. If she held that against them, they were truly afraid that...","This realization sent cold sweat beading on the foreheads of those kneeling, dripping onto the ground below. They felt an icy chill spread through their bodies, their hearts pounding with profound fear and unease. Feng Jiu intended to temper their initial enthusiasm, so she allowed them to remain kneeling, holding them in that position. It was a long while before she finally spoke.","\"I will not pursue your past actions, but from this moment on, if anyone disobeys me, their fate will be the same as that of the Great Emperor Northern Flame, whose remains have been reduced to dust!\" Her cold voice carried a chilling tone. She spoke slowly and calmly, yet her words sent a shiver down everyone's spine, like a terrifying wave!"]},{"number":4845,"title":"Chapter 4845: Alarm","paragraphs":["Chapter 4845: Alarm","The Great Emperor Northern Flame is indeed dead!","And he really did die at the hands of the Phoenix Sovereign!","Even though they had already guessed as much, when they heard the words come out of her mouth, everyone was still shocked.","“Yes, we dare not have any second thoughts.” Everyone hurriedly said.","“Get up!” Feng Jiu said, her gaze falling on the immortal who had knelt down first, and asked, “Organize everyone’s information and send it to my immortal island when the time comes.”","“Old Qinghua Immortal, I will obey the Phoenix Sovereign’s orders.” The old man was a little surprised and hurriedly responded with a bow, reporting his name at the same time.","“Everyone, withdraw!” Feng Jiu said, her gaze sweeping over the crowd.","Everyone responded with a bow, then dispersed.","Feng Jiu watched them leave, and when they had all disappeared from view, she looked at the ruined immortal island. In the next moment, she gathered her immortal power and waved her sleeves, and one after another, exquisite and magnificent immortal palaces reappeared below...","In Yunxiao Mountain, the Azure Emperor sensed the death of the Great Emperor Northern Flame.","He left his cave abode and looked up at the distant sky with his hands behind his back, a hint of surprise flashing across his eyes: “I didn’t expect Feng Jiu to actually kill the Great Emperor Northern Flame. It seems that they must have been seriously injured by that blow!”","If it weren’t for Feng Jiu’s strike when she ascended, even with her full strength and cultivation, it would not have been so easy to kill the Great Emperor Northern Flame. But now she was able to kill him, which meant that all four Great Emperors had been seriously injured by that strike.","“Once the news of the Great Emperor Northern Flame’s death spreads, the other three should also be afraid.” He said in a low voice, chuckled and shook his head.","They were already great emperors, why provoke Feng Jiu? Wasn’t that asking for death?","At the same time, when Mo Chen sensed something unusual in the Immortal Palace, he also came out to take a look, shook his head, and revealed a helpless smile: “I said we wouldn’t touch those people for now, but I didn’t expect that after only a few days, one of them has already been killed.”","He knew Feng Jiu’s strength, and with her vengeful nature, it was only a matter of time before the Four Great Emperors would meet their end from the moment they became Feng Jiu’s enemies.","Now that one was dead, not only would the other three be afraid, but all sides would be alarmed, especially those Great Emperors who had withdrawn from the world. Even if they didn’t care about worldly affairs, after this incident, they would surely hear of Feng Jiu’s name...","Mo Chen’s guess was correct. Not only did the three Great Emperors who were in seclusion recovering from their injuries know that the Great Emperor Northern Flame was dead, but even the Great Emperors who had been hiding from the world were alarmed by the death and replacement of one of their peers, and they sent people to find out everything they could about Feng Jiu.","In contrast, Feng Jiu was busy rearranging the newly recovered immortal island. Once everything was in order, she would bring the floating immortal island back to her immortal island and merge the two islands to expand her territory.","After waiting for three days at the inn, Song Mi’er saw that Feng Jiu had not returned, so she couldn’t help but glance at the little beast sleeping on the chair. Because she had said something wrong that day, the little beast didn’t pay much attention to her and even pushed her away when she tried to touch it.","“Little Cloud, your Master hasn’t come back yet. How about we go out for a walk?”"]},{"number":4846,"title":"Chapter 4846: Dispute","paragraphs":["Chapter 4846: Dispute","Song Mi’er stood up, a smile gracing her lips as she looked at the fluffy creature. “It’s been a few days since we’ve had anything exciting to do. Let’s go out and buy some food! When we get back, I’ll cook you a delicious meal. How about it?”","Cloud Devouring glanced at her. It was undeniably true that she was an excellent cook. It had savored her culinary creations just two days prior, and they had indeed been exceptionally delicious. So, it straightened itself, jumped down from the chair, and dutifully followed her.","“I didn’t expect that! You’re also a glutton, no wonder you’re so fat,” Song Mi’er teased, letting out a laugh. She couldn’t resist the urge to reach out and playfully touch Cloud Devouring’s soft, plump fur once more.","Cloud Devouring, in response, cast a disdainful look at her and deftly dodged her hand.","Song Mi’er didn’t mind in the slightest. She opened the door, and with Cloud Devouring trailing behind, headed straight for the bustling market. Unlike many other young women who preferred Browse jewelry stores or shops selling pretty clothes and knick-knacks, Song Mi’er found her joy wandering through the market, meticulously seeking out all sorts of kitchen knives.","“Fresh lingzhi mushrooms, fresh lingzhi mushrooms! Hey, madam, take a look at these lingzhi mushrooms. They were just picked and are still very fresh!” A man’s voice boomed from within an alleyway, calling out to passersby.","A young woman and a small beast ambled through the market. Song Mi’er was scanning her surroundings when her ears caught the man’s shouts about selling lingzhi mushrooms. She casually glanced over and saw several mats laid out on the ground in the alley, with piles of the mushrooms resting on them. Her eyes lit up.","“Are these freshly picked?” She squatted down, picked one up, examined it closely, and then brought it to her nose to inhale its scent, a happy smile spreading across her face. “They still have the smell of soil!”","The vendor, seeing a potential customer, quickly offered a wide smile. “Miss, buy some lingzhi mushrooms to make soup and cook with! They are all incredibly fresh, just picked, and taste absolutely delicious! And the price is quite reasonable, I assure you.”","“How much are they?” Song Mi’er inquired.","“Ten gold coins per catty,” the man stated, looking at her expectantly. “If you buy a lot, I’ll even give you a discount. How about that?”","Hearing the price, Song Mi’er couldn’t help but widen her eyes, staring at him in surprise. “Ten gold coins per catty?”","Seeing her expression, the man misinterpreted her surprise as concern over the price and quickly interjected. “Miss, these mushrooms are very fresh and quite different from ordinary mushrooms. They are also very hard to find. How about this? If you still think it’s too expensive, I’ll give them to you for eight gold coins per catty. Buy a catty to try, and if you like them, you can always come back for more.”","“Whoa, that’s fantastic! Wrap them all up, I’ll take them all!” Her eyes sparkled with delight, and she waved her hand excitedly, staring brightly at the pile of lingzhi mushrooms the man was selling. These were, in fact, incredibly precious lingzhi mushrooms. She remembered the dishes her father had prepared with them back home, and they were truly exquisite. However, they were exceptionally rare and difficult to come by, and very few people recognized their true value, often mistaking them for common fungi.","Hearing her declaration, the man’s face lit up with joy. “Oh, oh!” he quickly agreed. “I just have ten and a half catties left, so I’ll give you all ten catties.”","Song Mi’er swiftly produced the money, handing him two hundred gold coins. “Big Brother, please keep this money safe,” she said. “By the way, where did you pick these mushrooms?”","The man was taken aback by her generosity and paused for a moment before replying. “I picked them in Huashan Mountain, where there’s a dense forest of mixed Huashan pine and oak trees.”","“Thank you, Big Brother,” Song Mi’er said with a bright smile. She was about to reach for the mushrooms when a voice abruptly cut in.","“I want that!”"]},{"number":4847,"title":"Chapter 4847: Good Stuff","paragraphs":["The voice was suddenly followed by a pair of large hands that snatched the wrapped bag. Seeing her purchase stolen before her very eyes, Song Mi'er immediately rushed forward to grab it. However, the middle-aged man holding the bag quickly backed away. As he opened the bag, a surprised smile spread across his face upon seeing its contents.","\"Oh, it's this!\" He then pulled out a money bag and threw it at the man. \"I'll buy this.\"","The man was taken aback. He looked at the money bag, then at Song Mi'er, and finally said apologetically to the middle-aged man, \"Sir, I already sold these mushrooms to this lady.\"","\"Is that so? Then I'll buy them from you,\" the middle-aged man said, looking at Song Mi'er before turning to leave with the mushrooms.","\"Give me back my stuff!\" Song Mi'er was furious. From seemingly nowhere, she produced a kitchen knife, grabbed it, and swung it forward. A sharp gust of wind whistled past the middle-aged man, who was startled and instinctively dodged. The kitchen knife whizzed past him and plunged into the ground.","\"Give me back my things! Otherwise, don't even think about leaving!\" Song Mi'er shouted, lunging forward to grab the bag from the middle-aged man's hand.","\"You dare to fight me? You're looking for death!\" the middle-aged man snorted, backing away. At that moment, two men in black jumped out from the shadows, blocking Song Mi'er's attack.","\"You have help!\" Song Mi'er gritted her teeth and brandished her own weapon.","\"Am I seeing this right? Is that girl pulling out a frying pan? Can a frying pan really be used as a weapon?\"","Witnessing the fight, some nearby onlookers stared in astonishment at the frying pan, which looked just like the ones in their kitchens.","\"Why is that girl fighting with Chef Wei from Wei's Fragrant Restaurant? Chef Wei is a member of the Wei family. Everyone here knows him. Why doesn't she give him some face? They're just some spirit mushrooms. They're not a big deal. Is it worth offending Chef Wei?\"","\"Don't run! Give me back my stuff!\" Song Mi'er shouted, growing anxious as she saw the middle-aged man turn and leave with her spirit mushrooms. Cloud Devouring, who had been overlooked because he looked like a small pet, glanced at Song Mi'er. Seeing that she was holding her own against the two men, he swiftly moved past her and rushed after the middle-aged man.","Meanwhile, the middle-aged man was walking back, happy with his find, completely unaware that a small pet—no, a mini version of a Super Sacred Beast—was following him. Cloud Devouring was in no hurry to attack. He followed the man as he turned left and right and entered an alley. Suddenly, he lunged from behind and kicked the man hard with his two hind legs.","\"Ahhhhh!\"","The middle-aged man cried out in surprise as he was sent flying by a tremendous force. The bag he was holding was snatched away, and he crashed into the alley wall, his head bleeding profusely. When he wiped the blood from his forehead and looked back, the alley was empty—not even a ghost was in sight. Even the bag of spirit mushrooms had vanished.","\"Damn it! Who is it? Who dared to steal my things!\"","He gritted his teeth in anger and roared, then stood up with the help of the wall and rushed out to chase after the thief, looking around but not knowing where to start. At that moment, Cloud Devouring was making its way back with the bag of spirit mushrooms in its mouth. It looked like a small, snow-white, chubby beast with a large bag in its mouth, drawing the attention of people on the street."]},{"number":4848,"title":"Chapter 4848: Battle Prowess","paragraphs":["Chapter 4848: Battle Prowess","“Look at that little pet,” a man said, looking curiously at the chubby creature. “It’s not only cute but also holding a big bag in its mouth.”","“What a cute little pet. I wonder where you bought it? I want one too,” a young girl said, completely charmed. She couldn’t help but follow the adorable pet with her eyes, watching its hips sway as it walked. Her eyes lit up, and she pulled on the young man beside her. “Brother, I want a pet like that too—it’s so cute!”","“I don’t know what kind of pet that is. It’s very rare. It’s probably the baby of some kind of spirit beast!” the young man said thoughtfully, also staring at the little beast that ran with a side-to-side gait. He believed such a creature was truly unique.","“Brother, let’s go see who this little pet belongs to,” the young girl said, pulling her brother forward.","At that moment, the middle-aged man had caught up. After asking around, someone told him they had seen a cute little beast running toward them with a bag in its mouth, so he naturally came looking for it. Over there, Song Mi’er turned the frying pan in her hand, and it instantly became several times larger. She fiercely slammed it toward the two men in black.","“Get out of here!”","As her angry shout rang out, she swung the frying pan with both hands and hit the two men hard with the bottom of the pan, sending them flying.","“Ah!”","Two screams rang out, and the two black-clad guards were instantly knocked dozens of meters away, crashing heavily onto the street. The crowd watched in shock, their eyes wide with disbelief. They stared at the angry young girl, unable to believe what they were seeing. Two grown men had been sent flying dozens of meters by the bottom of a frying pan. Moreover, that ordinary-looking frying pan could actually change size! It looked like a treasure!","Not far away, Cloud Devouring was returning with the bag in his mouth when he saw Song Mi’er send the two men flying with the pan. The corners of his mouth twitched. His master probably never imagined that such a petite girl could be so strong.","“Ah! Cloud Devouring! Did you get my things back?”","Song Mi’er, who had been furious a moment ago, saw the small, snow-white pet standing not far away, biting the bag that had contained the spirit mushrooms. Her eyes lit up, and a surprised and delighted smile appeared on her face. She hurried over with the frying pan, took the bag from its mouth, opened it, and confirmed that it was indeed the items she had purchased earlier. She quickly put them away in her space so no one could steal them again.","“You did a great job today. I’ll give you extra chicken legs when we get back!”","Song Mi’er said with a smile, just as she saw the middle-aged man from earlier returning. She immediately grabbed Cloud Devouring and said anxiously, “No! That old thief is coming back!” Cloud Devouring hadn’t even reacted before she snatched it and ran, causing the creature to roll its eyes in disbelief. It was a Super Sacred Beast—did it really need to run for its life?","“Don’t run! Stop right there!” The middle-aged man’s face was stained with blood. As soon as he saw the girl and the beast turn and run, he immediately gave chase, shouting, “Stop right there!” No one knew that Feng Jiu had just finished her business and was on her way over..."]},{"number":4849,"title":"Chapter 4849: Here","paragraphs":["Chapter 4849: Here","The city, already under the control of powerful clans, was abuzz with news of the incident. It quickly reached the ears of several families, particularly the Wei family, who immediately dispatched men to capture the culprits. After all, this was their territory. If they allowed outsiders to bully their people, how could they maintain their standing in the city?","As the Wei family’s men moved to surround Song Mi’er, Feng Jiu, dressed in red, was walking through the city gates. She didn’t expect her trip to have been so smooth. When she went to the Immortal Island to find the Great Emperor Northern Flame, she was just trying her luck. Even if he wasn’t there, she would still destroy his lair to dampen his spirit. To her surprise, he hadn’t gone anywhere else to hide and recover from his injuries; he had stayed on the Immortal Island.","Having dealt with such a formidable enemy, she felt an inexplicable sense of relief and happiness. Only three enemies remained, but she was in no hurry. She would take them down one by one; it was only a matter of time.","Walking down the street, Feng Jiu was about to enter an inn when she saw the innkeeper rush out with an anxious expression. “Oh my, young lady, you’re finally back,” he said.","Feng Jiu raised an eyebrow. “What’s wrong? Did something happen?”","“The young lady traveling with you is in big trouble,” the innkeeper replied. “I heard from guests that she offended someone from the Wei family and is now being surrounded by them on West Street! I heard the Wei family threatened to break the young lady’s legs and even said they would stew her pet and eat it!”","Hearing this, Feng Jiu’s lips curved into a slight smile. “I see. Thank you for letting me know.” She nodded slightly and asked, “Which way is West Street?”","“Go straight down this street, turn left, go straight for 200 metres, then turn right, and you’ll be there,” the innkeeper explained. He looked at her again and said hesitantly, “Miss, you’re not going there alone, are you? If you go alone, remember not to provoke the Wei family again.”","“I know, shopkeeper. Please ask the waiter to prepare some water for me to bathe. We’ll be back soon,” Feng Jiu said with a light smile, then walked toward the street the shopkeeper had indicated.","Seeing this, the shopkeeper paused for a moment before shouting, “Waiter, hurry up and boil some water and bring it to the guest room at the back of the second floor.” Judging by the woman in red’s demeanor, she must come from an extraordinary background, so maybe nothing would happen after all.","On West Street, Song Mi’er hugged Cloud Devouring and glared at the people surrounding her. “How dare you! What are you doing in broad daylight?” she challenged.","“Hmph! You stupid girl! I’ll show you!” The middle-aged man with the head injury snorted coldly, glaring at Song Mi’er before waving his hand and shouting, “Grab her!”","“Hmph, I’d like to see you try!” Song Mi’er glared angrily and, with a quick movement, the frying pan appeared in her hand again. When the middle-aged man saw the pan, he recalled the previous scene, and a fiery, covetous look appeared in his eyes.","“Grab her! Grab her for me!” he yelled. He believed that the frying pan, which could change in size, must be a magical artifact. It could be used to cook food and as a weapon for self-defense. Such a treasure was perfect for a chef like him.","Cloud Devouring glanced at the people around him, darted out of Song Mi’er’s arms, and landed steadily beside her."]},{"number":4850,"title":"Chapter 4850: Ran off","paragraphs":["Chapter 4850: Ran off","Though her fighting style was unconventional, Song Mi’er’s lethal moves made her a formidable opponent. She faced the four men with her frying pan, holding her own with remarkable strength despite her small stature. Every time she struck a guard, they were forced to retreat several steps.","When Feng Jiu arrived on West Street, she found a crowd too dense to push through. Instead, she went to the second floor of a teahouse overlooking the street, where she sat down and ordered a pot of tea. The moment she settled in, Cloud Devouring sensed her presence. He looked up and saw her leaning against the railing, watching the scene unfold below.","Feng Jiu glanced down, smiled, and winked at him. Cloud Devouring then crouched, observing Song Mi’er handle the dozen or so guards with surprising ease. He had expected her to be overwhelmed, but she was holding her own effortlessly.","From the teahouse, Feng Jiu sipped her tea, amused by Song Mi’er’s fighting technique, which looked exactly like stir-frying. She’d never heard of such a martial art, but judging by the skill, the technique was extremely well-practiced. To Feng Jiu, it seemed Song Mi’er wasn’t treating her opponents as men at all, but rather as ingredients in a frying pan. Her moves were impressive; eleven men were no match for her.","Feng Jiu’s eyes narrowed when she saw the middle-aged man’s hand twitch slightly. Something slipped from his sleeve, and a hidden weapon flew toward Song Mi’er. With a flick of her wrist, Feng Jiu sent a gust of wind to knock the weapon away. At the same time, a few drops of tea flew from her cup, instantly freezing into ice and striking the middle-aged man’s limbs.","“Arghhhh!” A scream rang out. The middle-aged man convulsed and collapsed, his body emitting a chilling cold. In moments, his face and eyebrows were covered in frost.","“Master Wei!” the guards shouted in shock. They rushed to his side, helped him up, and, forgetting the fight, carried him back to the Wei family’s compound.","“Hmph! You think I’m an easy target? How dare you bully me? Have you asked my frying pan?” Song Mi’er snorted, raising her chin with a smug smile as she brandished the deadly frying pan.","Cloud Devouring walked over and gently tapped her foot with his claw.","“What’s wrong?” Song Mi’er asked, looking down at the chubby pet.","Cloud Devouring glanced up at the teahouse’s second floor before running up the stairs. Song Mi’er followed his gaze and saw Feng Jiu, dressed in a red robe, holding a teacup and smiling at her. She couldn’t help but cry out in surprise.","“Sister, you’re back!” She happily followed Cloud Devouring upstairs, sat at the table, and said, “Sister, when did you get back? Why are you here?”","Feng Jiu smiled and replied, “I just got here. I heard you were fighting with someone, so I came to take a look.”"]},{"number":4851,"title":"Chapter 4851: Heirloom","paragraphs":["Chapter 4851: Heirloom","“Those people wanted to steal my things! I bought something nice at the market today. Sister, have you eaten yet? How about I make you something delicious?” Song Mi’er said with a smile.","Hearing her change from calling her Feng Jiu to sister, and now directly calling her sister, Feng Jiu just smiled, glanced at her, and said, “Sure! I haven’t eaten in days.”","She smiled and asked, “What good things did you buy that made those people want to steal them?”","“This, sister, do you know what this is?” Song Mi’er mysteriously took out the mushrooms and showed them to Feng Jiu.","Seeing that, Feng Jiu raised her eyebrows and laughed, “So it’s this! I’ve eaten it before; they’re lingzhi mushrooms!” No matter how good this thing was, it wasn’t anything rare or precious to her, but seeing how she treasured it, she couldn’t help but find it amusing.","“These are hard to find. I bought them at the market. They’re delicious in stews and soups, and they contain pure spirit energy, which is very nourishing,” said Song Mi’er as she carefully put the mushrooms away.","Feng Jiu smiled, took a sip of tea, and asked, “Mi’er, I see that all your moves are cooking moves. Could this be a martial art passed down in your family?”","“Sister, you’re really smart.”","She gave Feng Jiu a thumbs up and said with a smile, “Isn’t my family a family of chefs? Our family is a family of chefs, so naturally we practice martial arts that are unique to our family. Don’t be fooled by the cooking moves; they’ve been modified and can easily deal with ten people.”","“Where did you get that frying pan? It looks like a valuable treasure.” Feng Jiu drank her tea and looked at her leisurely as she asked.","“My father used it before, then passed it down to me. I heard that it was made by a very skilled weapon master a long time ago, and it’s the only one of its kind! None of my brothers have one, so my father left it to me.” Speaking of this, she couldn’t help but smile happily. She felt that her father loved her the most.","Hearing this, Feng Jiu nodded and said, “If I have the chance, I’d really like to meet your family. I’m sure they’re all very talented people.”","Hearing this, Song Mi’er’s eyes lit up and she said, “Sister, when I go home, will you come with me? You can stay at my house for a while. I promise you’ll get to eat different delicious food every day. If you come to my house, everyone there will be very happy.”","“Mm, when I have the chance, I’ll definitely go.” She smiled and said, “Let’s go back to the inn first.”","So, they headed back to the inn. The innkeeper was a little surprised to see them return unharmed and hurriedly invited them in, saying, “Miss, the bath water is ready.”","“Thank you,” Feng Jiu replied, nodding to him.","“Sister, you go take a bath first! I’ll go to the kitchen and cook for you,” Song Mi’er said, not waiting for her to reply, and ran to the kitchen, eager to cook with her new ingredients.","Feng Jiu shook her head, smiled, and went upstairs to take a bath, while Cloud Devouring stayed outside the room to guard it.","The Wei Family","“Who dares to go against the Wei family? Have you found out?” The middle-aged man on the seat of honour stared grimly at the people kneeling below him.","“Yes, Patriarch, they should be from out of town. They don’t look like they’re from our city,” said the guard kneeling below."]},{"number":4852,"title":"Chapter 4852: Comes Again","paragraphs":["Chapter 4852: Comes Again","Hearing this, the middle-aged man on the seat of honor frowned even more. He stood up with his hands behind his back, paced a few steps in the hall, then ordered, “Go, ask the two guardians to go and bring her back!”","“Yes, sir!” The guards responded immediately.","If the family’s revered elders went to arrest her, they would definitely be able to bring the woman back. After all, anyone who had become a revered elder of a noble family must have exceptional abilities. For the other noble families in the city, this was nothing more than a trivial matter. They heard the news but didn’t give it much thought. Besides, it wasn’t them who had lost face, but the Wei family. Naturally, they treated the whole affair as nothing more than a show to watch.","As for the two guardians of the Wei family, when they heard the order from the Patriarch, they were displeased. They were guardians after all, with extraordinary abilities. If they were asked to deal with stronger opponents or handle more difficult matters, it would be understandable, but now they were being asked to go and catch a little girl? Even though they were dissatisfied, they didn’t dare say much. After all, the order came from the Patriarch, and they were in the Wei family’s employ, so it was only right that they did as they were told.","So, the two followed the guards down the road, with one of them muttering, “She’s just a little girl. I didn’t think we’d have to deal with her ourselves.”","“Since it’s the Patriarch’s order, we’ll just do as we’re told,” the other man said as he walked slowly. “Let’s catch her and return early so we can report back.”","“Have you heard? The Great Emperor Northern Flame is dead and gone. Now, the Phoenix Sovereign has taken over. The news has already spread secretly, and I believe it won’t be long before everyone knows.” One of them whispered.","“I just heard about it this morning. Some of the family heads already know, but it hasn’t spread outside yet,” the man replied. “Come to think of it, the Phoenix Sovereign has only been promoted for a short time! The Great Emperor Northern Flame had been famous for a long time and was so powerful. I never thought...” The man sighed and shook his head.","“You’re not the only one who didn’t expect it. No one could have imagined it! Not long ago, the Great Emperor Northern Flame ordered that all resources be cut off, and now this has happened. All the people from the various families are worried that the Phoenix Sovereign will settle the score in the autumn!”","The two whispered to each other until the person leading the way stopped.","“Two Guardians, we’ve heard that the person is inside this inn,” the guard said, taking a step back. He was still scared by the frying pan, and his face still hurt from being hit.","At this moment, Feng Jiu was taking a break in her room after her bath. She hadn’t had time to rest while dealing with matters these past few days. Now that she had taken a bath, she was completely relaxed, and sleepiness was overwhelming her.","Cloud Devouring was crouching outside the room. It was a small, snow-white, and chubby creature, causing everyone going up and down the stairs to look involuntarily at the little pet in front of the innermost door. Song Mi’er was still busy in the kitchen, unaware that the Wei family had come looking for her again.","Upstairs, Cloud Devouring seemed to sense something. It stood up, walked to the second-floor balcony, glanced at the front door, thought for a moment, and then walked downstairs.","At that moment, a young girl was pulling a middle-aged man toward the inn, complaining, “Second Uncle, if you hadn’t sent someone to grab me and my brother earlier, I might have found out where that little pet was bought.”"]},{"number":4853,"title":"Chapter 4853: Who’s talking?","paragraphs":["They had originally gone to see the commotion, but halfway there, her second uncle sent people to grab them and bring them back. Now, she had pestered her second uncle so much that he finally agreed to take her out. However, when the middle-aged man being pulled by the young girl saw the people in front of the inn, he frowned and stopped in his tracks.","\"Second Uncle?\"","The girl called out, following his gaze, and saw the people in front of the inn. She couldn't help but say contemptuously in a low voice, \"Second Uncle, those are the Wei family. I don't think they're very nice. They're always bullying people.\"","\"Don't get involved in this. Let's go over there and have some tea.\" Seeing this, the middle-aged man took them to a teahouse not far away.","\"Are you staying here with a woman who has a little white pet? Call her out for us.\" One of the guardians said to the innkeeper who came to greet them.","Upon hearing this, the innkeeper's smile froze slightly, and he said, \"Please wait a moment.\" With that, he hurried into the kitchen.","Song Mi'er was cooking and was in a good mood, working enthusiastically, when she heard a knock on the kitchen door. \"Miss, miss, the Wei family is here. Miss, miss, come out quickly.\"","Because she didn't like being disturbed while cooking, she had paid the innkeeper well, so there was only her in the kitchen at that moment. Plus, she had closed the kitchen door, so even if the innkeeper wanted to enter, he couldn't, and could only shout from outside the kitchen.","\"I'm busy right now. Tell them to come back later if they want to fight!\" Song Mi'er shouted, focused on what she was doing.","Cloud Devouring, who was walking down the stairs, rolled his eyes when he heard the words coming from the kitchen. This person really had no brains. Did others have to wait for her to be free before they could cause trouble for her?","\"Hey, young lady, you'd better come out! It's the two guardians of the Wei family. They're not easy to deal with,\" the shopkeeper shouted anxiously.","\"Alright, don't bother her. Let her cook,\" Cloud Devouring said as he came down the stairs.","The shopkeeper froze when he heard the voice and looked around. \"Who? Who's talking?\"","The waiter next to him was pale and tugged at the shopkeeper's sleeve.","The shopkeeper slapped the waiter's hand away and snapped, \"If you have something to say, just say it. Why are you pulling my clothes? Have you forgotten your manners?\"","The waiter swallowed hard, withdrew his hand, and said in a trembling voice, \"Shopkeeper, it's that little pet talking.\" He pointed to the little white pet coming down the stairs, his heart pounding.","A talking pet? What kind of rank is that? The shopkeeper looked toward the staircase and saw the little pet glance at them, then walk out.","\"Did you hear that right? Is it really talking?\" The shopkeeper's expression changed, and he couldn't help but confirm again.","\"Yes, I heard right, it's talking.\" The second waiter nodded in bewilderment.","The shopkeeper was stunned and muttered, \"I misjudged it, I misjudged it, I didn't expect this!\" With that, he quickly recovered and followed after it. When he arrived at the door of the inn, he bowed to the two guardians and said sheepishly, \"Excuse me, the young lady said she is cooking. Could you please come back later?\"","Hearing this, the two guardians' faces darkened, and they immediately shouted, \"Tell her to come out immediately! Otherwise, don't blame us for being rude!\"","\"You'd better speak softly and not disturb my Master's sleep, otherwise, don't blame me for being rude!\""]},{"number":4854,"title":"Chapter 4854: That’s not an ordinary pet!","paragraphs":["Chapter 4854: That’s not an ordinary pet!","“Who dares to speak?!” The two guardians looked around, searching for the source of the voice.","The shopkeeper glanced at the small, inconspicuous snow-white pet beside him and silently took a step back.","“Open your dog eyes and look carefully.”","The voice of Cloud Devouring rang out again. It still appeared in its small and cute form, but it tilted its head back, stuck out its chest, and glared at the two men, exuding the aura of a powerful being that was completely at odds with its small stature and cute appearance.","When they saw that the voice came from the little pet in front of them, the two guardians’ expressions changed, and they involuntarily took a step back, staring at it warily. “What are you?!”","“Hmph! How rude.”","Cloud Devouring’s eyes turned cold, and a bloodthirsty killing intent flashed in them. A trace of pressure attacked the two, and at the same time, it leaped forward and attacked the two with its sharp claws.","Whoosh!","In that instant, the two felt a terrifying pressure coming toward them, their bodies stiffened, and in the next moment, a white shadow flashed before their eyes, and intense pain spread from their chests.","“Arghhhh!”","The two cried out in pain, retreating backward while looking down. They saw that their chests had been slashed by the claws’ energy blades, their robes torn open, and deep claw marks were visible on their chests.","The two were shocked, retreating further, too frightened to even think of counterattacking. After retreating several meters, they finally looked at the small white beast and met its bloodthirsty gaze. In an instant, they felt an overwhelming sense of danger spreading through their hearts. The fear deep within them turned their faces pale, and a chill ran up their spines, reaching their hearts, causing them to shiver violently. At the same time, they quickly reacted.","“Go! Quickly!”","The panicked voices carried undisguised fear, and they left as if fleeing, leaving the people around them stunned.","Cloud Devouring glanced at the fleeing people but did not pursue them. Instead, it turned around and walked inside with a wobbly gait, returning to the door of the room on the second floor to crouch down.","The innkeeper wiped the cold sweat from his brow and pressed his hand against his pounding heart, too frightened to recover for a long time. The large inn was so quiet at that moment that even the sound of a pin dropping could be heard. No one dared to make a sound until they saw the snow-white beast go to the second floor. Only then did they breathe a sigh of relief, but they still didn’t dare to discuss what had happened.","Song Mi’er in the kitchen was completely unaware of what was happening outside. At that moment, she was happily humming a tune as she cooked, the aroma of the food filling the air and bringing a satisfied smile to her face.","Meanwhile, in the teahouse diagonally opposite the inn, the middle-aged man sat with the young man and young woman. The young man and young woman looked stunned, while the middle-aged man was deep in thought.","“Are you talking about that snow-white little beast?” The middle-aged man looked at the two and asked.","The two swallowed hard and nodded. The girl said, “Yes, that’s the little pet.” As soon as she finished speaking, she couldn’t help but ask, “Second Uncle, why can that little pet talk? Why did the Wei family run away? That little pet...”","The middle-aged man interrupted her and said thoughtfully, “That’s definitely not an ordinary little pet. I’m afraid it’s a sacred beast!”"]},{"number":4855,"title":"Chapter 4855: Cannot believe","paragraphs":["Chapter 4855: Cannot believe","He looked at the inn diagonally opposite and said, “I wonder what kind of person owns a Sacred Beast?”","Back at the Wei family, the two guardians reported what had happened in the hall and finally said, “Patriarch, that was definitely a Sacred Beast. We really...”","“A Sacred Beast?” The Patriarch of the Wei family narrowed his eyes and said, “Didn’t you say it was just a little girl? How could she have a Sacred Beast following her? Are you sure you didn’t see it wrong?”","“There’s no mistake. The pressure at that moment was terrifying. We think that beast was at least at the level of a Sacred Beast.”","This was still a conservative guess. They even felt for a moment that it was more than just a Sacred Beast. However, even though they had their suspicions, they didn’t dare say anything. After all, Super Sacred Beasts were extremely rare. If they said anything, the Patriarch wouldn’t believe them and would think that they were just making excuses because they couldn’t defeat it.","Patriarch Wei stood up, walked a few steps in the hall with his hands behind his back, then glanced at the two of them and saw that their wounds had not been bandaged. He said, “You two go back and treat your wounds first. You don’t need to worry about this.”","“Yes.” The two replied, not knowing what else to say, and withdrew.","Patriarch Wei thought for a moment, then called his butler, gave him some instructions, and left. He was going to take a look himself to see if it was really a Sacred Beast.","Feng Jiu slept for a while and felt much better. She tidied herself up, put on her outer robe, and walked out. As soon as she opened the door, she saw Cloud Devouring crouching at the door.","“Where’s Mi?”","Feng Jiu asked as she came to the balcony and looked downstairs. She saw that there were many people sitting on the first floor, but they were all quiet and didn’t dare to speak loudly. As she walked out, those people looked up at her with a questioning look in their eyes.","“She’s cooking in the kitchen,” said Cloud Devouring.","“What’s going on? Why is the atmosphere so strange?” She had only taken a short nap, so why was the atmosphere in the inn so strange when she woke up?","Cloud Devouring glanced down and said, “Earlier, when the master was asleep, the Wei family came looking for trouble again. I dealt with them, and that’s how it is.”","Hearing this, Feng Jiu was taken aback, then smiled and said nothing. Instead, she walked over to a table by the window on the second floor. As soon as she sat down, the waiter hurried over to serve tea.","The kitchen door opened and a delicious smell wafted out, attracting the attention of everyone on the first floor. They saw Song Mi’er come out, untie the apron tied around her waist, and look up at the second floor. She was about to go upstairs to see if Feng Jiu was awake when she saw the innkeeper walking over.","“Miss, the lady has woken up. She’s sitting at the table by the window on the second floor.”","“She’s awake? Then please ask the waiter to bring the food upstairs,” said Song Mi’er with a smile.","“Yes, ma’am.” With that, he hurriedly called the waiter to bring the food.","Song Mi’er returned to the kitchen, carried the bowls upstairs herself, placed them on the table, and smiled, “Sister, you got up just in time. This soup has been simmering for a long time and the flavor is just right. Come and try some.”","Feng Jiu saw that she was busy in the kitchen, her pretty face flushed but looking full of energy, so she smiled and said, “You should sit down and rest for a while!” With that, she picked up the teapot and poured her a cup of tea.","“Thank you, sister,” Song Mi’er said with a smile. She scooped a bowl of soup for her, then picked up her cup of tea and drank it in one gulp. As soon as she put the cup down, she saw a bowl of soup that had just been scooped out in front of her."]},{"number":4856,"title":"Chapter 4856: Self-inflicted","paragraphs":["The shopkeeper and the waiter personally helped bring the dishes from the kitchen to the second floor before leaving.","Looking at the exquisite dishes in front of her, Feng Jiu smiled even more broadly. \"I haven't eaten yet, but just looking at this makes me hungry.\"","\"Sister, if you like it, eat more.\" She helped Feng Jiu pick some dishes, telling her what ingredients they were made with.","Feng Jiu listened while she ate, enjoying the delicious food and soup, occasionally accompanied by a few sips of wine. The taste was beyond words. After she was half full, she put down her chopsticks and said to Song Mi'er, \"Tomorrow, I'll take you to find that master craftsman. When we get there, you can tell him what kind of kitchen knife you want, and he'll make one for you.\"","\"Yeah!\" Song Mi'er was delighted and smiled happily.","She wasn't stupid. After following Feng Jiu around for these past few days, she naturally knew that Feng Jiu was very powerful. Although she hadn't seen her use her skills much, she had a gut feeling that the longer she spent with her, the stronger this feeling became.","Plus, she was beautiful, and looking at her stunningly beautiful face all day long made her feel great. That was one of the reasons why she had been willing to follow her for so many days without mentioning about the armement master. Because she believed that if Feng Jiu promised something, she would definitely do it, so all she had to do while following her was concentrate on cooking.","\"Sister, you've been gone for so many days. Have you finished everything?\" Song Mi'er asked.","\"Yes, everything is done,\" Feng Jiu replied, taking a sip of wine and tapping the table lightly with one hand, her gaze falling on the people walking toward them in the distance.","Behind her were several people with impressive cultivation, dressed in luxurious clothes, walking with steady steps and exuding an imposing aura. Their air of superiority made them stand out from the people around them. Song Mi'er followed her gaze and saw that among the people walking down the street, one was the person she had fought with earlier. She said in surprise, \"They're really back? Earlier, when I was cooking, I heard the innkeeper say that the Wei family had come looking for us again. I told them to come back later, but I didn't expect them to actually show up!\"","Cloud Devouring rolled his eyes. This was already the umpteenth group. Did she think they were the same people as before? Regardless, he didn't care. He squatted down like a human and picked up the bowl with his paws to drink the soup. It really was delicious, and it was full of spirit energy, making him feel comfortable all over.","The Wei family Patriarch arrived at the inn with his people. As soon as they entered, the innkeeper greeted them. \"Oh my, what wind has blown you here today? It's Patriarch Wei! Please come in.\"","\"It's fine.\" Patriarch Wei waved his hand, looked at the innkeeper, and asked, \"Where is the girl? I want to see her.\"","\"Hehe, Patriarch Wei, please take a seat. I'll go upstairs and let them know,\" the innkeeper said, but was pushed aside by one of Patriarch Wei's men.","\"No need, we can go up ourselves.\" The middle-aged man who pushed the innkeeper aside looked at the patriarch and gestured for them to go ahead.","Patriarch Wei didn't say anything, but with his hands behind his back, he walked straight to the second floor.","\"Hey, Patriarch Wei, this...\"","The shopkeeper called out from behind but didn't follow. As a shopkeeper who had seen countless people here every day, the girl who cooked probably didn't have much of a background, but the woman in red with the exquisite beauty was different..."]},{"number":4857,"title":"Chapter 4857: How are you going to resolve this matter?","paragraphs":["Chapter 4857: How are you going to resolve this matter?","Therefore, when he saw them rush up to the second floor, he lagged behind by a few steps before following closely behind.","Upon reaching the second floor, Patriarch Wei saw the two women sitting by the window, pointed out by his guards. When he saw the two, his gaze naturally fell on the woman in red. It was because she was so dazzling, like the bright sun, radiating a light that was difficult to ignore.","As the head of a family with the strength of a Divine King, he was considered one of the most powerful figures among the city’s noble families. What kind of beautiful women had he not seen? However, even at his age, when he saw the stunning woman in red, a look of amazement flashed across his eyes.","Beautiful!","Very beautiful!","So beautiful that one couldn’t take one’s eyes off her.","That kind of beauty wasn’t just the kind that captivated one’s heart and left one speechless, but a kind of beautiful aura that emanated from within, leaving a lasting impression on anyone who saw her.","However, he was still the head of a family and the leader of a clan, so after a moment of astonishment, he quickly regained his composure and took a closer look. He saw that this red-clad woman of extraordinary beauty and grace had a cultivation that he couldn’t detect, but her bone age was less than thirty. In the cultivation world, at such a young age, even if she had been born a divine embryo, her cultivation wouldn’t be that strong. After all, which of the powerful had not cultivated for hundreds, or even thousands of years, to attain such strength?","Out of contempt for the woman, even though he could not discern the extent of her cultivation, he was certain that her strength was inferior to his. Therefore, he shifted his gaze again and landed on the young girl sitting opposite the woman in red. When his gaze fell on her, he saw something hanging from her waist and knew where this young girl came from.","As for the beast that the two guardians had described as terrifying... He pondered, his gaze falling on the small, round, snow-white beast. It was tiny, like a little puppy, and was now humanly holding a bowl and drinking soup, not even looking in this direction. It was just a greedy little beast. Even looking at it from such a close distance, he didn’t sense any aura of a Sacred Beast emanating from it.","“Patriarch, it’s that young lady,” the guard whispered, pointing in the direction of Song Mi’er.","“Are you a member of the Song family?” He walked over, his majestic gaze falling on Song Mi’er with the pressure of a powerful man.","Song Mi’er glanced at him and said, “Yes! I’m from the Song family.” Her family was a renowned family of chefs, the only one of its kind in the entire Immortal Realm. Their fame was well known, and most of the other families and sects had heard of her family.","“Since you are from a renowned family, you should know that seriously injuring my family is a disgrace to the Wei family. I will ask you one question today. How do you intend to resolve this matter?” He spoke in a calm voice with his hands behind his back, his majestic gaze fixed on Song Mi’er.","Feng Jiu held a glass of wine in one hand and gently swayed it, her eyes downcast, as if she hadn’t heard Patriarch Wei’s words. She looked lazy and carefree as she played with the wine glass in her hand, occasionally taking a sip of the wine. After he finished speaking, Patriarch Wei saw the woman in red holding the wine and drinking it. His gaze couldn’t help but follow the wine glass as it approached her lips, and his eyes darkened slightly."]},{"number":4858,"title":"Chapter 4858: Crippled","paragraphs":["Chapter 4858: Crippled","However, in the next moment, a powerful pressure enveloped him, causing him to fall directly to his knees with a thud.","“Ughhhhh!”","As his knees hit the ground, the blood in his body surged, and a mouthful of blood gushed out of his throat, seeping from the corners of his mouth. Cold sweat the size of beans seeped from his forehead, and his face turned pale in an instant. His eyes were filled with fear and disbelief as he looked at the woman in red in front of him.","“Patriarch!”","“Patriarch!”","The few people following behind him cried out in shock, their faces turning pale from the sudden change. They tried to step forward but found that they couldn’t take a single step, as if a powerful force was blocking their path. In that instant, the few people looked at the woman in red with horror. Their bodies trembled uncontrollably, and they knelt down involuntarily.","The shopkeeper, who had followed them up the stairs, stood at the top without moving. Seeing the Wei family members kneeling on the ground, he looked at the red-clothed woman, who was still drinking wine as if nothing had happened, and his expression turned stunned. He glanced at her, then quietly stepped back. When he reached the ground floor, he ran outside, preparing to quickly report to his master.","A powerful beast, a stunningly beautiful woman in red, and unfathomable strength that could make Patriarch Wei kneel... It could only be the Phoenix Sovereign who had ascended some time ago!","Thinking of the news that had been secretly passed down by his master over the past two days, his heart pounded with nervousness and excitement. It had to be the Phoenix Sovereign! The news of the Great Emperor Northern Flame’s death had not yet spread, but the noble families and various factions had already learned that it was the newly ascended Phoenix Sovereign who had killed the Great Emperor Northern Flame and taken over their territory, becoming their new lord! Reporting this news to his master would be a great achievement!","On the second floor of the inn, by the window. Song Mi’er watched the scene in front of her, her eyes shining with admiration as she looked at Feng Jiu across from her. She knew her sister was no ordinary person! Even Patriarch Wei was kneeling before her. But who exactly was this sister she had only recently come to know? How could she scare the Wei family so much?","Feng Jiu took a sip of wine and gently turned the wine glass in her hand, not even glancing at Patriarch Wei kneeling on the ground, as if she didn’t see them. With her current status and identity, who would dare to look at her with such a bold and aggressive gaze? That would be pure suicide.","Patriarch Wei knelt on the ground, his body so weighed down by the pressure that he couldn’t stand up straight. He lowered his head, blood continuously seeping from his mouth, his face becoming increasingly pale. He tried to speak but couldn’t even manage to utter a word of surrender. Finally, unable to hold on any longer, he coughed up a mouthful of blood that splattered the ground. His entire body felt as though all his strength had been drained from him, and he fainted.","The other Wei family members kneeling behind him dared not utter a word, their heads pressed against the ground as their bodies trembled uncontrollably. At that moment, even if they were allowed to leave, their weak legs would not have been able to support them.","Feng Jiu put down the wine cup in her hand, waved her hand, and directly destroyed the cultivation of Patriarch Wei on the ground. Then, she slowly said to Cloud Devouring, “Throw them out of the inn. Don’t let them ruin our appetite.”"]},{"number":4859,"title":"Chapter 4859: Jiang Family","paragraphs":["Seeing their Patriarch's cultivation being destroyed and turning old in an instance, the Wei family members fainted from shock.","Cloud Devouring jumped down from its chair, opened its mouth, and threw them out of the window onto the street.","An elderly man who had rushed over upon hearing the innkeeper's report, accompanied by another elderly man and two middle-aged men, was about to enter the inn when they saw several objects flying down from the second floor. They hurriedly stepped back to avoid them, only to see that what had been thrown down were not objects, but people! Among them was the elderly man whose cultivation had been stripped away, leaving him old and dying.","Seeing this scene, the faces of the people traveling with him changed. The elderly man in the lead took a deep breath, looked up, and saw the red figure on the second floor. He hurriedly said to the people behind him, \"Follow me inside. Remember, do not offend them in any way, otherwise, even I cannot protect you.\"","\"Yes, we will obey the Old Predecessor's orders.\" The group hurriedly responded respectfully, suppressing their superior aura and following the old man in an orderly manner.","When they arrived on the second floor, a waiter was trembling as he cleaned the bloodstains on the floor. When the leader of the group saw the red figure sitting at the edge of the table, he hurriedly stepped forward and bowed, \"Greetings, Phoenix Sovereign.\"","\"It's you?\" Feng Jiu saw the old man and raised her eyebrows. \"What are you doing here?\" This old man, Immortal Elder Qinghua, was the immortal she had once bowed to, and now he was bowing to her.","Hearing Feng Jiu's words, the immortal hurriedly replied with a smile, \"It is I. The Jiang family of this city is the main branch of my family. I returned to give them some instructions, but I didn't expect to hear that the Phoenix Sovereign was here, so I brought my descendants to pay their respects.\" As he spoke, he turned slightly and shouted to the people behind him, \"Hurry up and pay your respects to the Phoenix Sovereign!\"","The old man and two middle-aged men behind him hurried forward and respectfully performed a kneeling bow to Feng Jiu.","\"I am Chang Chenghe of the Jiang family.\"","\"I am Jiang Xianren, Patriarch of the Jiang family.\"","\"I am Jiang Xianyi, a descendant of the Jiang family.\"","\"Greetings, Phoenix Sovereign.\"","After introducing themselves, the three bowed their heads in excitement and awe.","Feng Jiu glanced at them and said, \"Get up!\"","\"Thank you, Phoenix Sovereign.\"","They hurriedly responded, then stood up and respectfully retreated behind their Old Predecessor. They only glanced at her as they went up to the second floor, not daring to look at her again for fear of offending this incomparably noble and supreme sovereign.","\"Phoenix Sovereign, I'm afraid the inn won't be able to entertain you properly. Why don't you come to our mansion to rest?\" Immortal Elder Qinghua said, looking at Feng Jiu.","\"No need, I won't be staying here long.\" Feng Jiu waved her hand, indicating that it wasn't necessary.","Hearing this, he said again, \"Phoenix Sovereign, we are willing to serve you and help you with your troubles. Is there anything we can do for you?\"","Feng Jiu's lips curved slightly as she glanced at the people outside who might have heard the commotion and rushed over. She said, \"The Wei family is one of the noble families, but they are only famous in name. As the saying goes, 'if the upper beam is crooked, the lower beam will also be crooked.' Such a family is truly unworthy of being a noble family in this city.\"","Hearing this, Immortal Elder Qinghua's heart stirred, and he immediately said, \"Phoenix Sovereign, rest assured, leave this matter to me. I will definitely give you a satisfactory result.\"","\"Hmm, you may withdraw. Don't let them come up. Don't disturb my peace,\" Feng Jiu said as she picked up her wine cup and took a sip.","\"Yes, we will take our leave.\" The few people responded immediately, bowed, and then withdrew."]},{"number":4860,"title":"Chapter 4860 - 100 Years","paragraphs":["Chapter 4860: 100 Years","After they left, the second floor was quiet again, leaving only Feng Jiu, Song Mi’er, and the little beast, Cloud Devouring. Seeing Song Mi’er staring at her with wide, surprised eyes, Feng Jiu couldn’t help but smile softly. “What’s wrong? Are you surprised?”","“Phoenix Sovereign?” Song Mi’er murmured.","“Yes, that’s what they call me.” Feng Jiu nodded, a smile spreading across her lips.","“Oh my goodness! I’ve been calling you ‘sister’ this whole time! We’ve been together the whole way! This isn’t a dream, is it?” Song Mi’er covered her mouth with both hands and whispered, still finding it hard to believe. She had guessed that her status must be quite high—perhaps she was from a hidden family or being groomed as a family’s next heir—but she never expected that she wasn’t from a distinguished family but was the mysterious female sovereign, the Phoenix Sovereign, who had recently ascended!","Seeing her shocked and surprised expression, Feng Jiu smiled lightly, propped her chin with one hand, and sighed as if she were joking. “What’s so surprising? Even though my identity is a little extraordinary, I can’t even find a good cook to go back with.”","Hearing this, Song Mi’er was stunned for a moment. Then, she patted her chest and looked at Feng Jiu with a flattering expression. “Sister, I’ll go back with you! I’ll cook delicious food for you! From now on, I’ll follow you wherever you go, and I’ll take care of all your meals!”","She would be stupid to refuse such a good offer. She didn’t know Feng Jiu’s identity before, but now that she did, she was naturally overjoyed. She also knew that powerful beings like the Phoenix Sovereign had a floating fairy island, which was truly filled with spiritual energy and extremely conducive to cultivating immortality. If she followed her, there would only be benefits and no disadvantages. What’s more, she loved to cook, and Feng Jiu loved to eat.","Feng Jiu raised an eyebrow and glanced at her. “Have you decided?”","“Yes! I’ve decided, and I won’t change my mind!” Song Mi’er said hurriedly. Then she looked at Feng Jiu again, hesitated, and asked, “Then should I call you Phoenix Sovereign in the future, or can I still call you sister?”","Hearing this, Feng Jiu smiled and said, “You’ve been calling me that the whole way here, and now you’re asking me? Don’t you think it’s a little late?”","Song Mi’er smiled happily. “Sister, you’re so nice!” If Feng Jiu hadn’t agreed, she wouldn’t have let her call her that this whole time. Song Mi’er considered herself really lucky. She came out to travel and found a powerful person to latch onto. If her father and brothers found out, they would probably be stunned.","The two chatted idly upstairs. Meanwhile, downstairs, Immortal Elder Qinghua stopped the people from the city’s prominent families who had rushed over to the inn. When he saw that the Wei family had also arrived, he stepped forward to block them, then led them aside to talk.","Because of what happened today and the news of the Phoenix Sovereign’s presence, the news of the Great Emperor Northern Flame’s death was also made public. The news spread like feathers scattered by the wind, and the news that the Phoenix Sovereign had taken over the Great Emperor Northern Flame’s territory and become their new ruler also spread quickly.","There was also another piece of news: before nightfall, the Wei family, which had several hundred years of family history, was stripped of its noble status. Overnight, the Wei clan fled into hiding and would not show their faces for a hundred years.","The next day, after Feng Jiu and Song Mi’er had eaten, the two of them and the beast quietly left the city and headed for the place where Grandmaster Iron was."]},{"number":4861,"title":"Chapter 4861: Dissonance","paragraphs":["Chapter 4861: Dissonance","In a remote, uninhabited spot halfway up a mountainside, a large area had been cleared in front of a simple thatched hut and planted with vegetables. At this moment, a man in his forties, dressed in gray and with a sturdy build, was turning the soil with a hoe. Sweat dripped from his sunburnt forehead, ran down his cheeks, and fell onto the soil.","The man worked hard in the field, each swing of the hoe sending sweat flying, and the sound of the hoe digging into the soil became the only sound in this quiet place.","From the thatched cottage, an elderly woman with white hair emerged. She held a bamboo basket in one hand and a water jug in the other. Her hair was snow-white, her face was wrinkled, her back was slightly bent, and her frame was frail. She moved slowly with each step.","When the man with the hoe saw the old woman walking toward him with something in her hands, he quickly put down his hoe and walked swiftly toward her. He took the items from her hands and put them aside, then took her hand and said reproachfully, “Didn’t you say you didn’t need to bring me water and food? It’s so close; if I’m hungry or thirsty, I’ll go home to drink.”","As he spoke, he took the cloth covering the basket and placed it on the ground as a mat. “Come, sit down.”","The old woman smiled and said in a warm voice, “I can carry this little bit; it’s not heavy.” As she spoke, she poured him a cup of water and pulled him down to sit beside her. “Have some water! Look how much you’re sweating.” She took out a handkerchief and wiped the sweat from his face.","The man sat beside her, looking at her with gentle eyes, letting her wipe the sweat from his face. He held her hand and said, “It’s okay, you don’t need to wipe it anymore. Just sit for a while, and the sweat will dry.” With that, he drank the water in the cup in one gulp, poured another cup, and handed it to her. “You drink some too! It’s hot today; drink more water.”","The old woman smiled, took the teacup from his hand, held it with both hands, and because of her old age, her hands trembled slightly, causing the water in the cup to sway gently. Seeing this, the man’s heart ached, and a hint of pain flashed across his eyes.","However, the pain in his eyes was fleeting. When he saw her drink the water and look at him, a smile appeared on his face again, and he picked up a steamed bun from the basket and ate it.","The old woman sat next to him, holding his hand. She looked at the vegetable patch in front of her and said gently in a hoarse voice, “These vegetables are growing so well. In a few days, they will be ready to harvest. When that time comes, I will dry them and make them into dried vegetables for you to eat.”","“Dry them and make them into dried vegetables so we can eat them later,” the man eating the steamed buns deliberately emphasized this point, looking at her.","Hearing this, the old woman smiled helplessly. “Alright, after they are dried, we will eat them together.”","Hearing this, the man smiled and pointed to the half-plowed empty lot in front of him. “By this evening, I’ll have finished plowing this new piece of land. Then I’ll move two fruit trees over from the left and right sides and plant them. Next year, we’ll be able to eat fruit that we grew ourselves. What do you think we should plant in the middle?”","The two sat in front of the vegetable patch, chatting. It was quiet all around, except for the sound of the wind and their low voices.","Not far away, halfway up the mountain, Feng Jiu and Song Mi’er were watching the scene from behind a large rock, feeling that something was amiss."]},{"number":4862,"title":"Chapter 4862: You’ve Come to the Wrong Place","paragraphs":["Chapter 4862: You’ve Come to the Wrong Place","The man was in his prime, muscular and well-built, with a handsome face. He wasn’t particularly good-looking, but he was definitely a tough guy.","The old woman had white hair and a wrinkled face. She was old and didn’t look like she had much time left to live. However, the two got along like husband and wife, and their behavior was full of affection and tenderness.","From a distance, Song Mi’er couldn’t hear what they were saying very clearly, but Feng Jiu could. It was the quiet coexistence of ordinary people, ordinary yet filled with warmth and deep affection, with expectations for life and the future.","Feng Jiu’s gaze couldn’t help but linger on the two people embraced by the man, with the woman’s head resting lightly against his chest. With her cultivation, Feng Jiu could see that the man was not young, but because of his strength and cultivation, he was able to maintain the appearance of a middle-aged man. The old woman spoke with a weak voice, probably because she had fatal internal injuries and was in her final moments. From her breathing, Feng Jiu could tell that she had at most three to five months to live.","However, even though the old woman’s beauty had faded, the man’s face was full of tenderness and affection. Feng Jiu couldn’t help but be moved. This was definitely true love.","“Sister, isn’t that old woman the middle-aged man’s mother? Why is she hugging him?” Song Mi’er looked puzzled and asked in a low voice.","“It looks like they’re husband and wife,” Feng Jiu said with a hint of tenderness in her eyes.","Hearing this, Song Mi’er was stunned for a moment. She looked at the two people leaning on each other but didn’t ask any more questions. Instead, she looked around and said, “Sister, we’ve searched all over this mountain, and there’s only this thatched cottage and this couple. We haven’t seen Grandmaster Iron’s mansion. So, have we come to the wrong place?”","“Let’s go ask and find out,” Feng Jiu said, stepping forward.","Earlier, Feng Jiu had concealed the two’s aura, so the middle-aged man hadn’t noticed anyone around. Now, as Feng Jiu and the others approached, the middle-aged man hugging the old woman frowned and turned to look at them.","“Excuse me, gentlemen,” Feng Jiu said with an apologetic smile.","“Who are you? What are you doing here?” the man asked, standing up and staring at the two of them.","Song Mi’er smiled sweetly and said, “Uncle, we wanted to ask if the Great Armament Master, Grandmaster Iron, is here on this mountain? We’ve looked everywhere but couldn’t find anyone.”","“There’re no Armament Masters here. You’ve come to the wrong place,” the man said as he put away the teapot and cups and prepared to take the old woman back.","Feng Jiu’s gaze fell on the hoe nearby, and her eyes flashed. The old woman gave the two a gentle, apologetic smile but didn’t say anything and let the man lead her back.","“Sister, he said there are no Armament Masters here! Did we really come to the wrong place?” Song Mi’er’s gaze fell on the two who were leaving. She looked at the simple thatched cottage not far away, frowned, and thought deeply.","Feng Jiu smiled slightly and said, “No, we’re not in the wrong place. This is the right place.” With that, she walked slowly behind the two, watching the vegetables growing in the field.","Song Mi’er didn’t understand, but she didn’t ask. Instead, she followed Feng Jiu and came to her side."]},{"number":4863,"title":"Chapter 4863: An Affectionate Person","paragraphs":["Chapter 4863: An Affectionate Person","After the two entered the thatched cottage, the door closed behind them, and the man didn’t even acknowledge Feng Jiu. Feng Jiu didn’t mind. She sat down at the table outside, propped her chin on her hand, looked around, and said, “It’s a bit simple, but the air is nice and it’s very quiet.”","Song Mi’er looked around and said, “This place is too quiet. Only the two of them live here, and it’s halfway up the mountain. There are a lot of trees around, so there might be wild animals at night. It’s also too far from town, so it’s not convenient to go to the market.”","Hearing this, Feng Jiu smiled lightly and said, “Everyone has a different ideal life. Although this place is a bit simple, they have each other to rely on and love. How do you know they aren’t happy?”","Song Mi’er thought for a moment and said, “Sister, that big man must love his wife very much, because my mother said that men in this world value appearance and all like young, beautiful women with good figures. There are very few men who value inner beauty over appearance.”","Feng Jiu smiled, just looking around, tapping the table lightly with one hand, and said, “I haven’t been here long, and all I know about this Grandmaster Iron is that he’s very good at smithing. I didn’t expect him to be such a romantic.”","“Eh?” Song Mi’er looked at her in surprise, then looked at the closed door, pointed at the room, and asked, “Sister, are you saying that the person we’re looking for is that uncle?”","“Who else but him would refine a hoe into a weapon?” Feng Jiu said absentmindedly, her gaze falling on the vegetable patch not far away.","Upon hearing her words, Song Mi’er immediately walked over to where the hoe was and took a closer look. She couldn’t help but exclaim, “It’s really true! Such a magical artifact was just left here? And a hoe can be forged into something like this? That’s amazing!”","The two did not lower their voices, and even with the distance between the thatched cottage and the outside, the two people inside the house could hear the voices outside. The man frowned, and the old woman patted his hand.","“That lady in red is amazing. She recognized you at first glance and guessed your identity.” The old woman said in a gentle voice, with a hint of surprise and admiration. Over the years, they had lived in seclusion here, but it wasn’t that no one had come looking for them. It was just that there was only one young lady in red who could recognize their identities at a glance.","“You rest here, I’ll go chase them away.” The man said as he stood up and walked outside. The old woman hurriedly said, “Don’t scare the young lady, just let them leave.”","“I know,” the man replied, then opened the door and walked out. He saw the woman in red sitting leisurely at the table, resting, with one hand supporting her chin and her eyes looking ahead.","“We don’t welcome strangers here. You two should leave quickly!” The man came to Feng Jiu and said in a deep voice.","“Uncle, we came to ask you to help me forge a kitchen knife,” Song Mi’er ran over and looked at him excitedly. “Iron Uncle, you say, as long as you are willing to help me forge a kitchen knife, you can ask for whatever reward you want, and I will definitely find a way to get it for you.”","Seeing that even a hoe could be forged into such a sharp weapon, Song Mi’er was even more excited. If he forged a kitchen knife, maybe it would be able to cut through the bones of those fierce beasts with a single blow.","“I don’t know how to forge weapons. Please leave!” He frowned and said in a deep voice."]},{"number":4864,"title":"Chapter 4864: Treatment","paragraphs":["\"Cough, cough... cough...\"","Inside the room, a few low, suppressed coughs were heard. As soon as he heard the coughing, the man, no longer concerned with chasing away the two outside, rushed back into the room nervously.","\"What's wrong? Why are you coughing again? Quickly, drink some water.\" The man hurriedly poured a cup of water and carefully handed it to her.","However, the old woman took only one sip before coughing again. She felt a rush of blood rise in her throat, and the water she hadn't yet swallowed spurted out along with the blood.","\"Pfft!\"","\"Yueniang!\" The man cried out in alarm, his face turning pale.","Outside, Feng Jiu heard his cry and immediately got up and rushed inside. When she arrived, she saw the old woman spitting blood from her mouth, her face pale as she fainted.","\"Quickly carry her to the bed!\" Feng Jiu said.","The man, in a panic, listened to Feng Jiu. He hurriedly picked up the unconscious woman and carried her to the bed inside, shouting, \"Yueniang, Yueniang, wake up, don't scare me, don't scare me...\" The man, who was usually so strong and tough, had tears welling up in his eyes, and his voice was choked with emotion.","After putting her on the bed, he still held her hand and shouted, \"Yueniang, Yueniang, wake up!\"","\"Move aside, let me take a look at her,\" Feng Jiu said. But as she was about to step forward, the red-eyed man pushed her away.","\"Get away! Get away! Don't touch my Yueniang! Get away!\" The man shouted angrily, furious at this woman of unknown origin for trying to approach the person most important to him.","Seeing that this man was deeply in love, Feng Jiu did not argue with him. However, looking at the old woman on the bed who was breathing very weakly, she couldn't bear to see a pair of lovers separated forever.","\"I am skilled in medicine. She has an old illness that she has been suffering from for many years. It is not easy for her to have held on until now. Now she is vomiting blood, which has worsened her condition. If you don't let me treat her, she won't live past today,\" Feng Jiu said lightly. She didn't step forward, but stood three steps away from the bed, watching the man who was going crazy.","Upon hearing this, the man's eyes were filled with struggle. He didn't know who these two people were, but he knew the condition of the woman he loved. How could he let a stranger treat his beloved? He... His heart was struggling. In the end, he was frightened by the words, \"If you don't let her treat her, she won't live past today.\"","He stood up and silently backed away, but his eyes were fixed on the red-clothed woman, afraid that she would do something bad to her.","Seeing him staring at Feng Jiu like a mad wolf, Song Mi'er said, \"Uncle Iron, don't worry, we're not bad people. We won't do anything to hurt you.\"","However, the man didn't say anything, as if he hadn't heard her. He just stared at Feng Jiu and watched her take the old woman's pulse. When she took out the silver needles to treat her, he saw how skilled she was and pursed his lips, forcing himself to resist the urge to rush forward and grab the needles.","Feng Jiu ignored him and concentrated on giving the old woman on the bed emergency first aid. As time passed, the old woman, who had fainted, gradually regained consciousness. At this moment, Feng Jiu was removing the silver needles from the acupoints on her body.","\"Yueniang!\" The man called out in surprise and hurried forward."]},{"number":4865,"title":"Chapter 4865: Conditions","paragraphs":["Chapter 4865: Conditions","“Yueniang, how are you? Do you feel any pain?” He held her hand and asked nervously.","The old woman on the bed shook her head gently and tried to sit up.","At that moment, Feng Jiu said, “You’d better lie down! The spiritual energy in your body is almost depleted. It’s best to stay in bed for the time being to avoid a recurrence of what just happened.”","“If it weren’t for my sister helping you with the needles, you probably wouldn’t have woken up. So you’d better listen to what she says,” said Song Mi’er, who was standing nearby.","“Thank you, miss.” The old woman thanked her weakly. She didn’t try to sit up again but lay on the bed, looking at the man holding her hand, her expression carrying a hint of sadness and a reluctance that she couldn’t hide.","“Thank you. I apologize for my earlier behavior. Please don’t hold it against me.” The man stood up and bowed to Feng Jiu, speaking apologetically.","“It’s fine,” Feng Jiu said indifferently, glancing at the man and looking at the old woman on the bed. “I just took her pulse and found that she not only has an old illness but also that her Neidan1 has cracked, causing her spiritual energy to leak out and making it impossible for her to cultivate and recover on her own!”","Seeing how skilled she was when she treated the old woman earlier, and that Yueniang woke up not long after the silver needles were inserted, the man knew that she was well-versed in medical techniques. So he didn’t hide anything from her and nodded in agreement. “Yes.”","“Since the Neidan is damaged, causing spiritual energy to leak out, why not repair it?” Feng Jiu asked with a hint of doubt.","However, although she asked naturally, the people listening to her were all stunned, their faces filled with shock and disbelief.","“Miss, you said that a cracked Neidan can be repaired? Did I hear you correctly?” the man asked in a trembling voice, his expression tinged with excitement and caution. Who among those who cultivate immortality doesn’t know that once the Neidan is damaged and the spiritual energy leaks out, it’s only a matter of time before death? Who has the ability to repair a damaged Neidan? I’ve never heard of such a thing!","Seeing this, Feng Jiu raised her eyebrows and looked at Song Mi’er. “Are there no alchemists or doctors here who can repair a damaged Neidan?”","Song Mi’er shook her head. “Sister, once the Neidan is damaged, the spiritual energy will leak out. No one can repair it. All we can do is wait to die.” As she spoke, her eyes darted around and fell on her surprised face. She asked curiously, “Sister, can you repair a damaged Neidan?”","At that moment, the man knelt down with a thud and begged, “Miss, please save my Yueniang! As long as you are willing to help me save Yueniang, I will do anything you ask!”","Hearing this, Feng Jiu smiled, glanced at the old woman on the bed, and said to the man, “If I ask you and your wife to come with me, would you agree?”","Hearing this, the man paused for a moment and did not answer immediately. This was because he did not know who this young lady in red was. What would she want them to do if they went with her?","Feng Jiu was not in a hurry. She walked over to the table and sat down, saying slowly, “Don’t worry, I won’t ask you to do anything harmful or unjust. I just admire your craftsmanship and want you to work for me.”","As she spoke, she paused and said, “If you don’t agree, it’s alright. I can extend her life for another three years, but you must forge a knife in exchange.”","Song Mi’er listened to this and couldn’t help but look at him anxiously. She wanted to remind him but didn’t dare, so she could only stand by and worry."]},{"number":4866,"title":"Chapter 4866: Agrees","paragraphs":["Chapter 4866: Agrees","After a while, his eyes filled with determination and resolve. He looked up at Feng Jiu and said in a calm voice, “As long as you can save Yueniang’s life, my life is yours!”","Hearing this, Feng Jiu smiled and gave him a meaningful look, saying, “You won’t regret your decision today.”","Yueniang looked at the man on the bed and silently shed tears. It was all because of her. If it weren’t for her, he wouldn’t have to do this. They didn’t know who this young lady in red was or what her background was. What if in the future...","“It will be impossible for her to recover in a short period of time. I will stay and help treat her for the time being. As for you, Mi’er needs a knife. You can discuss with her what kind of knife she needs,” Feng Jiu said to the man, but her eyes were on Song Mi’er, who was standing nearby.","“But Yueniang...” The man was also a little worried.","“I’m here with her, and you can’t help here. I don’t like having people around when I’m treating her,” Feng Jiu said slowly.","Hearing this, the man thought for a moment before replying, “Alright, I understand.”","So, the man and Song Mi’er went outside. Song Mi’er told him what kind of knife she wanted, what it would be used for, and how big it should be.","In the room, after the two left, Yueniang looked at Feng Jiu and asked in a weak voice, “Miss, why do you want us to follow you? Aren’t you worried?”","Hearing this, Feng Jiu smiled, stood up, walked to the bedside, and said, “What is there to worry about? Are you worried that you will change your mind after I cure you? Or are you worried about your character?”","She didn’t give her a chance to speak but sat down on the bedside and smiled. “I believe I have a good eye for people. Besides, I have just acquired a new place. It is large, but I have few servants. It wouldn’t hurt to take a few more who I like.”","Not expecting to hear such words, Yueniang stared at her blankly, not knowing what to say for a moment.","“Open your mouth.” Feng Jiu took out a medicinal pill.","Yueniang instinctively opened her mouth and felt something drop into it. It slid down her throat, and a faint medicinal smell spread in her mouth, accompanied by a rich and pure spiritual energy that made her pause for a moment.","Immediately afterwards, she felt a warm stream of spiritual energy begin to flow through her body. She felt a wave of comfort wash over her, and before she knew it, she had fallen asleep.","At this moment, Feng Jiu placed one hand on her chest and sent a thread of Blue Lotus energy into her body, slowly repairing her shattered Neidan. However, since her Neidan had been broken for a year or two, Feng Jiu was afraid that her body would not be able to withstand repairing it all at once, so she could only do it little by little.","Outside, the man took out a refining furnace and some tools about a hundred meters away from the house. He selected one, took out a piece of black iron, and began to put it in the furnace to burn.","When Feng Jiu came out of the house and saw that the man a hundred meters away had already started refining the weapon, she smiled with satisfaction. She took a soft couch out of her space and placed it in a cool spot in front of the house. She took out some spiritual wine and drank it while half-closing her eyes, enjoying the quiet and seclusion of the mountainside.","Song Mi’er was already preparing to cook. Seeing Feng Jiu drinking there, she asked, “Sister, do you need to boil any medicine or anything?”"]},{"number":4867,"title":"Chapter 4867: Astonished","paragraphs":["Feng Jiu tilted her head back slightly and poured some wine into her mouth. After a mouthful of the spirit wine, she smiled lightly and said, \"No need.\" When she healed people, apart from the power of the Blue Lotus, she also had various medicinal pills in her space, so she naturally didn't need to boil any medicine to drink.","\"Sister, how do you even know medicine? I've never heard of anyone who can repair a Neidan.\" Song Mi'er looked at her admiringly and asked with a smile, \"Sister, is there anything you don't know?\"","Feng Jiu smiled, drank her wine leisurely, and said, \"That's hard to say because I'm proficient in many things.\" She even knew how to refine weapons, but she was just too lazy to do it.","The two chatted outside for a while, then Song Mi'er went to prepare dinner, leaving Feng Jiu to rest.","Life in the mountains was quiet and boring, with no other entertainment. So after three days, Feng Jiu spent most of her time lying on the soft couch and kneading Cloud Devouring, which she had brought out of her space.","The man didn't want the noise of forging iron to disturb her rest, so he worked a hundred meters away, separated by some trees. The sound was much quieter, but with Feng Jiu's cultivation, the sound of hammering could still be heard clearly in her ears. The sound had been almost non-stop for the past three days, as the man was hammering day and night.","Song Mi'er came out of the room, smiling as she carried an empty bowl to Feng Jiu's side. \"Sister, Yueniang has finished her porridge and said she feels much better. Can she get out of bed and walk around?\"","\"Let her continue to lie down and rest. When she can get out of bed and walk around, I'll let her,\" Feng Jiu said without opening her eyes. Her hand, resting on her abdomen, tapped gently in rhythm with the distant hammering sounds.","\"Alright, I'll go tell her,\" Song Mi'er said and ran back inside, returning a short while later.","Two days later, Feng Jiu said to Yueniang on the bed, \"Get up and walk around today! Wash up and tidy yourself up.\"","Hearing this, Yueniang, who had been lying in bed for five days, was overjoyed, and a gentle smile appeared on her face. She said, \"Miss, I feel that the spiritual energy in my body has gradually gathered over the past two days. Am I getting better?\"","It was impossible not to be shocked. In just five days, she had gradually transformed from a frail old woman in her seventies to a woman in her forties. Although her white hair had not yet turned black, half of it was now black. Not only that, but her body had also returned to its state in her forties. If she hadn't seen it with her own eyes, she would never have believed that she could have such a day.","Feng Jiu walked slowly toward the door and said, \"It will probably take about a month to fully recover, but your neidan has gradually been repaired, and your internal injuries are 70–80% healed. It's only a matter of time before you return to your peak condition. All right, go wash up!\"","Watching her leave, Yueniang couldn't wait to get out of bed. She came to the bath that Song Mi'er had prepared for her and looked at her reflection in the water. She couldn't help but shed tears of joy. \"I never thought I could recover. I never thought I could return to my younger self...\" She stroked her face, tears of joy rolling down her cheeks."]},{"number":4868,"title":"Chapter 4868: Surprised","paragraphs":["Chapter 4868: Surprised","Outside, a hundred metres away, the iron hammer continued to strike the red-hot iron block with a steady rhythm. What had once been an unremarkable piece of black iron now began to take shape.","Sweat poured down the man’s body, drying and then reappearing in a relentless cycle. He concentrated on hammering the iron and refining the tool, strike after strike, seriously and intently. With each blow of the hammer, a spark flew from the red-hot iron.","Looking at the iron that was beginning to take shape, he clamped it and dipped it into the water. The red-hot iron touched the water and immediately emitted a hissing sound, and the water began to bubble.","He stopped to rest for a moment, wiped the sweat from his face, looked toward the house, and thought for a moment. It had been five days, and he was still a little worried, so he walked back to see how Yueniang was doing.","When he reached the house, he saw the red-clad young lady resting on a soft couch in front of the house, with a snow-white pet curled up in her arms. Song Mi’er was picking vegetables in the vegetable patch.","“Uncle Iron? Do you want to see Yueniang? She should be bathing right now,” Song Mi’er raised her head from the vegetable patch and said with a smile. Seeing him covered in sweat, she put down what she was doing and quickly walked back to the table in front of the house and poured him a cup of water. “Uncle Iron, you’ve been working hard these past few days. Have some water to quench your thirst.”","Hearing Song Mi’er say that Yueniang was bathing, he paused for a moment but did not go in. Instead, he took the water she poured for him and said, “Thank you.”","After drinking the water, he paused for a moment and asked with some concern, “How has Yueniang been these past few days? Is she feeling better?”","Song Mi’er nodded with a smile. “Don’t worry, she’s been fine these past few days! She’s been lying in bed all this time, and today she was allowed to get out of bed and walk around, so you’ll see her after she takes a bath!”","Hearing her words, he felt relieved. He put the cup on the table and waited at the door, listening to the faint sounds of someone getting dressed. He couldn’t help but feel a little nervous. With her condition, wouldn’t it be too difficult for her to bathe and get dressed? What if she slipped and fell on the wet floor? Her body couldn’t withstand a fall like that. The more he thought about it, the more worried he became, so he called out anxiously from outside, “Yueniang? Are you taking a bath? Be careful of the slippery floor, don’t slip and fall. Just get dressed; I’ll help you dry your hair in a minute, you...”","Feng Jiu listened to his words and couldn’t help but smile, shaking her head secretly.","Before he could finish his sentence, the tightly closed door opened, and Yueniang stood in the doorway. She was dressed in plain clothes, her face slightly red and looking a little embarrassed as she glanced at the man standing in front of the door staring at her. “The ladies are all here! What are you talking about?” Although the two had always been very loving, she felt a little embarrassed when he said those words in front of the two young girls. After all, they were both quite old.","“Yueniang? You, you...how did you become so young?” He stared at her blankly, seemingly unable to recover from his shock.","“The young lady helped me repair my neidan and treat my internal injuries, and my body has gradually recovered. The young lady said that in a month at most, my strength will return to its peak, and my appearance will also return to its prime.” As she said this, her heart was filled with joy. After all, there was no woman who did not want to be forever young and beautiful."]},{"number":4869,"title":"Chapter 4869: The Forged Knife","paragraphs":["Chapter 4869: The Forged Knife","Hearing this, he excitedly stepped forward, grabbed her arms with both hands, and wanted to say something, but didn’t know what to say. In the end, he just kept repeating, “That’s great, that’s great!”","After a while, he came to his senses and quickly turned to Feng Jiu and knelt down. “Thank you, Miss, thank you!”","“Alright, it’s no big deal. She hasn’t fully recovered yet,” Feng Jiu said gently.","If he had been a little skeptical before, at this moment, seeing Yueniang’s recovery, he felt nothing but excitement, endless joy, and anticipation. At this moment, it was like a new life for them! In order to cure Yueniang, he had sought out many famous doctors and alchemists, but no one had the ability to repair a neidan. He never expected that he would find their chance for survival here.","“I’m going to continue forging the knife. I’ll go now,” he grinned, a big smile on his face. He patted Yueniang’s hand and, without waiting for Feng Jiu to say anything, turned and continued forging the knife. At this moment, his blood was rushing through his veins. He was excited and thrilled, as if he had all this energy with nowhere to go. He thought about it and decided that only forging could calm him down.","Feng Jiu narrowed her eyes and listened to the sound of hammering, thinking to herself. Once she had dealt with her enemies in the Upper Immortal Realm, she would find a way to break through the barrier between the realms and bring her family here to live with her.","Thinking about it, the corners of her lips couldn’t help but turn up slightly, and her mood also soared. By then, they could live whatever life they wanted, and she would have her three children. Come to think of it, she had been here for quite some time, but she hadn’t been able to see them. She wondered how they were doing with the Azure Emperor. Had they lost weight? Or had they gained weight? Or had they grown taller?","Accompanied by these random thoughts, she gradually fell asleep in the gentle breeze.","Seeing that she was asleep, Song Mi’er took a blanket from her space and covered her with it. Only then did she and Yueniang go to the vegetable garden.","A few days later, early in the morning, Song Mi’er was boiling porridge for breakfast when the man who had been making knives came over with a smile on his face.","“Mi’er, try this knife and see how it is.” He handed her a sharp kitchen knife and said, “I made this according to your instructions. Since you are a woman, I made this kitchen knife light and thin. I made a few changes according to your suggestions. Come, try it out.”","When Song Mi’er saw that the knife was thinner than an ordinary kitchen knife and had a sharp, cold gleam, her eyes lit up, and she quickly took it to have a look.","“Uncle Iron, it looks thin and smaller than an ordinary kitchen knife. Can it cut cow bones?” she asked curiously, fondly touching the blade.","“Hahaha, of course, it can. Moreover, it is made of black iron, and I have forged a defensive array on it. If necessary, it can also be used as a weapon to defend yourself. Just make do with it for now, and I’ll forge a better one for you in the future,” he laughed loudly.","“Yay, thank you, Uncle Iron!” Song Mi’er said happily, thanking him and rushing to the kitchen to try out the knife.","“Let me boil some water for you to bathe! Look at you, you’re covered in sweat after all these days. Take a bath and get some rest,” Yueniang walked over and handed him the tea she was holding."]},{"number":4870,"title":"Chapter 4870: Knows","paragraphs":["Chapter 4870: Knows","“No need to bother boiling water. I’ll just go take a cold bath in the stream,” he said with a grin.","Knowing that he usually took cold baths, she didn’t say anything, but smiled gently and said, “Then I’ll prepare some food for you. It’ll be ready when you come back.”","“Thank you.” He nodded and turned to leave.","As Yueniang’s health was gradually improving and the knife Song Mi’er wanted had been forged, Feng Jiu took them all down the mountain after lunch that day.","“Sister, where are we going now?” Song Mi’er asked, looking at Feng Jiu beside her.","Feng Jiu walked slowly and said, “Let’s go back first! We’ve been out for a while; we should go back and check if everything is fine.”","The two people following behind heard this and couldn’t help but glance at each other. At this point, they still didn’t know who she was or where she was taking them. However, since they had already agreed, they naturally wouldn’t go back on their word, so they didn’t ask any more questions.","It wasn’t until Feng Jiu took them to the floating fairy island in her airship that Yueniang couldn’t help but ask, “Miss, we still don’t know your name. I don’t know...”","“My name is Feng Jiu.” Sitting at the bow of the ship and drinking spirit wine, she smiled.","However, they were better off not asking. Upon hearing her name, they were stunned. “Surnamed Feng? I’ve never heard of a family with the surname Feng. Where is your family from?”","Song Mi’er, who was eating fruit nearby, heard this and said with a smile, “There wasn’t one before, but there is now! The Phoenix Sovereign who ascended not long ago is my sister!”","“What?”","Hearing this, the two couldn’t help but cry out in surprise. They had always lived in the mountains and didn’t know much about the outside world, so they naturally didn’t know about the Phoenix Sovereign who had just ascended. So, Song Mi’er told them everything that had happened recently, and the two listened with surprise and excitement in their eyes.","They never expected that the person they had stumbled upon was actually a great emperor! And she was the only female emperor among all the great emperors!","“Miss, we really didn’t know who you were. Please don’t take it to heart.” The two of them hurriedly knelt down and bowed.","“There’s no need to be so formal when you’re with me. Get up!” Feng Jiu said, took a sip of wine, looked at them, and said, “From now on, you can stay at my immortal palace on the Spirit Island! There aren’t many people there now, but it will be very lively in the future.”","“Yes, thank you, Miss!” The two replied, glancing at each other and smiling. They never imagined that they would find themselves in such a situation, so they would naturally cherish this opportunity.","The airship was flying when suddenly Feng Jiu raised her eyebrows and looked outside. The man also seemed to sense something and quickly looked behind the airship. He saw a group of about thirty or forty people chasing them, some riding flying birds and some riding flying swords, coming towards them fiercely.","“Miss, there’s a group of about thirty or forty people chasing us. They’re gradually forming an encirclement,” he said, turning back to Feng Jiu.","Feng Jiu curled her lips and smiled. “Let’s see what they want!” As soon as she finished speaking, the airship, which had been flying steadily, gradually descended, as if preparing to land."]},{"number":4871,"title":"Chapter 4871: Bone-Devouring Asura","paragraphs":["Chapter 4871: Bone-Devouring Asura","As the airship landed, it came to a stop beside a stream. Several people stepped out of the airship. Feng Jiu swept her sleeves, and the airship vanished. At the same time, the pursuers arrived and surrounded them.","“Big Brother, there are only a few of them. It looks like we’ve struck gold today!” A cultivator said, glancing at the group before fixing his gaze on Feng Jiu, who was dressed in red. His eyes sparkled with admiration.","“Big Brother, there’s a stunningly beautiful woman here!”","At that moment, a man in his thirties stepped out of a flying beast, holding a triangular blade in his hand. He wore a black robe, with a black cross mark on his left cheek. His gaze was cold and ruthless, exuding a bloodthirsty aura.","As his cold, snake-like gaze swept over the group, it lingered on Feng Jiu, and a flash of admiration flickered in his eyes. His cold gaze fixed on her like that of a predator locking onto its prey.","Grandmaster Iron, Tie Song, who had been holding Yueniang’s hand, frowned and stepped forward to block Feng Jiu, cutting off the man’s gaze. At the same time, he spoke in a low, sharp voice.","“Bone-Devouring Asura! You should know that there are some people you cannot provoke. If you don’t want to die, you’d better leave now!”","“Haha...”","The man laughed softly, his voice cold and chilling. He stared at Tie Song, looked him up and down, and said, “Everyone who has seen me is dead. How did you recognize me?”","Tie Song stared at the triangular blade in his hand and said, “Isn’t that three-bladed dagger your weapon that you never part with? I’ve never seen you before, but I know the weapon in your hand.”","“I see.” He nodded, staring at him with a smile as cold as a snake’s. “So what if you recognize me? Everyone who has seen me must die, and you are no exception!”","As soon as he finished speaking, he swung the three-bladed dagger in his hand and attacked with such speed that it brought with it a sharp, cold wind. The people around them just surrounded him and started cheering.","“Kill him! Kill him!”","They knew their Big Brother’s rules. When he killed someone, he didn’t like them to come forward and help him. Unless he gave them the order to do so, suddenly attacking would only anger him. In his words, there was no one he wanted to kill that he couldn’t kill! He didn’t need anyone’s help!","As the three-bladed dagger lunged toward him, Tie Song stepped forward, twisting his wrist to draw a large sword, which he swung down with a powerful strike. The collision of the blades sent a surge of spiritual energy erupting outward, accompanied by the clanging sound of metal and sparks flying from the friction.","Behind them, Feng Jiu watched the scene calmly, neither intervening nor speaking, simply observing silently. No one knew what she was thinking.","Song Mi’er knew she was no match for that man, so she dared not intervene, instead standing beside Feng Jiu. She knew there was no safer place than by her side.","Yueniang felt some worry and tension. Tie Song hadn’t fought anyone in a long time, and after so long without combat, she didn’t know if he could match the Bone-Devouring Asura. Moreover, the Bone-Devouring Asura was infamous for his brutal strength and ruthless methods."]},{"number":4872,"title":"Chapter 4872: One Sword","paragraphs":["Chapter 4872: One Sword","Thinking of this, she couldn’t help but look ahead nervously, deciding that if he was in danger, she would rush forward to save him!","“Whoosh!”","“Good! Big Brother, kill him!” The cultivators around them shouted as they swung their weapons.","Feng Jiu watched for a while and also saw the disparity in strength between the two sides. The man called the Bone-Devouring Asura’s attacks were so fierce that every move was deadly.","Tie Song was slightly inferior to him. He was probably a weapon maker, and combat was not his strong suit. After only a few exchanges, Tie Song had already suffered several injuries, and his attacks were always inferior. If the fight continued, he would surely lose.","“Bang!”","In just a moment, Tie Song was kicked flying by his opponent, landing several meters away. His body slid backward along the ground, leaving a trail of friction marks behind him.","“Puff!”","Yueniang, who had been watching the fight, couldn’t help but cry out in surprise. She wanted to rush forward, but was held back by Mi’er.","“Your injuries haven’t healed yet! If you go up there, you’ll die,” Mi’er exclaimed while holding her back with both hands.","At that moment, the Bone-Devouring Asura looked at Tie Song lying on the ground and revealed a cold, sinister smile. He twisted the triangular blade in his hand and suddenly lunged forward. The blade carried a terrifying aura as it stabbed toward Tie Song’s chest, intending to take his life with this single strike!","“No!”","Yueniang screamed, her legs trembling and her face pale.","Tie Song lay on the ground, unable to help himself as he watched the triangular blade stab towards him. The aura of death enveloped him in that instant, making him feel as if he had stepped into the realm of death. A terrifying aura covered him, making it difficult for him to even breathe.","But he did not close his eyes, nor did he scream or beg for mercy. He just stared intently at the person coming towards him.","However, in the next moment, he saw a sharp sword qi with a green glow slash down in front of his eyes with a “whoosh,” as fast as lightning in the sky, catching him off guard.","The sword qi was so sudden and fierce that even the Bone-Devouring Asura didn’t expect such a powerful and murderous sword qi to appear out of nowhere. He tried to block it, tried to dodge it, but all he could do was turn his head to look at the sword qi as it came towards him.","It was a stunningly beautiful woman in a red robe, standing there with a long sword that emitted a faint blue glow in her hand. The blue sword qi, filled with overwhelming pressure, had emanated from the sword in her hand.","His eyes were wide open in shock, and in that instant, his eyes, wide open in terror, were filled with despair. His mouth opened instinctively to cry out, “No...”","Before the sound had even left his mouth, the sword qi had already struck, splitting him in two with a single blow.","Blood spurted out, and his spirit energy dissipated. His entire body fell backward, and as he fell, the two halves of his body shattered into pieces, like a piece of wood split in two, scattering across the ground...","On the ground, blood gushed out, and the man’s internal organs spilled onto the ground, causing everyone to tremble with fear and nausea...","“Big Brother!”","A cry rang out, and the surrounding cultivators finally came to their senses, staring in shock and horror at the split corpse on the ground and the red-clothed woman with a calm expression on her face..."]},{"number":4873,"title":"Chapter 4873: Missing","paragraphs":["Tie Song stared blankly at the corpse split in two before him, unable to suppress a swallow as he glanced toward Feng Jiu, dressed in red, not far away.","Although they had learned on the way that she was the Phoenix Sovereign, they had never seen her fight before. Now, witnessing her single sword strike decapitate the Bone-Devouring Asura, who possessed the strength of a Divine King, he finally realized that, despite being a woman, she possessed power capable of shattering the heavens and destroying the earth.","\"Kill her! Avenge our Big Brother!\"","Those men snapped out of their daze, their eyes glowing red with murderous intent as they stared at Feng Jiu, drawing their swords and closing in on her.","Seeing this, Tie Song on the ground quickly regained his senses, rose swiftly, and rushed forward with his knife to attack the cultivators.","Meanwhile, Song Mi'er, who was by Feng Jiu's side, stared at the approaching crowd, revealing a sly smile. She extended her hand, and a pot appeared in her palm. She swept forward and struck the cultivator who had charged at her.","She was no match for the Bone-Devouring Asura, but she could easily kill a few of these people. After all, she had undergone training and testing before being sent out by her family to gain experience.","Both sides began to fight. Standing beside Feng Jiu, Yueniang did not stand idly by. Her body had gradually recovered, and although her strength had not yet fully returned, she had no problem fighting others.","However, when she tried to step forward, she was held back by Feng Jiu.","\"Step back,\" Feng Jiu said, blocking the blade in front of her with her sword and kicking out at the same time.","Upon hearing Feng Jiu's words, the others avoided the attacks and moved behind Feng Jiu. In that instant, they saw a powerful aura emanating from Feng Jiu. As soon as the aura struck them, they froze in place, as if enduring immense pain, unable to move for a long time.","\"Pfftttt!\"","A mouthful of blood sprayed out, and they knelt down. At that moment, a cold light flashed in front of them, and sharp sword qi crossed their throats, instantly taking their lives.","The few people behind her paused for a moment, realizing that they hardly had to lift a finger to help her.","\"Go and search them for anything valuable,\" Feng Jiu said, putting away her sword.","\"Yes.\" The three men obeyed, quickly searching the bodies and handing everything over to her.","Feng Jiu took the items and said, \"Now that we're here, let's see if there's anywhere nearby to rest. We'll find a place to rest for the night and continue tomorrow.\"","\"Miss, if we go a little further, there should be a town where we can rest,\" said Tie Song, pointing in the direction of the road.","\"Let's go!\" She took the flying feather from her waist, sat on it, and headed in that direction.","The three people behind her hurriedly followed on their swords or flying artifacts.","Back at Yunxiao Mountain, Yue'er sat cross-legged under a tree, her hands supporting her chin, blinking her big eyes as she looked at the clouds and mist in front of her.","She missed her Mother. She wanted to see her Mother so badly.","In the past, her Mother wasn't here, but now her Mother had ascended, yet they still couldn't see her.","\"Yue'er, what are you doing here?\" Hao'er walked over. Seeing that the little face that usually wore a smile was now expressionless, he couldn't help but ask, \"Are you missing Mother?\""]},{"number":4874,"title":"Chapter 4874: Sparring","paragraphs":["Chapter 4874: Sparring","Yue’er turned to look at him and said, “Big Brother, don’t you miss Mother?”","Hao’er stood beside her, looking at the clouds and mist ahead, and said, “I do.”","How could he not miss her? He also wanted to see his mother and check on her. But their master had forbidden them from leaving the mountain, and there were protective barriers and spells in place. Without their master’s permission, they couldn’t leave.","“Big Brother, let’s sneak out and go find Mother, okay?” Yue’er’s eyes sparkled with excitement, her innocent voice tinged with anticipation. “Mother ascended to the heavens; she must have a celestial mansion! We’ve never been there before! Her immortal palace must be very safe, and Mother is very powerful! Even if there is danger, she will protect us. Big Brother, can we go see Mother?”","She stretched out her small hand and tugged at his sleeve, acting spoiled. After all, there were only the three siblings and their master in the mountains, and since they had returned, their master had not allowed them to go down the mountain. She really wanted to go out, to see her mother, to let her mother hug her.","“Big Brother... Big Brother, let’s go out! Let’s call our older brother and sneak out together, okay? We can protect ourselves now! Even if we encounter bad people, we won’t be afraid. Big Brother, please!” She pleaded softly, her little face filled with anticipation.","Hao’er’s heart was torn. On one hand, it felt like a little voice inside him was saying, “Go out! Go see your Mother, because you miss her too!”","But on the other hand, another voice was saying, “The master forbade them from going down the mountain, and their Mother also told them to obey the master and cultivate here. They shouldn’t go down the mountain...”","“Little sister.”","Just as Hao’er was struggling, Muchen’s voice came.","He was still holding a sword in his hand, sweat dripping from his face, his clothes soaked with sweat, breathing slightly heavily, looking as if he had just finished practicing swordplay.","“Brother.” Yue’er saw him and couldn’t help but call out softly, lowering her head.","She thought that her brother was going to scold her again.","Sure enough, as soon as she had this thought, she heard her brother’s voice.","“You haven’t been concentrating on your cultivation lately, and now you want your Big Brother to take you down the mountain. Don’t you know that this will not only make Master angry, but Mother will also be angry?”","Muchen, looking like the older brother he was, scolded her with a stern expression. “Mother’s enemies are very powerful. If we stay by her side, we will be seen as her weak point and used to threaten her. If that happens and Mother is put in danger, what will you do then?”","“I... I... I just miss Mother so much...” Her head drooped lower and lower, her voice trembling with sorrow and resentment.","“We all miss Mother, but we can’t help her. However, we can at least not hold her back.”","Muchen said, looking at her, “Focus on your cultivation. In a while, we’ll ask the master to take us to see Mother. If the master takes us, nothing will happen.”","“Listen to your brother and cultivate hard!” Hao’er rubbed her head and said.","“Mmm.” Yue’er replied softly and didn’t say anything else.","“Big Brother, I learned a new sword technique today. I want to spar with you.” Muchen looked at him and said.","Upon hearing this, Hao’er nodded: “Alright.” With that, the two headed toward the open area."]},{"number":4875,"title":"Chapter 4875: Slips Away","paragraphs":["Chapter 4875: Slips Away","Yue’er sat there, watching them practicing swordsmanship and sparring in the distance. She couldn’t help but hug her knees, rest her chin on them, and stare blankly at the clouds and mist in front of her.","On the other side, Hao’er, who was sparring with Muchen, kept an eye on her. Seeing her low spirits, he felt uneasy. After sparring with Muchen for a while and taking a break, he saw her still sitting there motionless and couldn’t help but feel concerned.","“Why don’t we go ask our master? I’m worried about Yue’er.” Hao’er said, furrowing his brows slightly and pursing his lips.","Muchen felt just as bad inside. He nodded and said, “Let’s go ask our master.”","Saying that, the two headed towards their master’s cave abode.","Yue’er sat there. Although she knew that her brothers were right and that she should listen to them, she just missed her Mother so much!","The more she tried not to think about it, the more she wanted to think about it.","In the past, she couldn’t see her Mother, but now that they were both in the Immortal Realm, even if she couldn’t see her openly, she could at least sneak a peek, right?","She would just look from afar and come back right away.","With that in mind, she immediately got up and ran to her cave abode, where she left a message for her brothers. Then, she summoned her contract beast, the Nine-Tails Spirit Fox.","“I’m going to see my Mother. You can travel across dimensions, can’t you? Take me there!”","“Master, isn’t it a good idea to go secretly?”","The Nine-Tails Spirit Fox asked with some concern. Although it had become smaller and weaker due to its contract master’s weak power, it still had the ability to travel across dimensions. But if it left like this, wouldn’t the Azure Emperor be angry?","“Master won’t let me go down the mountain. If I don’t sneak out, how else can I go? Plus, Big Brother and my brother won’t let me go either. I have no choice but to sneak down on my own.” Yue’er said, looking at it and adding, “Hurry up, hurry up, before they come back.”","The Nine-Tails Spirit Fox hesitated and said, “But my power is so weak now. Even if I still have the ability to transfer through space-time, I’m not sure if I won’t make a mistake, so I’m worried...”","It was worried that it would send its master to another place, which would be troublesome.","“Where could you possibly send her? Even if you make a mistake, it would still be within this Immortal Realm, right? It’s fine, don’t worry. Even if I can’t go directly to where my mother is, I can find her myself when I get there.”","“But... but I’m worried...” It was truly worried! If something happened to its young master, what would it do?","“Stop worrying. There’s nothing to worry about. Father and Mother said that good people are protected by heaven, and I’ve been working hard to cultivate myself since I became a disciple! I can protect myself now, nothing will happen to me. Hurry up, hurry up, or else my brothers will come back and I won’t be able to leave even if I want to.”","She said anxiously. Her two brothers were sparring and she didn’t know where they had gone. What if they came back? How would she leave?","She still wanted to see her Mother! She promised that she would come back as soon as she saw her Mother.","Seeing her insist, the Nine-Tails Spirit Fox sighed helplessly and said, “Alright, go outside. There’s an array barrier in this cave abode, and I won’t be able to teleport you through the layers of restrictions.”","“Alright, hurry up.” Yue’er hurried out of the cave abode and looked around outside. “Is this fine? This should be alright, right? Let’s quickly start!”"]},{"number":4876,"title":"Chapter 4876: Furious","paragraphs":["The Nine-Tails Spirit Fox looked around, nodded, and walked forward, unable to resist asking, \"Are you really sure you want to leave? What if I teleport you somewhere else?\" Its power had been weakened by its master's low power, and it hadn't tried its teleportation ability in so long that it was a little panicked.","\"I've made up my mind. I've left a message for my brothers, telling them not to worry. I'll be back soon.\" She said, worried that her two brothers would suddenly return, so she added, \"Hurry up!\"","Seeing this, the Nine-Tails Spirit Fox had no choice but to come to her side and say, \"Hold onto my tail.\"","\"Mm Hmm!\"","Yue'er's little face flushed with excitement, and she quickly grabbed its tail. In the next moment, a ray of light surged from its body...","Over there, Hao'er and Muchen were kneeling in front of their master's cave abode, begging, \"Master, we really want to see our Mother. Please, master...\"","Before they could finish, their master, who was drinking tea, frowned, put down his teacup, and Shadow One rushed outside.","Seeing this, the two looked at each other and quickly got up to follow.","When they came outside, they saw a ray of light shoot out of the barrier of Yunxiao Mountain and disappear into the sky. Seeing this, the two's expressions changed, and they both thought of their sister, assuming that someone had sneaked into Yunxiao Mountain and kidnapped her.","\"Yue'er!\"","\"There's no need to go.\"","The Azure Emperor said, folding his arms and looking up at the light that had disappeared in the sky. \"That's the aura of the ancient Sacred Beast, the Nine-Tails Spirit Fox. That girl must have asked the Nine-Tails Spirit Fox to take her away. She's so rebellious, she doesn't even listen to me anymore.\"","His brows were still furrowed, and his expression was slightly gloomy, as if he was a little displeased.","\"Master, what about Yue'er?\" Hao'er couldn't help but ask, but seeing his master's solemn expression, the words stopped at his lips.","Yue'er had left secretly, and it seemed that she had angered her master. They had been with their master for so long, but they had never seen him look so upset.","After thinking for a moment, Hao'er still spoke up and said, \"Master, let's go find Yue'er!\"","\"Find her?\" The Azure Emperor looked at him and asked, \"Do you know where she went? Are you sure that the Nine-Tails Spirit Fox will take her to Feng Jiu?\"","Hearing this, Hao'er was taken aback. Just as he was about to ask what his master meant, he heard Muchen ask the same question.","\"Master, are you saying that the Nine-Tails Spirit Fox won't take my sister to her Mother?\" Muchen looked at him and asked, his small hands hanging at his sides clenched into fists, his heart filled with worry.","The Azure Emperor stared at the sky for a long time before gently exhaling. His slightly furrowed brows relaxed, and he walked over to the soft couch under the tree and lay down, saying, \"The ancient nine-tailed spirit fox does indeed have the ability to teleport, but how old is that girl? Is she strong enough? Even if the ancient nine-tailed spirit fox has that ability, she will lower its power.\"","Hearing this, the two of them felt anxious, and worry appeared on their little faces. \"Master, what should we do?\"","\"What should we do? Hmph! Since that girl won't listen, let her go out and suffer a bit. At least she'll learn her lesson and stop disobeying in the future.\" He closed his eyes and ignored Yue'er, who had left Yunxiao Mountain.","\"Master!\"","The two knelt down, called out to him, and pleaded with him."]},{"number":4877,"title":"Chapter 4877: Accident","paragraphs":["Chapter 4877: Accident","The Azure Emperor lay still with his eyes closed, and the two of them remained kneeling quietly by his side. After a while, he seemed to open his eyes with a hint of resignation and looked at the two of them.","“The two of you have always been calm and steady in nature. That girl is different from you; she has a playful nature and is quite mischievous. Now that she has sneaked out, let her go out and learn a lesson. You two should return to your cultivation and not worry about her. I have a strand of my divine essence on her. If she truly faces danger, I will appear to save her.”","That girl was his disciple. No matter how mischievous or disobedient she was, she was still his disciple. He would never truly abandon her. However, using this opportunity to let her taste a bit of hardship was necessary.","Hearing this, the two finally relaxed. As long as the master had spoken, they could rest assured. Especially Hao’er, who had personally witnessed the master appearing to save him in a moment of danger last time. Therefore, he bowed respectfully to him.","“Thank you, Master.”","“Thank you, Master.” Muchen also kowtowed, then stood up and followed his Big Brother out.","After the two left, the Azure Emperor stretched out his hand and calculated with his fingers. He frowned and then relaxed, his gaze fixed on the distant clouds, lost in thought.","The two who had left returned to the cave abode and saw the note left by Yue’er. They felt helpless.","“Big Brother, do you think our sister will be in danger? From what I understood, our master wants her to suffer a little. She went to look for our Mother on her own. What if she can’t find her?” Muchen asked anxiously.","“Our master is very powerful. If he said it’s fine, then it’s fine. Don’t worry! Let’s just cultivate here and wait for our sister to return.” Hao’er patted him on the shoulder and said.","At the same time, Yue’er, who had been teleported away by the Nine-Tailed White Fox, was feeling rather unfortunate. The Nine-Tailed White Fox’s power had indeed weakened significantly. It had wanted to send Yue’er to Feng Jiu’s territory, but it was unable to do so despite its best efforts.","“Where am I? Why is there no one here?” Yue’er asked the little white fox beside her, frowning slightly, looking a little unhappy.","The Nine-Tailed White Fox lowered its head and said softly, “I don’t know where this is either. I wanted to send my master to the Phoenix Sovereign’s territory, but... my strength...”","It didn’t dare to say any more. It was afraid that what it feared would happen would happen. It had been worried that this would happen, and sure enough, it had made a mistake.","“Can you take me somewhere else?” Yue’er asked hopefully.","The Nine-Tailed White Fox shook its head: “The barrier array of the Azure Emperor is too powerful. This time, it drained a lot of my spiritual energy, and I can no longer transport you away. I have to wait until my spiritual energy recovers before I can take you out of here.”","It was also helpless. It had never wanted to make a contract with the little girl, but there was no choice. The master’s Mother had captured it, so it had no choice but to make the contract. Now even its teleportation ability, as a legendary ancient Sacred Beast, had weakened to this extent.","Upon hearing this, Yue’er thought for a moment and said, “Alright then! Go into the spatial realm to meditate and cultivate. Once you’ve recovered, be sure to let me know.”","“Alright, master, be careful here on your own.” It urged with concern.","“Alright, I know. I’ll protect myself.” Yue’er said, storing it in the space. She looked around at the surrounding forest, then summoned her flying sword and took to the air, wanting to see where she was."]},{"number":4878,"title":"Chapter 4878: Threat","paragraphs":["Chapter 4878: Threat","However, as she ascended on her flying sword, she saw an endless forest and mountain peaks disappearing into the clouds. She froze, her mouth agape in astonishment.","“Where on earth have they brought me? What kind of remote mountain forest is this? Where am I?” she muttered to herself. As she tried to ascend further, she felt an overwhelming sense of pressure permeating the sky.","“A barrier?” She froze, looking up at the sky, her heart filled with shock.","There was a barrier here; she could sense it.","Because her body contained the aura of an ancient Sacred Beast, she was not afraid of the barrier’s pressure. However, flying on a flying sword above the trees was too conspicuous, and she had no idea where she was, so she decided to head downwards.","Her tiny figure glided cautiously through the forest on her flying sword, maintaining a distance of about ten meters above the ground. When she saw the fierce beasts moving in the forest below, her eyes widened in shock.","Had she landed in a deep, old forest where fierce beasts roamed? How was she going to leave this forest? Looking up, she saw nothing but forest and mountains all around her. She couldn’t see any way out. Would she get lost and never find her way out?","Thinking of this, she couldn’t help but worry. At that moment, she also regretted her decision. If she hadn’t sneaked out, maybe she wouldn’t have ended up in such a place.","She kept walking in one direction until it grew dark, but she didn’t encounter a single person or see a way out. Instead, she saw many different kinds of fierce beasts.","However, because she had the aura of an ancient Sacred Beast, when she saw some flying beasts approaching her, she released the pressure of the ancient Sacred Beast within her to scare them away. Therefore, she didn’t encounter any major problems along the way.","As night fell, the atmosphere in the forest grew increasingly eerie and terrifying. She found a small cave to rest in and lit a small fire to keep warm.","“What is this?” As she sat down in the corner, she felt something on the ground and picked it up. It felt like the fur of a fierce beast. Just as she was thinking about it, she heard a roar from outside.","“Roar!”","Hearing the beast’s roar, she hurried toward the entrance, clutching the fur tightly in her hand. At the cave’s opening, she saw a red-flame lion with a wounded hind leg baring its teeth and roaring at her.","Looking at the ring of fur around the lion’s neck, she couldn’t help but glance at the fur she was holding in her hand. In an instant, she realized that this cave was the lion’s territory.","“Roar!”","It was a peak-level sacred beast—a fierce beast. Seeing its den occupied by a human child, it bared its sharp fangs and roared angrily. “Um, I know this is your den, but... but I have nowhere else to go! It’s too cold outside. Please let me stay here!”","Yue’er said, looking as if she was trying to negotiate. She wrinkled her little face, thought for a moment, and then tentatively said in a childish voice, “How about you come in too, but you can’t hurt me, okay?”","The sacred beast was intelligent and could understand her words, but it did not agree because this was its territory!","“Roar!”","It roared threateningly, taking steps forward, opening its mouth to reveal its teeth, as if ready to pounce.","Seeing this, Yue’er gripped the dagger, her eyes widening in anger: “Don’t think I’m afraid of you! I’m not afraid!”"]},{"number":4879,"title":"Chapter 4879: Treatment","paragraphs":["Chapter 4879: Treatment","As she spoke, she released the ancient Sacred Beast’s overwhelming pressure, aiming to intimidate the crimson-flame lion at the peak of the sacred beast realm before her.","The lion, which had been about to pounce forward and devour the human child as a snack, sensed the ancient Sacred Beast’s aura. Its paws halted mid-step, and a hint of fear and reverence flashed in its eyes. It looked at the tiny human figure before it and involuntarily backed away, emitting low, muffled growls.","Seeing it retreat, Yue’er secretly sighed in relief. It retreated to a tree outside the cave entrance, lying there while watching her inside the cave and licking the wound on its hind leg that was bleeding.","Seeing the wound on its leg oozing blood, even if it licked it clean, fresh blood continued to seep out after a while. Perhaps due to excessive blood loss, the lion also looked listless.","Yue’er sat by the fire in the cave, eating the dried rations from her spatial pocket, watching the lion lying listlessly under the tree outside. She felt torn inside. Should she let it in? But she was afraid it would attack her. Should she not let it in? After all, she had taken its den.","Just then, a flash of lightning split the pitch-black sky, followed by a clap of thunder. The wind picked up, rustling the leaves, and the small fire in the cave flickered in the breeze.","Soon, a light rain began to fall. At first, it was just a drizzle, but gradually, the rain grew heavier, accompanied by the rumbling of thunder...","The wind made her feel a little cold, so she took out a small cloak from her space and wrapped it around herself. She saw the lion under the tree still standing in the rain. After thinking for a moment, she bit her lip, walked forward, and called out, “Hey, come in!”","The crimson-flame lion heard her voice, glanced at her, thought for a moment, then got up and walked slowly towards the cave entrance, its hind legs slightly bent and its steps slow. When it reached the cave entrance, its eyes were guarded and hesitant.","“You can rest over there.” Yue’er stepped back to the side of the cave entrance and pointed to the corner inside.","Seeing this, the lion limped inside and lay down in the corner. However, the wound on its leg was still oozing blood. After a while, perhaps because it could no longer hold itself up, it lay there motionless, as if dead.","Yue’er kept watch. Seeing that the lion had fainted, with its leg wounds still bleeding and a large pool of blood seeping from where it lay, she thought for a moment before taking out some medicine and placing it over the fire.","Smoke mingled with the wind blowing in through the cave entrance, drifting into the darkness. The unconscious lion inhaled the smoke. After a while, Yue’er cautiously approached, retrieved the medicine, and began to stop the bleeding and bandage the wound.","Perhaps because of the medicine and bandages, the lion woke up and opened its eyes, but it remained motionless, staring at the young human girl who was bandaging it.","“I took your spot, so bandaging you is my way of making it up to you,” Yue’er said, stepping back to the fire. “You can’t move because I used medicine. I was worried you might attack me, so I had to use it on you. But don’t worry, I won’t kill you. I’ll leave as soon as it’s daylight.”","She held her hands over the fire to warm them, rubbing them together for warmth, then glanced at the lion again and muttered, “Your rank is so high, and your strength must be formidable. If not for a Sacred Beast-level creature, you shouldn’t have been injured, right? How did you end up getting scratched up so badly?”"]},{"number":4880,"title":"Chapter 4880: On the Verge of Death","paragraphs":["Chapter 4880: On the Verge of Death","“Roar!”","However, the response to her was not from the lion lying in the cave, but from the sound of a beast roaring in the stormy night.","“A beast’s roar?” Yue’er looked out of the cave warily, listening to the sound, which seemed to be coming from not too far away.","At that moment, the lion crouched in the corner heard the roar from outside and immediately struggled to stand up, but it had smelled Yue’er’s medicine, and the medicine had not yet worn off, so how could it stand up?","Seeing its state and hearing the repeated roars outside, Yue’er asked, “Are they looking for you? Could it be the fierce beasts outside that injured you like this? I can hear more than one beast from the sound.”","“Grrrrrr!” It let out a low growl toward Yue’er, its voice tinged with urgency.","“Do you want me to neutralize the medicine?” Yue’er asked.","“Grrrrrr!” It cried out urgently.","Seeing this, Yue’er thought for a moment and said, “Alright, I’ll neutralize it, but you must promise not to attack me.”","“Grrrr!”","Yue’er took out a bottle, brought it close to its nostrils, and let it sniff. After a moment, it stood up and swiftly darted out of the cave.","“Hey, lion, where are you going?”","Yue’er shouted, rushing to the cave entrance, but she didn’t follow it out. At that moment, she saw that the cave entrance was already surrounded by several lions identical to the injured one. Among them, one was as powerful as the injured lion, while the others, though Saint Beast-level, hadn’t reached the peak of their power.","Without hesitation, the six or seven lions charged forward to attack the injured lion. Seeing the fight, Yue’er gripped her dagger tightly and watched the lions battling in the rain.","One of the lions was knocked back to the entrance of the cave. Upon seeing Yue’er standing at the entrance, its eyes flashed with a bloodthirsty ferocity, and it opened its mouth and lunged toward her.","“Roar!”","“Rooooaaaaar!”","However, just as the lion lunged at Yue’er and she prepared to fight, the lion she had helped bandage suddenly pounced from behind, biting the lion that had attacked Yue’er and dragging it back with great force.","However, as it turned to bite the lion, it gave the other lions an opportunity. Almost simultaneously, several lions pounced, using their sharp claws and teeth with relentless ferocity, intent on killing it.","Yue’er stood there in shock. She hadn’t expected the lion to turn around and save her. Though, she was capable of saving herself and wouldn’t let the lion hurt her...","Watching the injured lion being attacked and torn apart by the other lions, its flesh ripped off and blood spilling everywhere, she felt a surge of anger. She immediately gripped the dagger and charged forward.","“Get out of the way!”","The aura of the ancient Sacred Beast surged forth alongside the dagger in her hand, enveloping the lions in an instant.","That was the aura of the king of beasts, the pressure of an ancient Sacred Beast—something those lions could never withstand. In an instant, the lions released their grip and let out a low growl. One of them, struck by Yue’er’s dagger, scattered and fled into the rain-soaked night...","On the ground, rain washed away the bloodstains. The lion with its hind legs bandaged lay dying on the ground, its body covered in gruesome wounds. The most fatal wound was the one on its neck, where it had been bitten..."]},{"number":4881,"title":"Chapter 4881: Advancement","paragraphs":["Chapter 4881: Advancement","Its body convulsed as the rain pelted down, washing away the blood-soaked fur on its neck. Its fur was matted together, and it stared at Yue’er with wide eyes, blood trickling from its mouth.","Yue’er looked at it, knowing that if she didn’t save it, it would surely die.","She thought for a moment, then took out a medicinal pill from her spatial ring and stuffed it into its mouth, saying, “This is a pill my Mother made. I’m giving it to you to see if it can save your life.”","She then took out some haemostatic medicine and sprinkled it on its neck to stop the bleeding. Just as she was about to bandage it, she saw a powerful aura surge from the lion that had eaten the medicinal pill. Immediately, a beam of light burst forth, and at the same time, a bolt of lightning suddenly split the sky.","Yue’er looked up and hurriedly retreated into the cave. Just as she reached the entrance, a lightning tribulation echoed, and a bolt of lightning struck the tree, sending sparks flying.","She gasped and retreated further into the cave, hiding in a corner. She heard three lightning tribulations strike the sky in quick succession, each more powerful than the last. As the three lightning tribulations fell, the area around her returned to calm, and even the rain stopped.","At the same time, in the mansion in this area, those who heard the three lightning tribulations looked up in surprise and stood on the roof of the mansion, looking towards the forest where the lightning tribulation had struck.","“It has been a long time since a Sacred Beast was born in this place. Why are there three lightning tribulations striking today, signaling the birth of a Sacred Beast?” an old man said, stroking his beard, his wise eyes filled with contemplation.","“Old Predecessor, the birth of a Sacred Beast on our immortal island is a great blessing. Let me lead some men to find it and see what kind of Sacred Beast has been born, so we can bind it to our clan’s descendants.” A middle-aged man smiled as he spoke, folding his arms and gazing at the distant forest.","Hearing this, the Old Predecessor smiled, paused for a moment while stroking his beard, and said, “A Sacred Beast is proud by nature. If we capture it and give it to the younger generation of the clan, it will be too easy for them to obtain. Furthermore, if it is not tamed by their own hands, it will retain some of its wild nature.”","He paused for a moment and said, “It’s already late at night, so let’s leave it until tomorrow. Let the younger generation of the clan go to the forest themselves to search for it. It will be good experience for them.”","“But, Old Predecessor, it’s a Sacred Beast. The younger generation of the clan won’t be able to tame it, will they?” The middle-aged man hesitated.","“None of them can tame it?” The old man glanced at him, his aged voice carrying an unknown meaning.","Hearing this, the middle-aged man’s heart stirred, and he said, “Old Predecessor, you want Jun Yan...”","“Go make the arrangements!” The old man said, turning and heading downwards without saying another word.","Hearing this, the middle-aged man fell silent for a moment before turning and heading downwards as well.","Meanwhile, in the forest, Yue’er was staring wide-eyed in surprise at the majestic lion looking at her with an air of arrogance.","Especially, the wounds on its body that should have been fatal had all healed as it advanced to become a Sacred Beast. Moreover, on its forehead, a flame-like mark was now clear and imposing.","“You... you’ve advanced?”","Yue’er stammered, thinking to herself, ‘How powerful are Mother’s medicinal pills? A single pill not only healed the lion’s wounds but also allowed it to advance from the peak of saint beast to a sacred beast. But why is the lion looking at her with such intense eyes?’"]},{"number":4882,"title":"Chapter 4882: Taking the Initiative","paragraphs":["Was it planning to eat her?!","Just as she was thinking this, she saw the lion bend its front paws and kneel down. \"Thank you for saving me and helping me advance to become a Sacred Beast. From now on, I will follow you, master.\"","\"Huh? Master?\" Yue'er was stunned and said, \"I already have a contract beast.\"","\"I know. Master's true contract beast is an ancient Sacred Beast. However, master, my combat strength is very strong. I can protect you. In this forest, there aren't many Sacred Beasts. With me by your side, you won't encounter any danger.\"","In truth, what was even more important was that she could provide the medicinal pills needed for its advancement, and with an ancient Sacred Beast as her contract beast, it knew that this human girl before it must be of extraordinary origin. Following her would bring only benefits, no drawbacks.","You must know that in this forest, there are countless fierce beasts of the Sacred Beast rank, but most of them have stagnated at the peak of the Sacred Beast rank and cannot advance further. Some have even waited for hundreds of years without becoming Sacred Beasts.","Having obtained the opportunity to become a Sacred Beast, it naturally wouldn't miss the chance to follow her.","Who knows? By following her, it might even advance to become a Super Sacred Beast!","Thinking of this, its gaze towards her grew even more intense.","Hearing this, Yue'er thought for a moment, her round eyes twinkling, and said, \"I already have a life-bound contract beast. If we form a contract, you can only be my servant.\"","\"Alright, master, please bind me quickly!\" It approached eagerly.","Coming across such a creature eager to become her servant beast, Yue'er couldn't help but feel helpless. However, she wouldn't refuse such a gift, especially since this lion had eaten one of her Mother's precious medicinal pills!","So, she recited the contract ritual her Mother had taught her, and a drop of her blood flew into the lion's forehead, forming a master-servant contract.","After the contract was formed, the flame on its forehead changed shape.","After binding the lion, Yue'er waved it into the cave, sat by the fire to warm her hands, and asked, \"What is this place? How can I leave here?\"","Hearing this, the lion paused, surprised, and asked, \"Master, you don't know where this is? How did you get here?\"","\"I was transferred here, but there was a mistake, so I ended up here.\" Yue'er said, resting her chin on her hand as she looked at it and asked, \"Do you know the way out of here?\"","Upon hearing this, the lion revealed a human-like wry smile: \"Master, you may not know, but this is no ordinary place. It is the forest where the floating immortal island of a great emperor resides. The emperor of this island is Xiao Tian the Great Emperor. As far as I know, he is a reclusive immortal who has withdrawn from the world to cultivate in seclusion. This immortal island is inhabited by the descendants of Xiao Tian the Great Emperor, and it is protected by a barrier array. Ordinary people cannot enter or leave this place.\"","It looked at its master before it, truly wondering how she had managed to get here. Not only had she entered the Xiao Tian Great Emperor's immortal island, but she had done so quietly and without a trace. It seemed that the Xiao Tian and the others were unaware that a human child had entered their immortal island territory!","Yue'er heard this and was speechless.","\"What? It's the immortal island where a great emperor has secluded himself to cultivate? If they find me on their territory, will they capture me?\" Yue'er couldn't help but worry.","\"That's just the beginning. There's another matter the master must prepare for mentally,\" the lion said."]},{"number":4883,"title":"Chapter 4883: Great Emperor Xiao Tian","paragraphs":["Chapter 4883: Great Emperor Xiao Tian","“What’s the matter? What preparation?” Yue’er wrinkled her little nose as she asked.","The lion gazed out at the pitch-black sky and said, “When I advanced earlier, three lightning tribulations struck. I fear it may have alarmed the descendants of the Great Emperor Xiao Tian. They must already know a Sacred Beast has been born in this forest. Knowing this, they will certainly send men in to search. Therefore...”","“So they’ll come looking for you, and might very well run into me!” Yue’er now grasped the gravity of the situation. If she were captured, who knew what fate awaited her? This place was utterly cut off from the world—even if she cried for help, no one would know she’d ended up here!","She rose to her feet, pacing the cave while murmuring to herself, “Let me think... there must be a way...”","Night deepened. The forest after the rain exuded the scent of earth and fallen leaves. Breezes swept into the cave, bringing waves of coolness.","The lion, concerned his young mistress might catch a chill, invited her to sleep beside him, offering the warmth of his body and the comfort of his thick fur.","Bound by their master-servant pact, Yue’er felt reassured, knowing the lion would never harm her. After all, one ironclad rule of such contracts was that should the master perish, the pact beast could not survive.","After much deliberation, Yue’er found no solution. Resigned, she curled up beside the lion and fell asleep...","The following dawn, at the Xiao Family Manor, disciples of all ages stood in orderly rows before the clearing, listening to the Patriarch’s address and instructions.","“This forest trial is meant to hone your adaptability and combat prowess. Remember: Xiao family disciples must always support one another. The foremost clan rule is etched in your minds—never raise a hand against kin.”","Patriarch Xiao stood with his hands clasped behind his back, delivering his address. Upon receiving the respectful acknowledgement from the assembled, he continued: “Once within the forest, you must rely solely upon one another for support. Ensure your own safety above all else. This is a trial to enhance your combat prowess, not a mission to sacrifice your lives. Should you encounter danger beyond your capacity to handle, remember to shatter your jade token immediately to be transported back.”","“Yes, Patriarch!” the group responded once more.","“Elder, escort them to the teleportation array,” the Patriarch Xiao instructed the elder standing beside him.","“Understood,” the elder acknowledged, leading the group towards the array.","Watching them depart, the Patriarch Xiao surveyed the surroundings, furrowing his brow. “Why has Junyan not arrived? Did you inform him?”","A middle-aged man stepped forward from behind. “I did, Patriarch. The Young Master set out early this morning.”","Hearing this, Patriarch Xiao remained silent for a moment before sighing. “That child is naturally aloof. While there are outstanding young talents within the family, none have caught his eye or earned his companionship. I had intended for Junheng to accompany him, yet it seems he has departed ahead of us.”","“The young master need not worry, Patriarch. He is the most gifted and capable scion the Xiao family has seen in centuries. Even the Old Predecessor speaks of him in the highest terms. He will manage perfectly well on his own,” the middle-aged man assured him.","“Go and inform Junheng. Once in the forest, he must seek out Junyan. It would be best if they journey together, for that is a Sacred Beast,” Patriarch Xiao instructed, his concern evident.","“Understood.” The middle-aged man acknowledged before swiftly departing towards the teleportation array.","Meanwhile, deep within the forest, Yue’er sat astride the lion’s back, darting swiftly through the forest..."]},{"number":4884,"title":"Chapter 4884: Waterfall","paragraphs":["\"Giggle, giggle... Slow down, slow down, don't run so fast.\" A silvery laugh escaped Yue'er's lips, carried by the breeze and scattered throughout the forest.","Yue'er's petite form sat astride the lion's back, her hands clutching tightly to the thick mane at its neck. Though her small frame jolted slightly with each stride of the galloping beast, her little face was lit up with a joyful, delighted smile.","At such a tender age, she had already cast aside last night's unease and worry. Now, perched atop the lion's back, she felt the speed of their flight through the forest and the cool breeze against her face, her whole heart soaring with the sensation.","She had made up her mind: since there was no other way, she would simply have to hide as best she could. Once the little fox had replenished the spirit energy it had expended, it could carry her away from this place.","In the meantime, as long as she remained well-hidden within the forest and avoided detection by the descendants of that Great Emperor Xiao Tian, she would be safe!","The galloping lion delivered her to the edge of a woodland near a waterfall, announcing: \"Mistress, this waterfall originates from mountain springs, and within it lies a spiritual spring. Bathing and cultivating within its waters greatly benefits one's cultivation. Should you wish to bathe, avoid the area directly beneath the cascading waterfall. The current there is far too swift, and the force of the water crashing down from such a height is too great. You are too small to withstand it. Bathe in the lower reaches instead.\"","\"Wow, this place is truly beautiful!\"","Yue'er gazed at the cascade. The water plunging from the heights resembled a celestial river cascading from the heavens. As it crashed onto the rocks below, it sent up a vast spray of water droplets. With the morning sun slanting down, a rainbow arched across the waterfall, creating a truly magnificent sight.","Yue'er promptly leaped down from the lion's back. She dared not approach the base of the falls, for the torrent was truly formidable. The spray from the cascading water flew in all directions, and she knew that if she ventured near, she'd likely be swept downstream. Besides, her petite frame wouldn't withstand the force there.","The lion grew uneasy about her safety, for its master was so small. Especially when it saw her removing her boots and preparing to enter the water, it was alarmed. Rushing forward, it seized her collar and began dragging her back.","\"Oh? Why are you biting my clothes?\" Yue'er, who had been about to enter the water, was now being hauled back by the lion's grip on her collar. She turned her head and asked.","Only after dragging her away from the water's edge did the lion release its grip. \"Mistress, this water is too deep. You won't be able to stand. Go over there.\" With that, it seized her hem and pulled her towards a shallower spot.","\"Hehe...\"","Yue'er giggled, her beautiful eyes crinkling into crescent moons. \"I can swim, you know! I can even hold my breath!\" Her mother had taught them. She and her two brothers could all swim. Mother said if you couldn't swim and fell into the water, you'd drown, so she taught them.","\"The water's too shallow here. It's no fun.\"","Yue'er looked at the spot the lion had dragged her to. It was a small area surrounded by rocks, with water only knee-deep in the center.","So, she looked around and chose another spot: \"I'll swim here! The water's deeper here. You just watch over me from the side. If any fierce beasts or people come near, just tell me.\" Yue'er moved to the back of the waterfall, where rocks blocked the flow, ensuring the cascading water wouldn't reach her."]},{"number":4885,"title":"Chapter 4885: Meeting for the first time","paragraphs":["Deep within these ancient mountains, not a soul was to be found. With Yue'er being so young, and seeing the lion standing guard nearby, she promptly stripped herself bare and leapt into the water.","The lion heard a splash behind him and glanced back with concern. Seeing his young mistress splashing about in the water, her face lit up with joy, he finally relaxed. It seemed the young mistress truly knew how to swim. With that settled, the lion needn't fret for her safety; keeping watch on their surroundings would suffice.","Yue'er floated in the cool, clear water, the refreshing sensation washing over her body. Lying back with her head resting on a rock, she kicked her feet at the surface, giggling softly.","\"Mistress, the mountain water is cold. Do not soak too long—its better to get out now!\" The lion turned to watch her in the water and called out.","\"I'll stay a while longer. I haven't washed my hair yet!\" Yue'er replied, sinking her body lower until her entire head was submerged. She untied her hair and rinsed it in the water.","The lion kept watch over their surroundings while observing her in the water. Suddenly, it whipped its head around and exclaimed, \"Mistress, rise at once! Someone approaches!\"","\"What?\" Yue'er surfaced, her hair splayed wetly across her face, obscuring her vision. She hastily pushed it aside and scanned the woods, catching a faint glimpse of a figure approaching on a sword. \"Quick!\" she whispered urgently. \"Get into the space!\"","With a flick of her thoughts, she drew it into the space. Just as she prepared to rise and find cover, the figure emerged from the woods. Startled, she instantly suppressed her aura and sank beneath the water.","Xiao Junyan's indifferent gaze swept the surroundings, his handsome brows slightly furrowed. He had distinctly sensed the aura of a Sacred Beast nearby moments ago. How could it have vanished upon reaching this spot? He stood motionless, carefully sweeping the area with his divine sense. Still, he detected nothing.","Glancing towards the waterfall, he heard the thunderous roar of the cascading water. The air was thick with mist, and where sunlight met the spray, a rainbow arched brilliantly across the falls. Thus, he strode over. Seeing the water was clear and clean, he crouched down, scooped up a handful from the edge, and washed his face.","About two meters upstream from him, Yue'er, holding her breath underwater, could no longer endure it. She quietly surfaced, took a deep breath with her face turned upwards, then slipped back down silently. The roar of the waterfall provided a perfect cover, and Xiao Junyan, two meters downstream, remained oblivious.","After washing his face, he took off his upper garment, loosened his sash, and removed his boots. Clad only in his undergarments and barefoot, he made his way to the rock where the waterfall crashed down. There, he sat cross-legged and began to cultivate his spirit energy.","The force of the cascading water and its icy chill proved an ideal training ground for one mastering the Frost Art. As his spirit energy circulated within, the qi within his meridians followed suit. His divine sense extended outward, sharpening his five senses and sixth awareness to extraordinary clarity.","Yue'er remained submerged in the water. After holding her breath for an extended period without seeing the figure depart, she quietly surfaced to take a breath. Having lingered too long in the icy mountain waters, her small body was beginning to struggle. Her lips trembled slightly, and her teeth chattered softly, emitting a faint, delicate sound."]},{"number":4886,"title":"Chapter 4886: Xiao Junyan","paragraphs":["Chapter 4886: Xiao Junyan","Though the sound was faint, muffled by the roar of the waterfall, to Xiao Junyan—who had released his senses beneath the cascade—a distinct aura was perceptible.","In that instant, his piercing eyes snapped open. Turning, he lunged towards the source of the aura.","The cold was unbearable. Yue’er was just about to slip quietly out of the water when, the moment her upper body emerged and she prepared to hide behind a rock, a fierce aura swept towards her. The speed was so swift she had no chance to react.","“Ahhhhhhh!”","She shrieked, feeling a hand seize her ankle. Instantly, her vision blurred as she was hoisted naked from the water, splashing droplets everywhere.","Xiao Junyan’s expressionless, handsome face studied the creature he’d pulled from the water. A barely perceptible twitch flickered at the corner of his mouth.","This completely naked... little girl?","Yue’er froze, genuinely stunned. Hanging upside down by one foot, her entire body dripping wet, she stared wide-eyed at the youth gripping her ankle, who was now frowning as he appraised her naked form.","“Ahhhhh!”","A shrill scream erupted from Yue’er’s throat. Almost simultaneously, her other foot lashed out viciously, aiming a fierce kick straight at the youth’s handsome face.","Xiao Junyan hadn’t anticipated this little girl suddenly shrieking and aiming a kick at his face. Caught completely off guard, his face—a beauty that provoked both divine and mortal resentment—took Yue’er’s kick squarely. He felt the slippery little foot he was holding twist, and the girl he’d been dangling upside down spun around and landed several metres away. Immediately afterwards, she hastily pulled a garment over herself.","Yue’er’s beautiful eyes brimmed with grievance. After pulling the clothes on, she plopped down onto the ground, tears welling in her eyes as she glared at the youth with a pitiful yet furious expression.","Waaah... She was wretched, she’d been wronged.","Mother had said a girl’s body must never be seen by boys, yet this man had lifted her naked from the water and scrutinised her thoroughly. He’d seen everything.","Xiao Junyan rubbed his face, feeling the sting of the kick. His tongue detected a faint taste of blood, confirming he’d bitten his lip.","He frowned as he looked at the little girl sitting on the ground, glaring at him angrily. Stepping forward, he asked, ‘Which branch of the family are you from? How did you end up here?’","In his view, their place was protected by barriers and formations; outsiders couldn’t enter their immortal isle. Any child appearing here must naturally be from the Xiao family.","However, he had never interacted with the children from the various branches of the Xiao family, so naturally, he had no idea which branch this little girl belonged to.","Therefore, recalling the training exercises arranged by the family for its young members, he assumed this little girl had probably snuck out to play. Still, she was awfully bold—a five or six-year-old girl daring to follow into a place like this.","Yue’er offered no reply, merely glaring at him with a mixture of anger and hurt. She was thinking: how furious would Father, Mother, and her masters be if they knew she’d been seen so completely by this youth?","Xiao Junyan, however, thought she was frightened.","“I am Xiao Junyan,” he said promptly."]},{"number":4887,"title":"Chapter 4887: Misunderstanding","paragraphs":["Chapter 4887: Misunderstanding","Seeing that she still didn’t respond, he couldn’t help but frown and said, “Young Master of the Xiao Family.”","Seeing that she still didn’t react after hearing his words, his frown wrinkled deeper as his gaze sized up the little girl and asked, “Whose child are you? Who brought you in? Don’t you know the rules of the Xiao family that no one under the age of ten is allowed to enter this forest?”","Yue’er saw that he didn’t say a single to the point sentence for half a minute, but instead was talking about him being the Young Master of the Xiao family or something like that, so she stood up at that moment and angrily yelled at him, “You’ve looked me bare!You have to apologize to me!”","Hearing this, Xiao Junyan glanced at her and said in a light tone, “What does it matter if a little doll is seen naked?” Saying this, he took out his clothes from the space to put them on while drying the water stains on his body with his spirit energy.","Walking forward, seeing that the little doll behind him didn’t follow, he stopped his steps, looked back at her and said, “Still not following?” In a place like this, she alone would not survive a night here.","“Not following!”","Yue’er grunted, threw off her face, and walked in the opposite direction after putting her clothes back on.","Unbeknownst to her, she hadn’t even taken a few steps before she was lifted up by her collar.","“Ah! Let go of me! Put me down!” She kicked as hard as she could, and when she saw that he grabbed her collar and didn’t let go, she grabbed his hand and put her mouth on it to bite it.","“Hiss!”","Xiao Junyan ate pain, low hissed, hand a loose, put the little girl to the ground to go, a look, his wrist was bitten out a circle of teeth marks, oozing a circle of blood.","He frowned, staring at the ground to get up and pull out his legs want to run the little doll, then lifted her up under his arm, while coldly drinking: “Do not move!If you move again, I will knock you out and carry you away!”","Yue’er stared at him with a pair of eyes like a small beast, then she saw him put his hand on her head, and the hair that was still wet and dripping with water was dried by him, and with the surging of his breath, her body that was still a bit cold gradually warmed up.","“Where is your teleportation jade token?”","Xiao Junyan asked in a cold voice, looking around he didn’t realize that this little doll had a teleportation jade tag on her.If it wasn’t for the fact that this was his Xiao family’s child, with his nature, he wouldn’t have paid any attention to this troublesome little doll.","“No!” Yue’er said without any good humor, turning her head away from him.","Xiao Junyan frowned, thinking that if this child had sneakily followed her in, naturally no one would have given her the life-preserving teleportation jade, so he was silent for a while and asked, “Are you the only one in this area? Who brought you in?”","Yue’er’s gaze turned, struggled to get down from his arm, stood in front of him and made a face at him, and grumbled in anger, “Other than me, aren’t you a human being?”","Xiao Junyan looked at her and didn’t say anything for half a second, seemingly pondering something.","Yue’er saw that he didn’t say anything and kept staring at her, so she stared at him as well, carefully sizing him up.This man looked fifteen or sixteen years old, and although she had seen many good looking people, there was no denying that this man was quite good looking.","He was wearing an ink-colored robe with embroidered cloud patterns on the sleeves and collar, a jade belt tied around his waist, and a cold-faced aura of “stranger don’t come near” that was very intriguing.","However, all of this was nothing to her, naturally she would not be intimidated by him.","After staring at the little dot in front of him for a long time, Xiao Junyan said in a cold voice: “Before you meet the other clansmen, you will follow me!”"]},{"number":4888,"title":"Chapter 4888: Take Her Away","paragraphs":["Chapter 4888: Take Her Away","Hearing his words, Yue’er’s gaze shifted, a hint of cunning flickering in her eyes. Did this man think she was part of the Xiao family?","The thought crossed her mind, and she blinked. Recalling how he’d introduced himself as Xiao Junyan, the young master of the Xiao family, a decision formed swiftly in her heart.","“Aren’t you leaving? Waiting to be fed to the beasts?” Xiao Junyan walked ahead, noticing her still standing there, and called out.","Yue’er immediately began walking at his pace, keeping up beside him without haste. However, her small frame meant her steps were tiny, and she gradually fell behind, creating a distance between them. The weeds in the forest stood waist-high, easily concealing her diminutive form.","As Xiao Junyan walked on, he noticed the little thing had gone quiet. Turning back, he saw the tiny figure struggling to push through the weeds toward him. Seeing this, he stood still. After a moment, when she reached his side, he reached out and scooped her up in one arm, striding forward again.","“I can run by myself! I don’t need you to carry me!” Yue’er protested, not wanting this man holding her at all!","“Your legs are too short.”","Xiao Junyan replied coldly. His stride lengthened as he darted through the forest. When encountering dangerous beasts, he simply leapt high into the air to avoid them.","After carrying the little one for a while, he realized she had some weight to her. After traversing a distance, the arm holding her began to feel slightly sore.","He had to admit, this little girl was a chubby child. Even though her frame was small, her entire body was soft and plump.","With someone carrying her, Yue’er didn’t demand to be put down. Instead, she settled comfortably in his arms. Her eyes twinkled as she announced, “I’m hungry.”","Hearing this, Xiao Junyan paused. He found a spot to stop, set the child down beside him, and retrieved a Fasting Pill from his spatial storage.","“Here, eat this!” he offered, holding it out.","Yue’er looked at it, her eyes widening. “This? I won’t eat this. It doesn’t taste good. I want meat.” She absolutely refused to take the fasting pills, especially since they weren’t even as good as the ones her mother made! No way was she eating them.","“Eat!” he pushed forward, making a move to stuff it into her mouth.","“No, no! I won’t eat this medicine!” she protested, backing away.","Xiao Junyan, who had never cared for a child before, watched the little thing stare at him warily, her eyes wide with suspicion, as if terrified he would force the Fasting Pill into her mouth. He couldn’t help but frown, his gaze darkening slightly.","After a moment’s pause, he tucked the pill away. “Wait for me up in the tree. I’ll go get you some meat.” Kids really were such a hassle.","Hearing this, Yue’er finally stopped resisting. She stepped forward, letting him lift her up and place her securely in a spot high in the tree.","“Sit tight. Hold onto this branch. Don’t fall. I’ll be back soon,” he instructed in a cold tone.","“Got it,” Yue’er replied. Watching him fly away, she pulled a spirit fruit from her spatial pouch and began eating it, her eyes darting around as if scheming something.","Meanwhile, Xiao Junyan, worried about the little one left behind in the tree, caught a gray-feathered spirit chicken and returned. Seeing her sitting obediently in the branches, he approached to bring her down. Gathering some twigs nearby, he proceeded to roast the spirit chicken.","“I’ve already sent word back to the clan. Someone will come to take you home,” Xiao Junyan said, tearing off a chicken leg for her."]},{"number":4889,"title":"Chapter 4889: Avoiding a Fight","paragraphs":["Chapter 4889: Avoiding a Fight","Upon hearing this, Yue’er’s small hand holding the chicken leg froze. Someone wanted to take her back? Back where? To the Xiao family?","If she went to the Xiao family, wouldn’t her secret be exposed?","She continued munching on the chicken leg while her eyes darted around restlessly.","Xiao Junyan watched the little girl devour the chicken leg with both hands. Before long, only a bare bone remained in her grasp. With her face glistening with grease, she looked up at him and reached out again.","Seeing this, he tore off another chicken leg for her before tearing off a wing for himself.","After they finished the roast chicken, Xiao Junyan carried her to a spring to wash their faces and hands. Just then, rustling sounds came from the woods. Xiao Junyan looked up to see a massive, fierce beast emerging from the forest, flattening the undergrowth wherever it passed.","“Roooaaaar!”","The fierce beast spotted the pair by the spring, let out a thunderous roar, and lunged fiercely toward them.","“Watch out!”","Xiao Junyan exclaimed, scooping Yue’er into his arms. With a tap of his toes, he leapt off the ground, carrying her out of the beast’s reach.","“Snap!”","A tree thick enough for one person to wrap their arms around snapped clean in two, crashing to the ground with a loud crack. The fierce beast lunged at empty air, whirling around to charge at the pair again, its speed a blur like a streak of light.","Xiao Junyan, holding Yue’er, didn’t confront it head-on. Instead, he swept through the forest with her in his arms to evade.","Yue’er, clinging tightly as she was carried, feared he might lose his grip and drop her. Her little hands gripped his robe fiercely, her chubby legs clamped tightly around his waist.","Xiao Junyan’s expression darkened—not because he was being pursued by that peak-level Sacred Beast’s fierce beast, but because the chubby child clinging to him like an octopus slowed his swift movement.","“Rooooaaaar!”","The beast’s roar reverberated through the forest, accompanied by the thunderous thudding when it ran. The air thickened with the oppressive pressure radiating from its mighty cry.","Whether it was an illusion or not, Xiao Junyan sensed the sounds of other beasts running and darting through the surrounding area, some near, some far, after the beast’s roar faded.","Yue’er, nestled in his embrace, glanced around. Her beautiful eyes flashed as she said, “Many fierce beasts are gathering around us. That beast behind us called them.”","Yue’er spoke, freeing one small hand to pat his shoulder. Curiously, she asked, “Why didn’t you kill that beast? Why did you turn and run when you saw it? Couldn’t you defeat it?”","“Because you were here,” Xiao Junyan replied coldly.","If he hadn’t been protecting this little one, why would he have turned and fled? If a fight broke out, he naturally couldn’t spare a thought for this child. No matter how much of a nuisance she was, he couldn’t possibly abandon such a young member of the Xiao family, could he?","Yue’er blinked in surprise, then piped up brightly, “Just put me down. I can take care of myself.” The moment the words left her mouth, the swift-moving figure abruptly halted. The sudden stop nearly flung her forward, but she clutched his robe tightly and avoided being thrown off.","“Even if you don’t want to get down now, you have no choice,” Xiao Junyan declared. His gaze swept the area as he gathered momentum and swept her up, carrying her to the nearest tallest and largest tree.","“Sit tight. Be careful not to fall,” Xiao Junyan instructed, setting her down on a triangular fork in the tree’s branches before descending once more."]},{"number":4890,"title":"Chapter 4890: Meeting again","paragraphs":["Chapter 4890: Meeting again","Yue’er looked down from the tree. He had placed her high up, and as she gazed downward, she could only make out vague shapes through the dense foliage. Below, Xiao Junyan, sword in hand, attacked the fierce beast that had lunged at him.","She had initially wondered if this man was weak. But witnessing his unrestrained attack, she realized he wasn’t weak at all—he was formidable. Judging by his skill and prowess, he likely surpassed even her Big Brother!","It made sense. He was several years older than her Big Brother, so being more skilled was natural. But who could say that her two brothers wouldn’t surpass him someday?","The beasts’ agonized screams and roars echoed through the forest, while the scent of blood spread on the wind. Watching from her perch in the trees, Yue’er saw Xiao Junyan below handling the beasts with ease. She immediately suppressed her aura and slipped away silently.","She wasn’t a true member of the Xiao family. If the men he summoned brought her back to the Xiao residence, who knew if she might be killed? At least in this forest, no fierce beast could harm her. Once the little fox’s spirit energy recovered, perhaps it could carry her away from here.","She still wanted to see her Mother!","After Xiao Junyan dealt with the fierce beasts, he gathered his strength to climb the tree and bring the little one down. But when he reached the top, he discovered the creature he’d left there was gone!","“Slipped away?” He frowned, scanning the surroundings. How had that little thing vanished without a sound?","Recalling how the little one had secretly followed him out, and how he’d told her family members were coming to take her back... She must have slipped away because she didn’t want to be taken back.","Thinking of how tiny she was, and how this place was filled with unknown dangers, if she encountered a fierce beast, that little thing could be swallowed whole in one bite.","Without hesitation, he mounted his sword and soared into the sky, searching for the little doll’s trace...","After slipping away from the tree, Yue’er wandered through the forest. Having stayed here for several days, she rarely needed to fight the fierce beasts. Whenever she released the ancient Sacred Beast’s aura from her body, those beasts would avoid her like the plague.","Humming an unknown little tune, she swung a branch picked up from somewhere, her steps light and brisk. Since leaving the great tree, she had been using the Swift Stride technique. In just a short while, she had covered a considerable distance, so she needn’t worry about being caught by Xiao Junyan.","Arriving beneath a tree, she paused to rest. Glancing around, she leapt up to perch on a branch, pulling a fruit from her spatial pouch to eat while dangling her legs in midair.","The tree’s foliage was dense, and her small frame made her nearly invisible when silent and still.","After eating a fruit, Yue’er yawned. Seeing the sun blazing overhead while the tree provided shade and a cool breeze, she found a comfortable spot in the branches and fell asleep.","She didn’t know how long she’d slept when the sounds of combat in the forest roused her. Opening her eyes, she saw a boy of fourteen or fifteen being attacked by two lion-like beasts of Sacred Beast rank. Though covered in wounds, he gritted his teeth and fought on.","Sitting up to observe more closely, she confirmed the attackers were indeed two Sacred Beast-level lions. Yet several other lions circled nearby, watching intently as if guarding against their prey escaping. Among them stood one lion—a peak Sacred Beast-level lion."]},{"number":4891,"title":"Chapter 4891: Falling","paragraphs":["Chapter 4891: Falling","She recognized them—these were the very lions that had attacked the lion in her space just days ago.","She recalled Xiao Junyan did mention that those who entered this place should carry a teleportation jade token at their waist. Her gaze swept over the youth, who was panting slightly and wounded, but she saw no such token.","“Roaaaaaar!”","The lion showed remarkable patience with its prey, toying with him rather than pouncing to kill him outright. Instead, it watched as he struggled.","Xiao Junheng bit his lip as he retreated. After prolonged combat, his stamina waned, compounded by his injuries, causing his steps to falter. To make matters worse, the teleportation jade token that could have saved his life had been torn from his waist during the earlier fight, lost to who knew where.","Yue’er watched the battle unfold ahead. The youth wore a crescent-moon-patterned robe and possessed striking features, though his strength seemed notably weaker.","Hmm, at least he was far weaker than that Xiao Junyan she’d encountered earlier. Yet the two appeared to be only a year or two apart in age—how could their abilities differ so drastically?","As she debated whether to intervene, a faint hissing sound reached her ears. A sudden chill brushed her neck, and instinctively, she reached out. Her hand closed around the head of a finger-thick, emerald-green venomous snake, its tail coiled tightly around her arm. The creature flickered its tongue, hissing menacingly at her.","“Trying to bite me?” Yue’er gazed at the green venomous snake with a playful smile, her voice soft and sweet. “I hold grudges, you know!” As she spoke, she drew a dagger from her sleeve and thrust it directly into the snake’s vital spot.","“Hiss!”","The snake hissed in agony. The dagger’s thrust and the snake’s convulsive writhing severed its body cleanly in two. One half fell to the ground, while Yue’er clutched the head section in her hand.","“Oh, my snake gallbladder!” Spotting the severed body, Yue’er leapt down after it, intending to retrieve the venomous snake’s gallbladder.","Little did she know, as she landed, her entire body landed squarely atop a lion that had been fixated on its human prey.","The sudden appearance of a tiny figure tumbling from the tree stunned not only the lion, now unexpectedly ridden atop its head, but also the youth leaning against the tree trunk, gasping for breath.","His expression shifted even more sharply when he realized the fallen figure was none other than a little girl, no older than five or six.","“Get down! Come behind me!”","He shouted urgently, trying to reach out and pull the little girl off the lion’s back. But suddenly, one of the lions lunged forward, charging at him. The impact forced him to shift his focus to fending off the lion.","“Roaaaaar!”","At that moment, another lion roared and lunged at the human child who had landed on its back.","“Watch out!” Xiao Junheng bit down, desperate to rush to the rescue but unable to break free.","Yue’er looked at the lion lunging toward her. Suddenly, a mischievous smile spread across her face. She flung the snake head she’d been clutching tightly, sending it straight into the lion’s gaping jaws.","Though the venomous snake had been severed at the body, its head remained open. Flung toward the lion, it snapped at the snake almost reflexively. The snake’s fangs sank into the lion’s tongue, the venom seeping into its flesh. In that instant, the lion let out a piercing, agonized roar."]},{"number":4892,"title":"Chapter 4892: Xiao Junheng","paragraphs":["Chapter 4892: Xiao Junheng","The lion instinctively lunged at the object in its mouth after it roared. As snake blood spattered, the lion convulsed and collapsed.","“Thud!”","The heavy impact of the body hitting the ground startled both the youth and the lions.","“Rooooaaaaaar!”","The other lions roared at Yue’er, staring at the tiny human standing atop the lion’s back. Suddenly, they realized this human child seemed strangely familiar.","“Yaaah!”","Yue’er was flung from the lion’s back. Mid-air, she flipped gracefully and landed steadily. Just as the lion that had thrown her off prepared to pounce and kill the human child, its eyes suddenly narrowed. A flash of terror appeared in its gaze. With a low growl, it retreated swiftly, vanishing without a trace within mere breaths.","It recognized the aura of an ancient Sacred Beast emanating from this human child. They dared provoke anyone, but never such a human.","The boy gasped for breath, staring blankly and puzzled at the lions’ sudden flight, unable to fathom what had just occurred. But his bewilderment deepened when he saw the little girl run to the tree, pick up a segment of green snake carcass, slit it open with a dagger, and extract a jade-green snake gallbladder from within.","“Are you okay?”","He approached the girl, finding her face unfamiliar. She didn’t resemble any of the young members he knew from his clan. But then, his clan was large, and she was so young—it made sense he hadn’t met her before. Besides, how could any child from outside their clan possibly be here?","Thus, he naturally classified the little girl as a member of the Xiao family.","After putting away the gallbladder, Yue’er finally looked at the youth before her. Pointing to the wound on his body, she said, “You’re the one with the problem! You’re bleeding.”","How pathetic! She was so small, yet she hadn’t even gotten hurt or bled!","“Yeah, I’m hurt.” Xiao Junheng let out a soft sigh, leaning his back against a large tree as he sat down. He took out some medicine and sprinkled it onto his wound, then roughly bandaged it with gauze.","Bandaging it himself, he could only use his teeth, so he ended up tying it into a tight knot.","“Do you need help?” Yue’er asked, her pure eyes blinking innocently. She couldn’t bear watching him pour the medicine backward—most of it was spilling onto the ground.","“Yes.”","He handed her the medicine bottle while studying her. “Who brought you in here? Don’t you know children your age aren’t allowed in this place?”","“Why? I’m not hurt,” Yue’er replied. After sprinkling the medicine, she carefully bandaged his wound, finishing with a neat bow.","“There are too many fierce beasts in this forest, and many are incredibly powerful. Even I got injured—how much more so for a child as small as you.” He leaned against a tree to rest, keeping a watchful eye on his surroundings as he spoke with puzzlement. “Those lions earlier... I don’t know what happened, but they just ran off.”","Yue’er looked at him with a bright smile. “I may be small, but the fierce beasts don’t eat me.”","“Wait here. I’ll send word back and have my father send someone to escort you home.” He spoke, pulling out a communication jade tablet.","Yue’er looked at him, her smile unchanged. “You stay here! When they arrive, let them take you back. Otherwise, the lions might come back and eat you.”"]},{"number":4893,"title":"Chapter 4893: Suspicion","paragraphs":["Chapter 4893: Suspicion","As soon as Yue’er finished speaking, she waved at him and scampered off into the woods on her little legs.","Seeing this, Xiao Junheng froze for a moment. Forgetting to send a message, he hurried after her. “Wait! It’s too dangerous for a child like you to be wandering around here! Don’t run off!”","Even if he hadn’t met her before, she was still a child of the main branch of the Xiao family. Naturally, he couldn’t let her face danger here. As for the lions that had suddenly disappeared earlier, he never imagined they could be connected to this little girl.","Yue’er pulled out a fruit and ate it as she walked, glancing back at him. Seeing him catch up in a few strides, she wrinkled her nose and said, “Don’t follow me. I’m perfectly safe on my own.”","“Who is your father? Which branch of the family? How did you sneak in? Who brought you? I see you don’t have a teleportation jade token. Who brought you in?” He came up beside her, his gaze fixed on the little girl who didn’t even reach his waist.","Seeing no trace of fear on her face, only a lively, spirited look, he couldn’t help but feel surprised. How had he never seen such a little girl in the family before?","Yue’er’s eyes twinkled as she munched on the fruit, her face breaking into a smile. “I came with Brother Junyan.”","“Junyan? Impossible! How could he bring you into this forest? And if you came together, why am I only seeing you and not him?” Xiao Junheng froze, his voice tinged with surprise.","“We encountered a ferocious beast in the woods and got separated. I have no idea where he is now,” Yue’er replied, finishing the fruit in her hand in just a few bites.","Xiao Junheng watched her finish the fruit in a few bites. His eyes flickered, his brow furrowing slightly. “Given his temperament, he wouldn’t have brought such a young child in here without a second thought. You’re not telling the truth. And that fruit you ate—it was a spirit fruit, wasn’t it?”","Though not the young master of the Xiao family, his father was the current patriarch. He’d seen many things, yet never a spirit fruit like the one she’d eaten.","Even just smelling it, he could sense a potent aura of spirit energy emanating from the fruit. Where on earth had this child come from? Was she truly a member of the Xiao family?","The thought made him tense, prompting him to keep his guard up.","“Since you’ve come into this forest, do you know why we’re here?” Xiao Junheng asked, his gaze fixed on the little figure beside him.","At his words, Yue’er beamed at him, her voice clear and bright. “Of course I know! Because a Sacred Beast appeared here!” Trying to test her? She was no fool.","Besides, that Sacred Beast had only advanced to its current form after consuming her Mother’s medicinal pill. How could she possibly be unaware?","Xiao Junheng was surprised to see she knew, yet a strange feeling lingered in his heart.","Suddenly, the sound of clashing weapons reached his ears. His footsteps halted instantly as he released his divine sense. The next moment, his expression changed. He grabbed Yue’er, who was about to leave, and pulled her toward another direction.","“Go! We must rescue them!”","Yue’er was dragged along, her little face utterly speechless. What kind of people had she stumbled upon? Why were all these Xiao family members like this?","Not far away, several Xiao family disciples were being besieged by a pack of wind wolves. Covered in wounds, their vital energy chaotic, they huddled together, gasping for breath. Gritting their teeth, they gripped their swords, staring intently at the wolves advancing step by step."]},{"number":4894,"title":"Chapter 4894: Rescue","paragraphs":["Chapter 4894: Rescue","“Huff, huff!”","One of them gasped for breath, his hand already gripping the teleportation jade token at his waist. Gritting his teeth, he said, “I don’t think we can hold out much longer. If we keep fighting, we’ll all end up here. Better to shatter the teleportation jade token!”","The other hesitated, saying nothing, though his face betrayed his reluctance.","A third gritted his teeth, fuming, “Break it yourself if you must! We finally made it to this forest—if we turn back now, we’ll be laughed to death! And we’ve barely been here. If we leave now, how can we ever hold our heads high again?”","Hearing this, the hesitant and resentful youth chimed in, “Exactly! It’s not the final moment yet! If things get truly desperate, we can shatter it then. I refuse to break it now. Besides, I want to bring my mother a gift from here!”","“Don’t forget what the elders told us—this is just a trial. Staying alive is the top priority. If you want to die, I’m not going down with you.” With that, the other youth crushed his teleportation jade token, vanishing from the spot in an instant.","His departure only compounded the plight of the two already wounded. With one less ally, facing the wolf pack became even more daunting.","“I’ll fight to the end! I’ll at least bring back a wolf fang for my mother!” The first youth gritted his teeth, brandishing his sword as he charged forward, slashing at one of the wind wolves.","“Stay right here! Don’t wander off!” Xiao Junheng watched the scene unfold, his expression growing grim. Especially when he saw the two still clinging to fighting the wolves instead of breaking their jade tokens to escape, his handsome face darkened further.","After placing the little girl he’d dragged along onto a tree branch, he snapped off a piece and thrust it into her hands. “Cover yourself with this. The wolves won’t see you.”","Yue’er’s lips twitched. Watching the youth shove a branch into her hands before dashing forward, she rolled her eyes in blatant disregard, silently expressing her utter exasperation.","A leafy branch held in front of her would make her invisible to the wolves? This youth was quite tall, yet his brain seemed to be rather slow.","And ahead lay a pack of wolves—at least a dozen or twenty Wind Wolves! One of them was even a peak-level Sacred Beast. Wasn’t he just running to his death?","Could the three of them really take on a peak-level Sacred Beast alpha and a dozen Sacred Beast-level Wind Wolves?","Perched in the tree, she toyed with the branch in her hand. Those two had teleportation jade tablets at their waists—if they truly reached a dead end, they might have a sliver of hope to save themselves. But that boy, who looked decent enough but clearly wasn’t the sharpest tool in the shed? Not so sure about him.","So, should she just leave? Or should she go help them?","Her small face was etched with conflict. She had never encountered this particular pack before. Unlike lions, they didn’t bolt at her sight. She knew she couldn’t outfight so many wolves in a coordinated attack. But if she unleashed her ancient aura, would those three detect it?","While she hesitated, Xiao Junheng had already charged forward, sword raised. The two youths’ eyes lit up with surprise and hope when they saw him.","“Second Young Master!”","They hadn’t expected to encounter Xiao Junheng here, their faces lighting up with excitement. Among the younger generation of the Xiao family, aside from the prodigy Xiao Junyan, Xiao Junheng’s prowess was unmatched!"]},{"number":4895,"title":"Chapter 4895: It’s me","paragraphs":["Chapter 4895: It’s me","With him lending a hand, they might not even have to shatter the teleportation jade!","“Attack the alpha wolf!”","Xiao Junheng commanded in a low voice, leaping directly toward the pack leader. To rout the wolves, the best strategy was to kill the Wolf King first. Once the Wolf King fell, the rest would scatter.","“Got it!”","The two responded immediately. With his addition, their confidence surged! Their weary bodies suddenly ignited with fierce fighting spirit. The three joined forces and charged toward the Wolf King.","However, their intentions were good, but reality was cruel.","The Wolf King didn’t approach. Instead, it crouched in a position further back, watching them. Seeing the attackers charge toward the Wolf King, the wind wolves intensified their vicious encirclement.","Xiao Junheng was already wounded, and with the other two also injured, their combined strength proved no match for the onslaught of nearly twenty vicious wolves. Before long, their wounds deepened, and their clothes were soaked in blood.","Yue’er watched, her gaze fixed on the Wolf King. She tossed aside the branch in her hand, her small form leaping lightly through the trees toward the Wolf King.","Dagger in hand, she prepared to strike the Wolf King. But the beast seemed to sense her presence, lifting its head to give her a cold, dismissive glance. Its jaws opened in a low, threatening growl, sharp fangs glistening as saliva dripped toward Yue’er.","Just as Yue’er prepared to pounce downward, she suddenly sensed a sharp, whistling blade streaking toward her from the distance. She halted her movement abruptly and turned toward the sound.","A cold gleam streaked through the air. Upon closer inspection, it was an arrow carrying a fierce aura, shot with blinding speed and precision, aimed squarely at the Wolf King.","The Wolf King’s fur bristled instantly at the perceived danger. It leaped violently, lunging toward the small figure crouched in the tree.","Its dual purpose was to evade the incoming arrow and to devour this human child radiating pure Spirit Energy!","“Watch out!”","Xiao Junheng, surrounded by several wind wolves, saw the Wolf King lunge at the little girl. His expression changed instantly, and he cried out in alarm.","However, though he desperately wanted to save her, he couldn’t spare the time or the hands.","Unexpectedly, at that very moment, he saw the little girl swing the dagger in her hand, striking toward the Wolf King. The blade sliced through the air with such sharpness that he couldn’t help but freeze in surprise.","The Wolf King lunged forward, only to see the cold gleam of the dagger approaching. He dodged instantly, leaping onto a nearby branch. Then, thrusting off with his hind legs, he charged once more at his targeted prey.","Perched awkwardly in the tree, Yue’er watched the Wolf King lunge toward her again. “Want to eat me?” she huffed indignantly. “I’ll knock your teeth right out!”","In that instant, she shifted her stance. As the Wolf King charged, she stepped back, appearing to lose her footing and fall—but it was a deliberate maneuver to evade, planning to land and fight again.","Yet as she leapt from the tree, an unfamiliar scent suddenly assailed her. Almost instinctively, she swung the dagger in her hand toward the source of the scent. Unexpectedly, a voice she recognized, though not entirely unfamiliar, reached her ears.","“It’s me.”","Xiao Junyan’s icy expression darkened slightly. Seeing this chubby child who had slipped away from under his watch now encountering wolves here, and wielding a dagger toward him, the frigid aura radiating from him was utterly chilling."]},{"number":4896,"title":"Chapter 4896: Knows","paragraphs":["Chapter 4896: Knows","Yue’er froze upon hearing the voice. In that brief moment of distraction, the dagger in her hand was snatched away, and simultaneously, she was swept into the arms of the intruder and pinned against his chest.","Xiao Junyan cradled the chubby infant in one arm while seizing the dagger from her grasp with the other. He immediately lunged toward the Wolf King charging once more. Unexpectedly, as he thrust the dagger forward, its sharpness and unusual nature became apparent.","Whoosh!","Awooooooo!","A fierce blade aura sliced through the air. The charging Wolf King likely hadn’t anticipated Xiao Junyan’s astonishing speed. Unable to dodge in time, its neck took the full force of the strike.","Blood spattered as a howl echoed through the air. The wolf king’s body plummeted downward, crashing onto the ground with a thud. Blood gushed from its neck, staining its fur crimson. Its body twitched convulsively as it struggled to rise, only to be met by another strike from Xiao Junyan, who had landed holding Yue’er.","“Whoosh!”","“Awooooooooo!”","The dagger pierced its flesh. The Wolf King’s howl now sounded hollow and weak. Its body stiffened, and in the next instant, it fell straight to the ground, its life extinguished.","With the Wolf King dead, the remaining eleven or twelve wind wolves let out a final howl before scattering in all directions, fleeing swiftly.","By then, Xiao Junheng and the two youths were already kneeling, swords braced against the ground, gasping for breath. Sweat poured down their bodies like rain, their dark hair plastered to their cheeks. Blood stained their robes crimson; some wounds ran deep enough to expose bone, while others had torn through their clothing entirely. They looked utterly battered and disheveled.","Yet now, all three eyes gleamed brightly as they gazed upon the suddenly appearing youth in black robes—Xiao Junyan! The young master of their Xiao family!","His arrival had averted their peril and indirectly saved their lives.","“Greetings, Young Master! Thank you for saving us!” The two youths, who had been propping themselves up with their swords in a half-kneeling position, dropped to their knees. Clasping their fists in salute, their words brimmed with reverence.","Xiao Junheng, after a moment’s pause, straightened and nodded to him. “Thank goodness you arrived.” His gaze then fell upon the little girl cradled in his arms, a flicker of surprise crossing his eyes.","Everyone in the Xiao family knew that no one could come within three steps of Xiao Junyan, let alone be held in his arms. So what was the story with this little girl? Had he truly brought her in?","Yue’er, held tightly in his embrace, lifted her head. Seeing that the Wolf King was dead and the danger had passed, yet Xiao Junyan still held onto her dagger without returning it, she immediately cried out, “Give me back my dagger!”","Xiao Junyan merely nodded to Xiao Junheng, paying no heed to the two kneeling youths. Instead, he turned his gaze to the plump little doll in his arms.","Hmm. Though this little thing was hardly a baby anymore, to him, she was nothing but a chubby little meat doll. Especially now, with those wide-eyed, pouting features—she looked utterly amusing.","Within the entire Xiao family, no one dared treat him this way.","“The dagger! It’s mine! Give it back!” Yue’er glared at him with her beautiful eyes, like a small beast, reaching out to snatch the dagger back.","But Xiao Junyan simply twisted his wrist, tucking the dagger away.","“Too sharp. Not something you should be playing with.”","If he had previously thought this chubby child belonged to the Xiao family, then seeing that dagger made him realize this plump little thing, who seemed to have appeared out of nowhere, was definitely not one of them."]},{"number":4897,"title":"Chapter 4897: Question","paragraphs":["Chapter 4897: Question","“You!”","Yue’er glared at him indignantly, watching helplessly as her dagger was confiscated, her teeth gritted in fury.","Seeing this, Xiao Junheng inquired, “Junyan, this child claims you brought her in? Which family’s child is she? Did you truly bring her here?”","At those words, Yue’er’s little head ducked back instinctively. Oh no, oh no—this time she’d been found out.","Xiao Junyan watched the little creature cowering silently, a faint curve lifting the corners of his lips. Even that slight shift startled Xiao Junying standing before him.","Had he seen correctly? Junyan had smiled?","His gaze shifted to the little girl nestled in his arms. Was it because of this child?","“She came with me,” Xiao Junyan stated, cradling the plump little doll. Her soft, squishy body felt incredibly comforting to hold, so he kept her close. Turning his attention back to the two in front of him, his expression turned stern as he reprimanded them.","“Are the teleportation jade tablets at your waists mere ornaments? Did you truly intend to battle a wolf pack alone? Had I not intervened, you would now be food for the wolves!”","The two youths, scolded, dared not speak, only lowering their heads.","“What are you standing around for? Hurry and clean up the battlefield!” Xiao Junyan frowned, his voice cold.","“Yes, yes!” They hurriedly responded, ignoring their own injuries as they began cleaning up the scene. They extracted the crystal cores from the wind wolves and finally pulled out the Wolf King’s fang.","However, they dared not keep these items for themselves, since they hadn’t killed the Wolf King. So they stepped forward and handed everything to Xiao Junyan.","“Young Master, the items...”","“These are yours.” Xiao Junyan said, not even glancing at the items. Instead, his gaze fixed on the little doll in his arms. Seeing her furrowed brow, lost in thought, he pinched her plump little cheek, lifting her head.","“What are you thinking about?”","To his surprise, the little thing’s face felt wonderfully soft to pinch. Soft, smooth, and plump—he almost didn’t want to let go.","Yue’er glared, swatting his hand away from her cheek with a sharp slap. “Don’t touch me!” she snapped.","“How dare you! Show no disrespect to the Young Master!”","The two youths paled at the little girl’s audacity to rebuke Xiao Junyan. They immediately snapped at her, only to catch their young master’s cold, dismissive glance. His expression clearly disdained their meddling, leaving them utterly bewildered.","“Bandage your wounds first,” Xiao Junheng instructed, motioning for the two to tend to their injuries.","The two youths responded immediately, retreating to tend to their wounds.","“Put me down!” Yue’er cried, struggling to free herself from his embrace.","But Xiao Junyan held her tightly, his handsome face expressionless as he declared, “You’re still young. It’s safer for me to carry you.”","“Give me back the dagger, and I can ensure my own safety,” Yue’er countered.","“If I give it back, you’ll just run off again,” he said expressionlessly, carrying her to the side.","Yue’er’s heart skipped a beat. Blinking her beautiful eyes, she replied without flinching, “Run off? What running off? I wouldn’t run off!”","Xiao Junyan watched her silently for a long moment before asking, “What’s your name?”","Yue’er blinked but said nothing.","“You’re not a member of the Xiao family. How did you get in?” Xiao Junyan pressed."]},{"number":4898,"title":"Chapter 4898: Follow","paragraphs":["Chapter 4898: Follow","Yue’er’s eyes darted about, about to speak, when his voice reached her.","“Tell me your real name. Don’t try to fool me.”","“I’m a descendant of the Xiao family’s collateral line! I just wandered here out of curiosity. With all these barriers and formations, how could anyone outside the Xiao family possibly get in?” Yue’er said with a smile.","Hearing this, he frowned, fixing his gaze on her. “You’re not.”","“You’ve never seen me before—how can you be so sure? With so many children in the Xiao family’s branches, have you met them all?” Yue’er gave a light, crisp snort.","“That dagger of yours is no ordinary weapon. It doesn’t belong to the Xiao family.” Xiao Junyan stared at the chubby little fox-like child in his arms, his voice cold. “You’d better tell me the truth. Otherwise, once we return to the Xiao family, no one will be able to save you.”","Yue’er’s eyes darted about. “Give me back my dagger, and I’ll tell you.”","Xiao Junyan stared at her but didn’t retrieve the dagger. Instead, he said, “Fine. If you won’t tell me, then you’ll just have to stay by my side.”","Seeing his stubborn nature, Yue’er wanted to clench her tiny fist and punch him square in the eye. But while she had the desire, she lacked the courage. After all, she was on his turf now.","“Junyan, my father sent me to help you search for that Sacred Beast. Have you encountered it? Or found any clues?” Xiao Junheng, having tended to his wounds, approached and found the two staring each other down. He couldn’t help but find it peculiar.","“No.”","Xiao Junyan replied, cradling the little doll in his arms. He turned to Junheng and asked, “Did you lose your communication jade token? If so, you should return first. I can manage on my own.”","Seeing this, Xiao Junheng offered a gentle smile. “Though my strength doesn’t match yours, I can still assist where possible. Besides, you’re facing a Sacred Beast. Father sent me here—if I returned alone, I doubt I could explain myself to him.”","His voice trailed off as his gaze fell upon the little girl in Xiao Junyan’s arms. “Besides, you’ve brought such a young child into this. If we really encounter a Sacred Beast, what will become of her? I should stay and help you! And I’ve already sent word back, asking Father to send someone to retrieve the child. It’s far too dangerous here.”","Hearing this, Xiao Junyan frowned, glanced at the little one in his arms, and said without further comment, “Let’s go.”","“Young Master, may we... may we accompany you?” The two youths cautiously followed and asked. Such a rare opportunity to draw close to the Young Master was one they truly didn’t want to miss.","After all, the Young Master would eventually select a personal guard from within the clan. If they could catch his eye, perhaps they could serve by his side in the future.","For members of a collateral branch like them, becoming the Young Master’s confidant would be an immense honor.","Xiao Junyan glanced at them, seemed to ponder something, then nodded. He continued forward, cradling the small figure in his arms.","Thus, a small group formed on the spur of the moment, with Xiao Junyan at its center.","By evening, Yue’er called out, “I’m hungry.”","“Hungry? We have Fasting Pill.” Xiao Junheng said, retrieving a medicine bottle from his spatial storage.","“She won’t eat those,” Xiao Junyan replied, turning to the two accompanying youths. “You two—gather branches, start a fire, and hunt for game.”"]},{"number":4899,"title":"Chapter 4899: Stupefied","paragraphs":["Chapter 4899: Stupefied","“Yes!” Though wounded, the two youths were eager to prove themselves before him. At his command, they immediately dashed into the woods.","Xiao Junheng paused, glancing at the little girl seated beside Xiao Junyan before turning back to him. “You didn’t bring them along just so they could do these things, did you?” he asked, slightly surprised.","“What else?” Xiao Junyan asked indifferently.","He stated it with such matter-of-factness that Xiao Junheng found himself at a loss for words, merely fixing a deep gaze upon him and the little girl.","He knew in his heart that Xiao Junyan held this little girl in high regard.","Yet, over all these years, he had never shown such devotion to anyone. To see him so preoccupied with a mere little girl now was truly unexpected.","“Thirsty? Want some water?” Xiao Junyan’s attention was entirely focused on the chubby little girl pouting beside him. Seeing her puffed-up expression, he couldn’t help but reach out and poke her little cheek.","Yue’er was sulking! Her dagger had been confiscated, and this man kept staring at her, holding her tight so she couldn’t escape. Now, seeing him reach out to poke her cheek playfully, she immediately turned her face and opened her mouth to bite his finger.","“Little brat,” Xiao Junyan chuckled softly, withdrawing his hand and instead gently flicking her forehead.","“I’m not a little brat!” Yue’er snorted softly. Having failed to bite his finger and instead received a flick on her forehead, she rubbed her forehead with one hand and turned her head away, refusing to acknowledge him.","“Have some water.” Xiao Junyan handed her the water sac he was holding.","“No.” Yue’er didn’t take it, crossing her arms and curling up.","“How about some fruit? “As if by magic, he produced more fruit—wild berries clearly picked from the forest.","“No.” Yue’er replied without even glancing at them.","Seeing her refusal, he passed the berries to Xiao Junheng beside him. Then, retrieving two crimson eggs from his spatial pouch, he held them before her. “How about these?”","Yue’er blinked at the eggs, curiosity sparking in her eyes. “What are these?”","Seeing her interest, Xiao Junyan’s lips curved into a faint smile, a trace of amusement flickering in his eyes. “These are Firebird eggs. They’re incredibly nourishing.” He placed the two crimson eggs in her hands. “Eat them.”","Xiao Junheng, standing nearby, was utterly dumbfounded. Suddenly, he felt as though he didn’t recognize this Xiao Junyan beside him. Was he truly Xiao Junyan? Was he really not someone else impersonating him?","Yue’er looked at the two red eggs in her hands, still slightly warm. Curious, she asked, “Can I eat them like this? Do I need to cook them?”","“Firebird spirit beast eggs can be eaten raw. Not only are they nourishing for the body, but they’re also exceptionally restorative—a rare treasure indeed,” Xiao Junheng explained, glancing at Xiao Junyan. He couldn’t fathom why his cousin was being so kind to this young girl from a collateral branch of the family.","What stunned him even more was when Xiao Junyan actually took an egg from the little girl’s hand, saying, “Let me peel it for you.” He carefully peeled the egg before handing it to her to eat.","Watching the chubby little girl puff out her cheeks like a squirrel as she ate the firebird egg, Xiao Junyan felt an oddly satisfying warmth rise within him. Seeing her eat with such delight brought him unexpected pleasure.","Meanwhile, the two had lit a fire and prepared the game, placing it on the grill. Just then, Xiao Junheng approached them, his expression blank and dazed."]},{"number":4900,"title":"Chapter 4900: Escaped again","paragraphs":["Chapter 4900: Escaped again","The two exchanged a glance before asking, “Second Young Master? What’s wrong?”","Xiao Junheng snapped back to his senses, waved them off, and walked over to sit by the spot where they were roasting the game. “Leave me alone. Just let me be.”","Seeing this, the two didn’t press further. They continued roasting the meat while keeping watch on their surroundings.","As dusk fell, the forest temperature dropped. The group gathered around the fire, eating meat.","After eating her fill, Yue’er helped tend the fire, poking at the embers or adding branches to keep it burning. Worried the little girl couldn’t withstand the night breeze in the woods, Xiao Junyan held her in his arms, covering her with his cloak as she fell asleep.","The next morning.","As the morning sun filtered through the dense foliage, its rays landing on Xiao Junyan’s face, he instinctively tightened one hand while the other reached to pull the cloak higher over the plump little bundle in his arms.","But his hand met only emptiness. His eyes snapped open. He looked down—where was the chubby little figure?","A sharp, cold gaze swept the surroundings. His divine sense spread out. Beyond the occasional chirping of insects in the woods, only the rustling of wind through the trees could be heard.","Escaped again?","His expression darkened. His hand reached for the dagger hidden in his sleeve, only to find it gone. Clearly, the little brat hadn’t just knocked them out and run away, but had also retrieved the dagger he’d confiscated.","Over all these years, this was the first time he’d been bested by such a chubby little baby. And to have her slip away right under his nose twice? The frustration was palpable.","He thought of this perilous forest and how tiny that little doll was. If she encountered a fierce beast, she wouldn’t even be enough to fill its teeth.","He frowned, glancing at the three still-sleeping figures. He didn’t wake them. Instead, he picked up several pebbles, gathered his breath, and flicked them toward the sleeping trio before darting into the woods. He was off to find that little doll, who had likely vanished into the forest again.","Xiao Junheng was jolted awake by the stinging pain of the stones. His eyes snapped open, and he froze in shock. They had taken turns keeping watch during the night—how could they all have fallen into such a deep, unbroken sleep?","Glancing around, he saw that Xiao Junyan and the little girl were gone. He called out, “Junyan? Junyan?”","“Second Young Master?” Two other youths stirred awake, rubbing their temples as their heads felt thick and groggy.","After calling out repeatedly with no response, Xiao Junheng turned to them and demanded, “Why did you all sleep so soundly last night?”","“I was on the second half of the night watch last night, but somehow I just passed out.” One of the youths scratched his head sheepishly, surprised he’d fallen asleep.","“Where are the young master and that child?” The other youth asked in surprise, noticing their absence.","Xiao Junheng felt a twinge of unease. He glanced at the two youths and said, “You two go back first. I need to return and find out which branch of the family that child belongs to.”","“Second Young Master suspects she’s not from our Xiao family?” the two youths asked in astonishment.","“I’d already had my doubts. But after meeting Junyan, he said he brought her, so I didn’t ask further. Now, however, we clearly all fainted from being drugged. Junyan couldn’t have drugged us—it must have been that child. That’s why I must return and get to the bottom of this.”” Xiao Junheng said, his brow furrowed tightly.","Hearing this, the two boys’ eyes widened in disbelief. “Th-that can’t be possible! She’s so young, how could she possibly...”"]}]);
